  ('A-mercury_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry-mercury-sextile-jupiter', 'relationship-mercury-sextile-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-jupiter_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-jupiter_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Sextile Jupiter', null, 'This person helps you see more than you can see on your own.

They help you see more possibility in what you are thinking about. An idea, question, or decision often feels clearer and more expansive after you talk to them.

The gift of this connection is perspective. This person reminds you not to limit yourself too quickly. They encourage possibility, but they do it in a way that helps you think more deeply, not just more positively.

The challenge is that this connection asks for participation. Its gifts tend to appear in the exchange itself. If you keep your thoughts tucked away until they are fully formed, you may never discover what this person could have helped you uncover.

Let them into the process before you have all the answers. Share the unfinished version. Sometimes their perspective reveals a path you could not have found alone.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person helps you see more than you can see on your own.\n\nThey help you see more possibility in what you are thinking about. An idea, question, or decision often feels clearer and more expansive after you talk to them.\n\nThe gift of this connection is perspective. This person reminds you not to limit yourself too quickly. They encourage possibility, but they do it in a way that helps you think more deeply, not just more positively.\n\nThe challenge is that this connection asks for participation. Its gifts tend to appear in the exchange itself. If you keep your thoughts tucked away until they are fully formed, you may never discover what this person could have helped you uncover.\n\nLet them into the process before you have all the answers. Share the unfinished version. Sometimes their perspective reveals a path you could not have found alone."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that this connection asks for participation. Its gifts tend to appear in the exchange itself. If you keep your thoughts tucked away until they are fully formed, you may never discover what this person could have helped you uncover."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let them into the process before you have all the answers. Share the unfinished version. Sometimes their perspective reveals a path you could not have found alone."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-jupiter_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s growth. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This person helps you see more than you can see on your own.\n\nThey help you see more possibility in what you are thinking about. An idea, question, or decision often feels clearer and more expansive after you talk to them.\n\nThe gift of this connection is perspective. This person reminds you not to limit yourself too quickly. They encourage possibility, but they do it in a way that helps you think more deeply, not just more positively.\n\nThe challenge is that this connection asks for participation. Its gifts tend to appear in the exchange itself. If you keep your thoughts tucked away until they are fully formed, you may never discover what this person could have helped you uncover.\n\nLet them into the process before you have all the answers. Share the unfinished version. Sometimes their perspective reveals a path you could not have found alone.","tension":"The challenge is that this connection asks for participation. Its gifts tend to appear in the exchange itself. If you keep your thoughts tucked away until they are fully formed, you may never discover what this person could have helped you uncover.","advice":"Let them into the process before you have all the answers. Share the unfinished version. Sometimes their perspective reveals a path you could not have found alone.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-jupiter_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-jupiter_square', 'synastry-mercury-square-jupiter', 'relationship-mercury-square-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-jupiter_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-jupiter_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Square Jupiter', null, 'This person has a way of stretching your thinking past its comfort zone.

They may see opportunity where you see risk, possibility where you see unanswered questions. Their instinct is often to go bigger, faster, further. At times, that can feel inspiring. At other times, it can feel like they are skipping over the practical realities that matter to you.

This connection often highlights the tension between vision and discernment. They may challenge assumptions you did not realize you were carrying. They may push against limits that have become so familiar you mistake them for facts. Around them, you may discover that some of your caution comes from wisdom, while some of it comes from fear.

When this dynamic is working well, they help you expand your sense of what is possible. They encourage you to think beyond the version of the story you have already accepted. They remind you that growth rarely happens inside the boundaries of certainty.

The challenge is separating real possibility from wishful thinking. They tend to expand. You tend to question. If you are not careful, one person becomes the visionary and the other becomes the skeptic.

At its best, this connection creates balance. They help you see beyond your usual limits, and you help turn possibility into something workable. Their vision gives the idea room to grow. Your discernment helps it take shape.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a way of stretching your thinking past its comfort zone.\n\nThey may see opportunity where you see risk, possibility where you see unanswered questions. Their instinct is often to go bigger, faster, further. At times, that can feel inspiring. At other times, it can feel like they are skipping over the practical realities that matter to you.\n\nThis connection often highlights the tension between vision and discernment. They may challenge assumptions you did not realize you were carrying. They may push against limits that have become so familiar you mistake them for facts. Around them, you may discover that some of your caution comes from wisdom, while some of it comes from fear.\n\nWhen this dynamic is working well, they help you expand your sense of what is possible. They encourage you to think beyond the version of the story you have already accepted. They remind you that growth rarely happens inside the boundaries of certainty.\n\nThe challenge is separating real possibility from wishful thinking. They tend to expand. You tend to question. If you are not careful, one person becomes the visionary and the other becomes the skeptic.\n\nAt its best, this connection creates balance. They help you see beyond your usual limits, and you help turn possibility into something workable. Their vision gives the idea room to grow. Your discernment helps it take shape."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is separating real possibility from wishful thinking. They tend to expand. You tend to question. If you are not careful, one person becomes the visionary and the other becomes the skeptic."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"At its best, this connection creates balance. They help you see beyond your usual limits, and you help turn possibility into something workable. Their vision gives the idea room to grow. Your discernment helps it take shape."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-jupiter_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s growth. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This person has a way of stretching your thinking past its comfort zone.\n\nThey may see opportunity where you see risk, possibility where you see unanswered questions. Their instinct is often to go bigger, faster, further. At times, that can feel inspiring. At other times, it can feel like they are skipping over the practical realities that matter to you.\n\nThis connection often highlights the tension between vision and discernment. They may challenge assumptions you did not realize you were carrying. They may push against limits that have become so familiar you mistake them for facts. Around them, you may discover that some of your caution comes from wisdom, while some of it comes from fear.\n\nWhen this dynamic is working well, they help you expand your sense of what is possible. They encourage you to think beyond the version of the story you have already accepted. They remind you that growth rarely happens inside the boundaries of certainty.\n\nThe challenge is separating real possibility from wishful thinking. They tend to expand. You tend to question. If you are not careful, one person becomes the visionary and the other becomes the skeptic.\n\nAt its best, this connection creates balance. They help you see beyond your usual limits, and you help turn possibility into something workable. Their vision gives the idea room to grow. Your discernment helps it take shape.","tension":"The challenge is separating real possibility from wishful thinking. They tend to expand. You tend to question. If you are not careful, one person becomes the visionary and the other becomes the skeptic.","advice":"At its best, this connection creates balance. They help you see beyond your usual limits, and you help turn possibility into something workable. Their vision gives the idea room to grow. Your discernment helps it take shape.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry-mercury-trine-jupiter', 'relationship-mercury-trine-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-jupiter_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-jupiter_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Trine Jupiter', null, 'This is the person who reminds you of your potential when you forget it.

Talking with them tends to pull you out of whatever narrow frame you''ve been stuck in. You might bring up a problem or an idea you''re trying to make sense of, and somehow the conversation leaves you seeing more room to move than you did before. They have a way of reminding you that there is a bigger context, a larger story, or another path forward, and that shift in perspective can make you feel more confident about where you''re headed.

At its best, this is a relationship that supports growth. They encourage your ideas in a way that helps you believe in them more fully. When you lose sight of your progress, they remind you how far you have come and what you are working toward. They have a knack for placing today''s challenges within a larger context, helping you see meaning and possibility where you might otherwise focus only on the immediate problem. Their support feels empowering because they broaden your perspective while still leaving the decisions and direction in your hands.

This person helps you see the bigger picture when you''ve gotten stuck in doubt, details, or fear.

The challenge is not settling for inspiration by itself. It can feel rewarding to explore ideas together, imagine different futures, and get excited about what might be possible. But possibility only becomes meaningful when something is done with it. What makes this connection valuable is its ability to turn broad thinking into real direction, helping ideas move beyond discussion and into something tangible.

Take what gets illuminated between you and put it to use. Let the conversation become a choice, a direction, a next step. The wisdom here grows when possibility is given somewhere real to land.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This is the person who reminds you of your potential when you forget it.\n\nTalking with them tends to pull you out of whatever narrow frame you''ve been stuck in. You might bring up a problem or an idea you''re trying to make sense of, and somehow the conversation leaves you seeing more room to move than you did before. They have a way of reminding you that there is a bigger context, a larger story, or another path forward, and that shift in perspective can make you feel more confident about where you''re headed.\n\nAt its best, this is a relationship that supports growth. They encourage your ideas in a way that helps you believe in them more fully. When you lose sight of your progress, they remind you how far you have come and what you are working toward. They have a knack for placing today''s challenges within a larger context, helping you see meaning and possibility where you might otherwise focus only on the immediate problem. Their support feels empowering because they broaden your perspective while still leaving the decisions and direction in your hands.\n\nThis person helps you see the bigger picture when you''ve gotten stuck in doubt, details, or fear.\n\nThe challenge is not settling for inspiration by itself. It can feel rewarding to explore ideas together, imagine different futures, and get excited about what might be possible. But possibility only becomes meaningful when something is done with it. What makes this connection valuable is its ability to turn broad thinking into real direction, helping ideas move beyond discussion and into something tangible.\n\nTake what gets illuminated between you and put it to use. Let the conversation become a choice, a direction, a next step. The wisdom here grows when possibility is given somewhere real to land."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is not settling for inspiration by itself. It can feel rewarding to explore ideas together, imagine different futures, and get excited about what might be possible. But possibility only becomes meaningful when something is done with it. What makes this connection valuable is its ability to turn broad thinking into real direction, helping ideas move beyond discussion and into something tangible."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Take what gets illuminated between you and put it to use. Let the conversation become a choice, a direction, a next step. The wisdom here grows when possibility is given somewhere real to land."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-jupiter_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s growth. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This is the person who reminds you of your potential when you forget it.\n\nTalking with them tends to pull you out of whatever narrow frame you''ve been stuck in. You might bring up a problem or an idea you''re trying to make sense of, and somehow the conversation leaves you seeing more room to move than you did before. They have a way of reminding you that there is a bigger context, a larger story, or another path forward, and that shift in perspective can make you feel more confident about where you''re headed.\n\nAt its best, this is a relationship that supports growth. They encourage your ideas in a way that helps you believe in them more fully. When you lose sight of your progress, they remind you how far you have come and what you are working toward. They have a knack for placing today''s challenges within a larger context, helping you see meaning and possibility where you might otherwise focus only on the immediate problem. Their support feels empowering because they broaden your perspective while still leaving the decisions and direction in your hands.\n\nThis person helps you see the bigger picture when you''ve gotten stuck in doubt, details, or fear.\n\nThe challenge is not settling for inspiration by itself. It can feel rewarding to explore ideas together, imagine different futures, and get excited about what might be possible. But possibility only becomes meaningful when something is done with it. What makes this connection valuable is its ability to turn broad thinking into real direction, helping ideas move beyond discussion and into something tangible.\n\nTake what gets illuminated between you and put it to use. Let the conversation become a choice, a direction, a next step. The wisdom here grows when possibility is given somewhere real to land.","tension":"The challenge is not settling for inspiration by itself. It can feel rewarding to explore ideas together, imagine different futures, and get excited about what might be possible. But possibility only becomes meaningful when something is done with it. What makes this connection valuable is its ability to turn broad thinking into real direction, helping ideas move beyond discussion and into something tangible.","advice":"Take what gets illuminated between you and put it to use. Let the conversation become a choice, a direction, a next step. The wisdom here grows when possibility is given somewhere real to land.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"mars","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry-mercury-conjunction-mars', 'relationship-mercury-conjunction-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-mars_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-mars_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Conjunction Mars', null, 'Talking to this person can bring your thoughts to the surface before you have had time to organize them. There is something about the exchange between you that invites honesty, immediacy, and response. Conversations may feel alive. They may encourage you to speak more directly, trust your instincts, and engage with what is unfolding in the moment.

This connection pushes both people to be more honest and direct. This person may challenge your thinking, question your assumptions, or encourage you to say what you really mean. The conversations between you are meant to get to the truth.

You enjoy talking to each other. One thought leads to another, and conversations tend to keep moving. There is interest, curiosity, and a sense that both people have something to contribute.

The challenge is learning when to slow the conversation down. Both of you may be quick to respond, quick to react, or quick to move to the next point before fully taking in what was said. At times, this can create unnecessary tension or make a simple difference of opinion feel bigger than it is.

This aspect invites both people to pay attention to how and when things are said.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Talking to this person can bring your thoughts to the surface before you have had time to organize them. There is something about the exchange between you that invites honesty, immediacy, and response. Conversations may feel alive. They may encourage you to speak more directly, trust your instincts, and engage with what is unfolding in the moment.\n\nThis connection pushes both people to be more honest and direct. This person may challenge your thinking, question your assumptions, or encourage you to say what you really mean. The conversations between you are meant to get to the truth.\n\nYou enjoy talking to each other. One thought leads to another, and conversations tend to keep moving. There is interest, curiosity, and a sense that both people have something to contribute.\n\nThe challenge is learning when to slow the conversation down. Both of you may be quick to respond, quick to react, or quick to move to the next point before fully taking in what was said. At times, this can create unnecessary tension or make a simple difference of opinion feel bigger than it is.\n\nThis aspect invites both people to pay attention to how and when things are said."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is learning when to slow the conversation down. Both of you may be quick to respond, quick to react, or quick to move to the next point before fully taking in what was said. At times, this can create unnecessary tension or make a simple difference of opinion feel bigger than it is."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This aspect invites both people to pay attention to how and when things are said."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-mars_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Mind meets drive. The Mercury person''s thinking gets energized and quickened; the Mars person sharpens it into action. Stimulating, decisive, fast. At worst, conversations turn into arguments and words turn into weapons. Failure mode: bickering and cutting remarks. Aim the mental heat at problems, not at each other.","summaryDeep":"Talking to this person can bring your thoughts to the surface before you have had time to organize them. There is something about the exchange between you that invites honesty, immediacy, and response. Conversations may feel alive. They may encourage you to speak more directly, trust your instincts, and engage with what is unfolding in the moment.\n\nThis connection pushes both people to be more honest and direct. This person may challenge your thinking, question your assumptions, or encourage you to say what you really mean. The conversations between you are meant to get to the truth.\n\nYou enjoy talking to each other. One thought leads to another, and conversations tend to keep moving. There is interest, curiosity, and a sense that both people have something to contribute.\n\nThe challenge is learning when to slow the conversation down. Both of you may be quick to respond, quick to react, or quick to move to the next point before fully taking in what was said. At times, this can create unnecessary tension or make a simple difference of opinion feel bigger than it is.\n\nThis aspect invites both people to pay attention to how and when things are said.","tension":"The challenge is learning when to slow the conversation down. Both of you may be quick to respond, quick to react, or quick to move to the next point before fully taking in what was said. At times, this can create unnecessary tension or make a simple difference of opinion feel bigger than it is.","advice":"This aspect invites both people to pay attention to how and when things are said.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"mars","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry-mercury-opposition-mars', 'relationship-mercury-opposition-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-mars_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-mars_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Opposition Mars', null, 'This person may challenge the way you think. They often bring a different perspective, ask the question you were not expecting, or push back when you assume something is settled.

This can be frustrating, but it can also be clarifying. They may expose gaps in your reasoning, ideas you''ve taken for granted, or places where you are reacting instead of reflecting.

At its best, this connection sharpens both people. The tension between your viewpoints creates a fuller picture than either of you could reach alone.

The challenge is becoming attached to being right. When disagreement turns into defensiveness, the conversation stops teaching you anything.

The gift of this connection is learning through contrast. What this person questions may be exactly what helps you understand yourself more clearly.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may challenge the way you think. They often bring a different perspective, ask the question you were not expecting, or push back when you assume something is settled.\n\nThis can be frustrating, but it can also be clarifying. They may expose gaps in your reasoning, ideas you''ve taken for granted, or places where you are reacting instead of reflecting.\n\nAt its best, this connection sharpens both people. The tension between your viewpoints creates a fuller picture than either of you could reach alone.\n\nThe challenge is becoming attached to being right. When disagreement turns into defensiveness, the conversation stops teaching you anything.\n\nThe gift of this connection is learning through contrast. What this person questions may be exactly what helps you understand yourself more clearly."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is becoming attached to being right. When disagreement turns into defensiveness, the conversation stops teaching you anything."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The gift of this connection is learning through contrast. What this person questions may be exactly what helps you understand yourself more clearly."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-mars_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Thinking faces drive across the table. The Mercury person wants to discuss; the Mars person wants to act. Lively debate that can tip into argument, each finding the other too slow or too hasty. Failure mode: a constant low-grade fight. Let the debate sharpen you both rather than divide you.","summaryDeep":"This person may challenge the way you think. They often bring a different perspective, ask the question you were not expecting, or push back when you assume something is settled.\n\nThis can be frustrating, but it can also be clarifying. They may expose gaps in your reasoning, ideas you''ve taken for granted, or places where you are reacting instead of reflecting.\n\nAt its best, this connection sharpens both people. The tension between your viewpoints creates a fuller picture than either of you could reach alone.\n\nThe challenge is becoming attached to being right. When disagreement turns into defensiveness, the conversation stops teaching you anything.\n\nThe gift of this connection is learning through contrast. What this person questions may be exactly what helps you understand yourself more clearly.","tension":"The challenge is becoming attached to being right. When disagreement turns into defensiveness, the conversation stops teaching you anything.","advice":"The gift of this connection is learning through contrast. What this person questions may be exactly what helps you understand yourself more clearly.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"mars","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry-mercury-sextile-mars', 'relationship-mercury-sextile-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-mars_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-mars_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Sextile Mars', null, 'This person helps you get to the point.

They can help you put your thoughts into words, make decisions, and move conversations forward when you''ve been going in circles. Talking to them often feels productive. Ideas turn into plans. Questions get clearer. Problems feel easier to tackle.

The potential is there, but it usually takes some effort from both people. The more willing you are to talk things through, be honest, and stay engaged, the easier it is to understand each other and make progress together.

The challenge is not settling for what''s easy. It can be tempting to stick to familiar topics or avoid conversations that feel a little more vulnerable. But this connection tends to grow when both people are willing to go a bit deeper.

Be direct. The more openly you communicate, the more useful this connection becomes.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person helps you get to the point.\n\nThey can help you put your thoughts into words, make decisions, and move conversations forward when you''ve been going in circles. Talking to them often feels productive. Ideas turn into plans. Questions get clearer. Problems feel easier to tackle.\n\nThe potential is there, but it usually takes some effort from both people. The more willing you are to talk things through, be honest, and stay engaged, the easier it is to understand each other and make progress together.\n\nThe challenge is not settling for what''s easy. It can be tempting to stick to familiar topics or avoid conversations that feel a little more vulnerable. But this connection tends to grow when both people are willing to go a bit deeper.\n\nBe direct. The more openly you communicate, the more useful this connection becomes."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is not settling for what''s easy. It can be tempting to stick to familiar topics or avoid conversations that feel a little more vulnerable. But this connection tends to grow when both people are willing to go a bit deeper."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Be direct. The more openly you communicate, the more useful this connection becomes."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-mars_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Thinking and drive spark each other. The Mercury person supplies ideas, the Mars person the push to act on them. Good for getting things decided and done. Use it to turn talk into motion.","summaryDeep":"This person helps you get to the point.\n\nThey can help you put your thoughts into words, make decisions, and move conversations forward when you''ve been going in circles. Talking to them often feels productive. Ideas turn into plans. Questions get clearer. Problems feel easier to tackle.\n\nThe potential is there, but it usually takes some effort from both people. The more willing you are to talk things through, be honest, and stay engaged, the easier it is to understand each other and make progress together.\n\nThe challenge is not settling for what''s easy. It can be tempting to stick to familiar topics or avoid conversations that feel a little more vulnerable. But this connection tends to grow when both people are willing to go a bit deeper.\n\nBe direct. The more openly you communicate, the more useful this connection becomes.","tension":"The challenge is not settling for what''s easy. It can be tempting to stick to familiar topics or avoid conversations that feel a little more vulnerable. But this connection tends to grow when both people are willing to go a bit deeper.","advice":"Be direct. The more openly you communicate, the more useful this connection becomes.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-mars_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"mars","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-mars_square', 'synastry-mercury-square-mars', 'relationship-mercury-square-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-mars_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-mars_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Square Mars', null, 'This connection creates friction in communication. The way this person speaks, questions, or responds can easily trigger a reaction in you, and vice versa.

The challenge is not necessarily what is being said, but how quickly conversations become defensive. Small disagreements can escalate. Both people may feel misunderstood, criticized, or pressured to explain themselves.

The invitation of this aspect is deeper self-understanding. It shows you where your nervous system speeds up before your mind has a chance to catch up. It reveals the stories you tell yourself about being misunderstood, criticized, or unheard. And it asks both people to become more conscious of how they speak, listen, and respond.

The growth here comes from not reacting to every disagreement. This person will get under your skin sometimes. You will probably do the same to them. If both of you can stay in the conversation instead of immediately defending yourselves, you can learn a lot from the differences between you.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection creates friction in communication. The way this person speaks, questions, or responds can easily trigger a reaction in you, and vice versa.\n\nThe challenge is not necessarily what is being said, but how quickly conversations become defensive. Small disagreements can escalate. Both people may feel misunderstood, criticized, or pressured to explain themselves.\n\nThe invitation of this aspect is deeper self-understanding. It shows you where your nervous system speeds up before your mind has a chance to catch up. It reveals the stories you tell yourself about being misunderstood, criticized, or unheard. And it asks both people to become more conscious of how they speak, listen, and respond.\n\nThe growth here comes from not reacting to every disagreement. This person will get under your skin sometimes. You will probably do the same to them. If both of you can stay in the conversation instead of immediately defending yourselves, you can learn a lot from the differences between you."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The invitation of this aspect is deeper self-understanding. It shows you where your nervous system speeds up before your mind has a chance to catch up. It reveals the stories you tell yourself about being misunderstood, criticized, or unheard. And it asks both people to become more conscious of how they speak, listen, and respond."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The growth here comes from not reacting to every disagreement. This person will get under your skin sometimes. You will probably do the same to them. If both of you can stay in the conversation instead of immediately defending yourselves, you can learn a lot from the differences between you."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-mars_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Words grate against action. The Mercury person feels pushed or talked over; the Mars person finds the other''s talk slow or provoking. Sharp exchanges and a quick rise to friction. Failure mode: a couple who argue for sport and wound with words. Workable if both slow the reflex to snap; debate the idea, not the person.","summaryDeep":"This connection creates friction in communication. The way this person speaks, questions, or responds can easily trigger a reaction in you, and vice versa.\n\nThe challenge is not necessarily what is being said, but how quickly conversations become defensive. Small disagreements can escalate. Both people may feel misunderstood, criticized, or pressured to explain themselves.\n\nThe invitation of this aspect is deeper self-understanding. It shows you where your nervous system speeds up before your mind has a chance to catch up. It reveals the stories you tell yourself about being misunderstood, criticized, or unheard. And it asks both people to become more conscious of how they speak, listen, and respond.\n\nThe growth here comes from not reacting to every disagreement. This person will get under your skin sometimes. You will probably do the same to them. If both of you can stay in the conversation instead of immediately defending yourselves, you can learn a lot from the differences between you.","tension":"The invitation of this aspect is deeper self-understanding. It shows you where your nervous system speeds up before your mind has a chance to catch up. It reveals the stories you tell yourself about being misunderstood, criticized, or unheard. And it asks both people to become more conscious of how they speak, listen, and respond.","advice":"The growth here comes from not reacting to every disagreement. This person will get under your skin sometimes. You will probably do the same to them. If both of you can stay in the conversation instead of immediately defending yourselves, you can learn a lot from the differences between you.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-mars_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"mars","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-mars_trine', 'synastry-mercury-trine-mars', 'relationship-mercury-trine-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-mars_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-mars_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Trine Mars', null, 'You can be direct with each other without creating unnecessary conflict. Conversations tend to move quickly, honestly, and toward a solution. This person helps you say what you mean, and you help them do the same.

At its best, this aspect creates straightforward communication. Problems get discussed instead of avoided. Decisions get made instead of endlessly debated. There is a natural ability to challenge each other without taking it personally.

The strength of this connection is the way honesty can move between you without getting stuck. Conversations have a way of clearing the air. What needs to be said often finds its way to the surface, making it easier to address what matters instead of circling around it.

The gift here is the reminder that truth can be a catalyst. When you are willing to meet each other with openness and sincerity, insight becomes action, and understanding creates momentum.

Use the honesty while it is flowing. This connection works best when what gets said out loud turns into something you actually act on.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You can be direct with each other without creating unnecessary conflict. Conversations tend to move quickly, honestly, and toward a solution. This person helps you say what you mean, and you help them do the same.\n\nAt its best, this aspect creates straightforward communication. Problems get discussed instead of avoided. Decisions get made instead of endlessly debated. There is a natural ability to challenge each other without taking it personally.\n\nThe strength of this connection is the way honesty can move between you without getting stuck. Conversations have a way of clearing the air. What needs to be said often finds its way to the surface, making it easier to address what matters instead of circling around it.\n\nThe gift here is the reminder that truth can be a catalyst. When you are willing to meet each other with openness and sincerity, insight becomes action, and understanding creates momentum.\n\nUse the honesty while it is flowing. This connection works best when what gets said out loud turns into something you actually act on."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The gift here is the reminder that truth can be a catalyst. When you are willing to meet each other with openness and sincerity, insight becomes action, and understanding creates momentum."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Use the honesty while it is flowing. This connection works best when what gets said out loud turns into something you actually act on."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-mars_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Sharp thinking and decisive drive flow together. The Mercury person thinks fast, the Mars person acts on it cleanly; strong for problem-solving and momentum. An easy, stimulating working rhythm. Lean on it for projects and decisions.","summaryDeep":"You can be direct with each other without creating unnecessary conflict. Conversations tend to move quickly, honestly, and toward a solution. This person helps you say what you mean, and you help them do the same.\n\nAt its best, this aspect creates straightforward communication. Problems get discussed instead of avoided. Decisions get made instead of endlessly debated. There is a natural ability to challenge each other without taking it personally.\n\nThe strength of this connection is the way honesty can move between you without getting stuck. Conversations have a way of clearing the air. What needs to be said often finds its way to the surface, making it easier to address what matters instead of circling around it.\n\nThe gift here is the reminder that truth can be a catalyst. When you are willing to meet each other with openness and sincerity, insight becomes action, and understanding creates momentum.\n\nUse the honesty while it is flowing. This connection works best when what gets said out loud turns into something you actually act on.","tension":"The gift here is the reminder that truth can be a catalyst. When you are willing to meet each other with openness and sincerity, insight becomes action, and understanding creates momentum.","advice":"Use the honesty while it is flowing. This connection works best when what gets said out loud turns into something you actually act on.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry-mercury-conjunction-mercury', 'relationship-mercury-conjunction-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-mercury_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-mercury_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Conjunction Mercury', null, 'Talking to this person can feel easy right away. Your minds may move in a similar rhythm. You catch the reference. They get the joke. One of you starts a thought and the other already knows where it is going.

There is relief in this. You do not have to translate yourself as much. You can think out loud without feeling like every sentence needs a disclaimer. Conversation can move quickly because both people are already standing in the same mental room.

When this works, communication becomes one of the easiest parts of the relationship. You can talk for hours. You can move from practical to personal to ridiculous and back again. You can process life together in a way that makes both people feel less alone inside their own heads.

The lesson is discernment. Similar thinking can become a gift, but it can also become an echo chamber. You may agree too quickly. You may skip the same uncomfortable question. You may confirm each other''s version of the story because it feels good to be understood.

Do not let ease replace honesty. Use the mental connection to get clearer, not just more comfortable. Ask the question that interrupts the pattern. Tell the truth that sharpens the conversation. The gift here is not agreement. The gift is learning to think clearly together.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Talking to this person can feel easy right away. Your minds may move in a similar rhythm. You catch the reference. They get the joke. One of you starts a thought and the other already knows where it is going.\n\nThere is relief in this. You do not have to translate yourself as much. You can think out loud without feeling like every sentence needs a disclaimer. Conversation can move quickly because both people are already standing in the same mental room.\n\nWhen this works, communication becomes one of the easiest parts of the relationship. You can talk for hours. You can move from practical to personal to ridiculous and back again. You can process life together in a way that makes both people feel less alone inside their own heads.\n\nThe lesson is discernment. Similar thinking can become a gift, but it can also become an echo chamber. You may agree too quickly. You may skip the same uncomfortable question. You may confirm each other''s version of the story because it feels good to be understood.\n\nDo not let ease replace honesty. Use the mental connection to get clearer, not just more comfortable. Ask the question that interrupts the pattern. Tell the truth that sharpens the conversation. The gift here is not agreement. The gift is learning to think clearly together."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The lesson is discernment. Similar thinking can become a gift, but it can also become an echo chamber. You may agree too quickly. You may skip the same uncomfortable question. You may confirm each other''s version of the story because it feels good to be understood."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Do not let ease replace honesty. Use the mental connection to get clearer, not just more comfortable. Ask the question that interrupts the pattern. Tell the truth that sharpens the conversation. The gift here is not agreement. The gift is learning to think clearly together."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-mercury_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s mind. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"Talking to this person can feel easy right away. Your minds may move in a similar rhythm. You catch the reference. They get the joke. One of you starts a thought and the other already knows where it is going.\n\nThere is relief in this. You do not have to translate yourself as much. You can think out loud without feeling like every sentence needs a disclaimer. Conversation can move quickly because both people are already standing in the same mental room.\n\nWhen this works, communication becomes one of the easiest parts of the relationship. You can talk for hours. You can move from practical to personal to ridiculous and back again. You can process life together in a way that makes both people feel less alone inside their own heads.\n\nThe lesson is discernment. Similar thinking can become a gift, but it can also become an echo chamber. You may agree too quickly. You may skip the same uncomfortable question. You may confirm each other''s version of the story because it feels good to be understood.\n\nDo not let ease replace honesty. Use the mental connection to get clearer, not just more comfortable. Ask the question that interrupts the pattern. Tell the truth that sharpens the conversation. The gift here is not agreement. The gift is learning to think clearly together.","tension":"The lesson is discernment. Similar thinking can become a gift, but it can also become an echo chamber. You may agree too quickly. You may skip the same uncomfortable question. You may confirm each other''s version of the story because it feels good to be understood.","advice":"Do not let ease replace honesty. Use the mental connection to get clearer, not just more comfortable. Ask the question that interrupts the pattern. Tell the truth that sharpens the conversation. The gift here is not agreement. The gift is learning to think clearly together.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry-mercury-opposition-mercury', 'relationship-mercury-opposition-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-mercury_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-mercury_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Opposition Mercury', null, 'This person may hear the side of the story you did not lead with. They may ask the question you were trying to move past. They may slow you down when you want to get to the point, or push the conversation forward when you are still sorting through the details.

This can be irritating. It can also be useful.

One of you may speak to understand. The other may need time before words feel honest. One of you may want facts. The other may hear the emotional truth underneath the facts. One of you may look at the pattern. The other may stay with the specific thing that happened.

When this works, the difference gives the relationship range. You stop mistaking your first thought for the whole truth. This person can help you see what you missed. You can help them name what they are circling around. Together, you can build a fuller picture than either mind could build alone.

The challenge comes when the conversation becomes more focused on proving a point than understanding each other. One person explains, the other responds, and before long both of you are reacting instead of listening. Each person is working so hard to be understood that genuine understanding starts to disappear from the exchange.

The practice is simple, but it takes intention. Slow down enough to hear what they are actually saying instead of rushing toward your rebuttal. Get curious about the perspective behind their words. You do not have to agree with their conclusions to learn from them. Sometimes the very thing that frustrates you is the thing expanding your view. Respect the possibility that their mind is holding a piece of the truth that is harder for you to see from your side of the conversation.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may hear the side of the story you did not lead with. They may ask the question you were trying to move past. They may slow you down when you want to get to the point, or push the conversation forward when you are still sorting through the details.\n\nThis can be irritating. It can also be useful.\n\nOne of you may speak to understand. The other may need time before words feel honest. One of you may want facts. The other may hear the emotional truth underneath the facts. One of you may look at the pattern. The other may stay with the specific thing that happened.\n\nWhen this works, the difference gives the relationship range. You stop mistaking your first thought for the whole truth. This person can help you see what you missed. You can help them name what they are circling around. Together, you can build a fuller picture than either mind could build alone.\n\nThe challenge comes when the conversation becomes more focused on proving a point than understanding each other. One person explains, the other responds, and before long both of you are reacting instead of listening. Each person is working so hard to be understood that genuine understanding starts to disappear from the exchange.\n\nThe practice is simple, but it takes intention. Slow down enough to hear what they are actually saying instead of rushing toward your rebuttal. Get curious about the perspective behind their words. You do not have to agree with their conclusions to learn from them. Sometimes the very thing that frustrates you is the thing expanding your view. Respect the possibility that their mind is holding a piece of the truth that is harder for you to see from your side of the conversation."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge comes when the conversation becomes more focused on proving a point than understanding each other. One person explains, the other responds, and before long both of you are reacting instead of listening. Each person is working so hard to be understood that genuine understanding starts to disappear from the exchange."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The practice is simple, but it takes intention. Slow down enough to hear what they are actually saying instead of rushing toward your rebuttal. Get curious about the perspective behind their words. You do not have to agree with their conclusions to learn from them. Sometimes the very thing that frustrates you is the thing expanding your view. Respect the possibility that their mind is holding a piece of the truth that is harder for you to see from your side of the conversation."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-mercury_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s mind. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person may hear the side of the story you did not lead with. They may ask the question you were trying to move past. They may slow you down when you want to get to the point, or push the conversation forward when you are still sorting through the details.\n\nThis can be irritating. It can also be useful.\n\nOne of you may speak to understand. The other may need time before words feel honest. One of you may want facts. The other may hear the emotional truth underneath the facts. One of you may look at the pattern. The other may stay with the specific thing that happened.\n\nWhen this works, the difference gives the relationship range. You stop mistaking your first thought for the whole truth. This person can help you see what you missed. You can help them name what they are circling around. Together, you can build a fuller picture than either mind could build alone.\n\nThe challenge comes when the conversation becomes more focused on proving a point than understanding each other. One person explains, the other responds, and before long both of you are reacting instead of listening. Each person is working so hard to be understood that genuine understanding starts to disappear from the exchange.\n\nThe practice is simple, but it takes intention. Slow down enough to hear what they are actually saying instead of rushing toward your rebuttal. Get curious about the perspective behind their words. You do not have to agree with their conclusions to learn from them. Sometimes the very thing that frustrates you is the thing expanding your view. Respect the possibility that their mind is holding a piece of the truth that is harder for you to see from your side of the conversation.","tension":"The challenge comes when the conversation becomes more focused on proving a point than understanding each other. One person explains, the other responds, and before long both of you are reacting instead of listening. Each person is working so hard to be understood that genuine understanding starts to disappear from the exchange.","advice":"The practice is simple, but it takes intention. Slow down enough to hear what they are actually saying instead of rushing toward your rebuttal. Get curious about the perspective behind their words. You do not have to agree with their conclusions to learn from them. Sometimes the very thing that frustrates you is the thing expanding your view. Respect the possibility that their mind is holding a piece of the truth that is harder for you to see from your side of the conversation.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry-mercury-sextile-mercury', 'relationship-mercury-sextile-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-mercury_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-mercury_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Sextile Mercury', null, 'There is real potential here, but potential only matters when it is used. What grows between you is built through participation. Every conversation, every thoughtful question, every moment of genuine curiosity adds another layer of understanding. This is not the kind of bond that has to announce itself dramatically. It develops through small, consistent exchanges, through paying attention, through helping each other find language for something that was difficult to explain before.

When this works, conversation becomes more than communication. It becomes a place where you can find yourself again.

We all have moments when our thoughts feel tangled. You know something is bothering you, but you cannot quite name it. You start talking, circling around the issue, and then this person asks a question that brings the whole thing into focus. Not because they have all the answers, but because they help you hear your own.

You may notice that after talking with them, you feel less overwhelmed by what was happening inside your head. The problem may not be solved, but it feels more manageable.

The challenge is not the conversation itself. It is using it fully. When talking feels easy, it is tempting to stay on the surface.

Stay with the conversation long enough to discover something new about each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is real potential here, but potential only matters when it is used. What grows between you is built through participation. Every conversation, every thoughtful question, every moment of genuine curiosity adds another layer of understanding. This is not the kind of bond that has to announce itself dramatically. It develops through small, consistent exchanges, through paying attention, through helping each other find language for something that was difficult to explain before.\n\nWhen this works, conversation becomes more than communication. It becomes a place where you can find yourself again.\n\nWe all have moments when our thoughts feel tangled. You know something is bothering you, but you cannot quite name it. You start talking, circling around the issue, and then this person asks a question that brings the whole thing into focus. Not because they have all the answers, but because they help you hear your own.\n\nYou may notice that after talking with them, you feel less overwhelmed by what was happening inside your head. The problem may not be solved, but it feels more manageable.\n\nThe challenge is not the conversation itself. It is using it fully. When talking feels easy, it is tempting to stay on the surface.\n\nStay with the conversation long enough to discover something new about each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is not the conversation itself. It is using it fully. When talking feels easy, it is tempting to stay on the surface."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Stay with the conversation long enough to discover something new about each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-mercury_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s mind. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"There is real potential here, but potential only matters when it is used. What grows between you is built through participation. Every conversation, every thoughtful question, every moment of genuine curiosity adds another layer of understanding. This is not the kind of bond that has to announce itself dramatically. It develops through small, consistent exchanges, through paying attention, through helping each other find language for something that was difficult to explain before.\n\nWhen this works, conversation becomes more than communication. It becomes a place where you can find yourself again.\n\nWe all have moments when our thoughts feel tangled. You know something is bothering you, but you cannot quite name it. You start talking, circling around the issue, and then this person asks a question that brings the whole thing into focus. Not because they have all the answers, but because they help you hear your own.\n\nYou may notice that after talking with them, you feel less overwhelmed by what was happening inside your head. The problem may not be solved, but it feels more manageable.\n\nThe challenge is not the conversation itself. It is using it fully. When talking feels easy, it is tempting to stay on the surface.\n\nStay with the conversation long enough to discover something new about each other.","tension":"The challenge is not the conversation itself. It is using it fully. When talking feels easy, it is tempting to stay on the surface.","advice":"Stay with the conversation long enough to discover something new about each other.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-mercury_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-mercury_square', 'synastry-mercury-square-mercury', 'relationship-mercury-square-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-mercury_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-mercury_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Square Mercury', null, 'This person can make communication feel more complicated than either of you intends.

A casual comment picks up a tone you never meant. A simple question lands like criticism. You send a text that feels completely normal when you write it, only to discover it was received very differently on the other side. Before long, the conversation has drifted away from the original issue. Now you are trying to untangle what was said, how it was heard, and why the same misunderstanding seems to keep showing up between you.

This is the contact of crossed wires. Not because nobody cares. The problem is translation. Tone, timing, wording, assumptions. The small things that seem too minor to matter until they keep happening.

When this works, it asks both people to become more intentional with language. You cannot rely on assumptions or expect your words to carry the meaning you intended on their own. The invitation is to slow down and stay curious about the gap between your intention and their experience. Over time, you learn that good communication is not just about expressing yourself clearly. It is also about making sure the message lands.

The challenge is that repeated misunderstandings can slowly put both people on guard. Over time, you stop entering conversations with curiosity and start entering them with expectation. A normal question can sound like doubt. A pause can feel like judgment. A simple clarification can land as rejection. Before long, the conversation is carrying the weight of every previous misunderstanding before it has even had a chance to unfold.

This is where the real work begins. When communication breaks down, the temptation is to turn one difficult moment into a larger conclusion about the relationship. Resist that impulse. Slow the conversation down. Get curious before you get certain. Ask what they meant. Share what you heard. Check the story you are telling against what is actually happening. The goal is not perfect communication. The goal is to keep returning to clarity instead of punishing each other for the places where the message got distorted.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can make communication feel more complicated than either of you intends.\n\nA casual comment picks up a tone you never meant. A simple question lands like criticism. You send a text that feels completely normal when you write it, only to discover it was received very differently on the other side. Before long, the conversation has drifted away from the original issue. Now you are trying to untangle what was said, how it was heard, and why the same misunderstanding seems to keep showing up between you.\n\nThis is the contact of crossed wires. Not because nobody cares. The problem is translation. Tone, timing, wording, assumptions. The small things that seem too minor to matter until they keep happening.\n\nWhen this works, it asks both people to become more intentional with language. You cannot rely on assumptions or expect your words to carry the meaning you intended on their own. The invitation is to slow down and stay curious about the gap between your intention and their experience. Over time, you learn that good communication is not just about expressing yourself clearly. It is also about making sure the message lands.\n\nThe challenge is that repeated misunderstandings can slowly put both people on guard. Over time, you stop entering conversations with curiosity and start entering them with expectation. A normal question can sound like doubt. A pause can feel like judgment. A simple clarification can land as rejection. Before long, the conversation is carrying the weight of every previous misunderstanding before it has even had a chance to unfold.\n\nThis is where the real work begins. When communication breaks down, the temptation is to turn one difficult moment into a larger conclusion about the relationship. Resist that impulse. Slow the conversation down. Get curious before you get certain. Ask what they meant. Share what you heard. Check the story you are telling against what is actually happening. The goal is not perfect communication. The goal is to keep returning to clarity instead of punishing each other for the places where the message got distorted."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that repeated misunderstandings can slowly put both people on guard. Over time, you stop entering conversations with curiosity and start entering them with expectation. A normal question can sound like doubt. A pause can feel like judgment. A simple clarification can land as rejection. Before long, the conversation is carrying the weight of every previous misunderstanding before it has even had a chance to unfold."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This is where the real work begins. When communication breaks down, the temptation is to turn one difficult moment into a larger conclusion about the relationship. Resist that impulse. Slow the conversation down. Get curious before you get certain. Ask what they meant. Share what you heard. Check the story you are telling against what is actually happening. The goal is not perfect communication. The goal is to keep returning to clarity instead of punishing each other for the places where the message got distorted."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-mercury_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s mind. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This person can make communication feel more complicated than either of you intends.\n\nA casual comment picks up a tone you never meant. A simple question lands like criticism. You send a text that feels completely normal when you write it, only to discover it was received very differently on the other side. Before long, the conversation has drifted away from the original issue. Now you are trying to untangle what was said, how it was heard, and why the same misunderstanding seems to keep showing up between you.\n\nThis is the contact of crossed wires. Not because nobody cares. The problem is translation. Tone, timing, wording, assumptions. The small things that seem too minor to matter until they keep happening.\n\nWhen this works, it asks both people to become more intentional with language. You cannot rely on assumptions or expect your words to carry the meaning you intended on their own. The invitation is to slow down and stay curious about the gap between your intention and their experience. Over time, you learn that good communication is not just about expressing yourself clearly. It is also about making sure the message lands.\n\nThe challenge is that repeated misunderstandings can slowly put both people on guard. Over time, you stop entering conversations with curiosity and start entering them with expectation. A normal question can sound like doubt. A pause can feel like judgment. A simple clarification can land as rejection. Before long, the conversation is carrying the weight of every previous misunderstanding before it has even had a chance to unfold.\n\nThis is where the real work begins. When communication breaks down, the temptation is to turn one difficult moment into a larger conclusion about the relationship. Resist that impulse. Slow the conversation down. Get curious before you get certain. Ask what they meant. Share what you heard. Check the story you are telling against what is actually happening. The goal is not perfect communication. The goal is to keep returning to clarity instead of punishing each other for the places where the message got distorted.","tension":"The challenge is that repeated misunderstandings can slowly put both people on guard. Over time, you stop entering conversations with curiosity and start entering them with expectation. A normal question can sound like doubt. A pause can feel like judgment. A simple clarification can land as rejection. Before long, the conversation is carrying the weight of every previous misunderstanding before it has even had a chance to unfold.","advice":"This is where the real work begins. When communication breaks down, the temptation is to turn one difficult moment into a larger conclusion about the relationship. Resist that impulse. Slow the conversation down. Get curious before you get certain. Ask what they meant. Share what you heard. Check the story you are telling against what is actually happening. The goal is not perfect communication. The goal is to keep returning to clarity instead of punishing each other for the places where the message got distorted.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-mercury_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-mercury_trine', 'synastry-mercury-trine-mercury', 'relationship-mercury-trine-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-mercury_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-mercury_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Trine Mercury', null, 'Talking to this person can feel like finally putting down something heavy you did not realize you were carrying. Communication tends to flow naturally between you. You say what you mean, and they usually hear what you meant. There is less effort spent translating, defending, or correcting, which creates a sense of ease that can make the relationship feel supportive and steady.

This kind of ease matters. A relationship can have chemistry, affection, loyalty, and history, but if the two of you cannot talk to each other in a way that creates understanding, everything eventually starts to feel heavier than it needs to. Here, communication can become a stabilizing force that helps both people stay connected even when life becomes complicated. Problems are easier to name because neither person has to spend as much energy defending themselves before the conversation has even begun. Repairs tend to happen more quickly because misunderstandings can be addressed before they grow into larger stories. Even silence does not automatically feel like distance, because there is enough trust in the connection to believe that the relationship still exists between the conversations.

When this works, communication becomes a source of trust. You can say what you actually mean instead of rehearsing it first. You can bring up something uncomfortable without assuming it will become a problem. Even when you disagree, there is usually enough understanding underneath the conversation to keep both people connected.

The challenge with easy communication is assuming it will take care of itself. It is tempting to rely on the fact that you usually understand each other. But relationships change. People change.

Keep staying curious. Let the conversation keep evolving as the relationship evolves. The real gift is not the ease itself. It is having enough trust in the connection to tell the truth more deeply as time goes on.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Talking to this person can feel like finally putting down something heavy you did not realize you were carrying. Communication tends to flow naturally between you. You say what you mean, and they usually hear what you meant. There is less effort spent translating, defending, or correcting, which creates a sense of ease that can make the relationship feel supportive and steady.\n\nThis kind of ease matters. A relationship can have chemistry, affection, loyalty, and history, but if the two of you cannot talk to each other in a way that creates understanding, everything eventually starts to feel heavier than it needs to. Here, communication can become a stabilizing force that helps both people stay connected even when life becomes complicated. Problems are easier to name because neither person has to spend as much energy defending themselves before the conversation has even begun. Repairs tend to happen more quickly because misunderstandings can be addressed before they grow into larger stories. Even silence does not automatically feel like distance, because there is enough trust in the connection to believe that the relationship still exists between the conversations.\n\nWhen this works, communication becomes a source of trust. You can say what you actually mean instead of rehearsing it first. You can bring up something uncomfortable without assuming it will become a problem. Even when you disagree, there is usually enough understanding underneath the conversation to keep both people connected.\n\nThe challenge with easy communication is assuming it will take care of itself. It is tempting to rely on the fact that you usually understand each other. But relationships change. People change.\n\nKeep staying curious. Let the conversation keep evolving as the relationship evolves. The real gift is not the ease itself. It is having enough trust in the connection to tell the truth more deeply as time goes on."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge with easy communication is assuming it will take care of itself. It is tempting to rely on the fact that you usually understand each other. But relationships change. People change."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Keep staying curious. Let the conversation keep evolving as the relationship evolves. The real gift is not the ease itself. It is having enough trust in the connection to tell the truth more deeply as time goes on."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-mercury_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s mind. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"Talking to this person can feel like finally putting down something heavy you did not realize you were carrying. Communication tends to flow naturally between you. You say what you mean, and they usually hear what you meant. There is less effort spent translating, defending, or correcting, which creates a sense of ease that can make the relationship feel supportive and steady.\n\nThis kind of ease matters. A relationship can have chemistry, affection, loyalty, and history, but if the two of you cannot talk to each other in a way that creates understanding, everything eventually starts to feel heavier than it needs to. Here, communication can become a stabilizing force that helps both people stay connected even when life becomes complicated. Problems are easier to name because neither person has to spend as much energy defending themselves before the conversation has even begun. Repairs tend to happen more quickly because misunderstandings can be addressed before they grow into larger stories. Even silence does not automatically feel like distance, because there is enough trust in the connection to believe that the relationship still exists between the conversations.\n\nWhen this works, communication becomes a source of trust. You can say what you actually mean instead of rehearsing it first. You can bring up something uncomfortable without assuming it will become a problem. Even when you disagree, there is usually enough understanding underneath the conversation to keep both people connected.\n\nThe challenge with easy communication is assuming it will take care of itself. It is tempting to rely on the fact that you usually understand each other. But relationships change. People change.\n\nKeep staying curious. Let the conversation keep evolving as the relationship evolves. The real gift is not the ease itself. It is having enough trust in the connection to tell the truth more deeply as time goes on.","tension":"The challenge with easy communication is assuming it will take care of itself. It is tempting to rely on the fact that you usually understand each other. But relationships change. People change.","advice":"Keep staying curious. Let the conversation keep evolving as the relationship evolves. The real gift is not the ease itself. It is having enough trust in the connection to tell the truth more deeply as time goes on.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"moon","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry-mercury-conjunction-moon', 'relationship-mercury-conjunction-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-moon_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-moon_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Conjunction Moon', null, 'This person may help you find words for feelings you usually keep inside. Something about the way they listen, ask, or respond can make your inner world feel easier to name.

When this works, it can feel incredibly validating. You may start talking and realize they are following the emotional thread, not just the facts. They can help you understand why something affected you, why a small thing felt bigger than it looked, or why you could not simply "move on" when part of you was still holding the feeling.

There is a quiet intimacy in this. You may feel less alone with your moods because someone can meet them with language. They may help you hear yourself more clearly. Not by telling you who you are, but by giving shape to something you were already feeling.

The challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.

Let the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may help you find words for feelings you usually keep inside. Something about the way they listen, ask, or respond can make your inner world feel easier to name.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel incredibly validating. You may start talking and realize they are following the emotional thread, not just the facts. They can help you understand why something affected you, why a small thing felt bigger than it looked, or why you could not simply \"move on\" when part of you was still holding the feeling.\n\nThere is a quiet intimacy in this. You may feel less alone with your moods because someone can meet them with language. They may help you hear yourself more clearly. Not by telling you who you are, but by giving shape to something you were already feeling.\n\nThe challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.\n\nLet the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-moon_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s feelings. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person may help you find words for feelings you usually keep inside. Something about the way they listen, ask, or respond can make your inner world feel easier to name.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel incredibly validating. You may start talking and realize they are following the emotional thread, not just the facts. They can help you understand why something affected you, why a small thing felt bigger than it looked, or why you could not simply \"move on\" when part of you was still holding the feeling.\n\nThere is a quiet intimacy in this. You may feel less alone with your moods because someone can meet them with language. They may help you hear yourself more clearly. Not by telling you who you are, but by giving shape to something you were already feeling.\n\nThe challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.\n\nLet the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace.","tension":"The challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.","advice":"Let the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"moon","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry-mercury-opposition-moon', 'relationship-mercury-opposition-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-moon_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-moon_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Opposition Moon', null, 'You and this person may process things in very different ways. One of you may need to talk in order to understand what is happening. The other may need quiet before the words come. One person reaches for language. The other is still trying to feel their way through.

This can create a real mismatch in emotional timing. They may ask questions when you need comfort. You may go quiet when they need a conversation. They may think they are helping by making sense of the feeling, while you feel like they are standing outside of it and explaining it back to you.

At its best, this connection teaches both people range. The person with words learns that not everything needs to be solved out loud. The person with feeling learns that language can become a bridge, not a threat. You both get better at translating inner experience into something the other person can actually meet.

The harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other.

The practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, "I need comfort right now," or "I need help making sense of this." Clear language can soften the whole pattern.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You and this person may process things in very different ways. One of you may need to talk in order to understand what is happening. The other may need quiet before the words come. One person reaches for language. The other is still trying to feel their way through.\n\nThis can create a real mismatch in emotional timing. They may ask questions when you need comfort. You may go quiet when they need a conversation. They may think they are helping by making sense of the feeling, while you feel like they are standing outside of it and explaining it back to you.\n\nAt its best, this connection teaches both people range. The person with words learns that not everything needs to be solved out loud. The person with feeling learns that language can become a bridge, not a threat. You both get better at translating inner experience into something the other person can actually meet.\n\nThe harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other.\n\nThe practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, \"I need comfort right now,\" or \"I need help making sense of this.\" Clear language can soften the whole pattern."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, \"I need comfort right now,\" or \"I need help making sense of this.\" Clear language can soften the whole pattern."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-moon_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s feelings. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"You and this person may process things in very different ways. One of you may need to talk in order to understand what is happening. The other may need quiet before the words come. One person reaches for language. The other is still trying to feel their way through.\n\nThis can create a real mismatch in emotional timing. They may ask questions when you need comfort. You may go quiet when they need a conversation. They may think they are helping by making sense of the feeling, while you feel like they are standing outside of it and explaining it back to you.\n\nAt its best, this connection teaches both people range. The person with words learns that not everything needs to be solved out loud. The person with feeling learns that language can become a bridge, not a threat. You both get better at translating inner experience into something the other person can actually meet.\n\nThe harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other.\n\nThe practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, \"I need comfort right now,\" or \"I need help making sense of this.\" Clear language can soften the whole pattern.","tension":"The harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other.","advice":"The practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, \"I need comfort right now,\" or \"I need help making sense of this.\" Clear language can soften the whole pattern.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-moon_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"moon","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-moon_sextile', 'synastry-mercury-sextile-moon', 'relationship-mercury-sextile-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-moon_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-moon_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Sextile Moon', null, 'There is a natural opening here, but it grows when someone uses it.

This person may be easy to talk to about emotional things. They may not always pull everything out of you, but when you choose to share, the conversation can become grounding. You may leave the exchange feeling clearer, softer, or more connected to what you actually feel.

When this works, the connection builds through small moments of emotional honesty. A check-in that becomes real. A question that helps you name the thing underneath the thing. A conversation that starts casually and ends with both people feeling a little more understood.

The strength here is gentle consistency. This person may help you trust that your feelings have a place to go. Not every emotion needs to become a crisis. Not every conversation needs to go deep. But over time, the willingness to listen, ask, and respond with care creates safety.

The challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.

Open the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is a natural opening here, but it grows when someone uses it.\n\nThis person may be easy to talk to about emotional things. They may not always pull everything out of you, but when you choose to share, the conversation can become grounding. You may leave the exchange feeling clearer, softer, or more connected to what you actually feel.\n\nWhen this works, the connection builds through small moments of emotional honesty. A check-in that becomes real. A question that helps you name the thing underneath the thing. A conversation that starts casually and ends with both people feeling a little more understood.\n\nThe strength here is gentle consistency. This person may help you trust that your feelings have a place to go. Not every emotion needs to become a crisis. Not every conversation needs to go deep. But over time, the willingness to listen, ask, and respond with care creates safety.\n\nThe challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.\n\nOpen the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Open the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-moon_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s feelings. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"There is a natural opening here, but it grows when someone uses it.\n\nThis person may be easy to talk to about emotional things. They may not always pull everything out of you, but when you choose to share, the conversation can become grounding. You may leave the exchange feeling clearer, softer, or more connected to what you actually feel.\n\nWhen this works, the connection builds through small moments of emotional honesty. A check-in that becomes real. A question that helps you name the thing underneath the thing. A conversation that starts casually and ends with both people feeling a little more understood.\n\nThe strength here is gentle consistency. This person may help you trust that your feelings have a place to go. Not every emotion needs to become a crisis. Not every conversation needs to go deep. But over time, the willingness to listen, ask, and respond with care creates safety.\n\nThe challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.\n\nOpen the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly.","tension":"The challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.","advice":"Open the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly.","policy"