le can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood.\n\nThe more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there.","tension":"The challenge is that affection does not always arrive in a recognizable form. One person may think they are showing care, while the other does not feel cared for at all. What one person sees as thoughtful may feel distant to the other. What feels sincere may feel awkward. What seems obvious may not register at all.\n\nBoth people can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood.","advice":"The more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"venus","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry-mercury-sextile-venus', 'relationship-mercury-sextile-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-venus_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-venus_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Sextile Venus', null, 'There is a natural opening for warmth here, but it grows when it is expressed. This person may be easy to talk to not only because of what they say, but because of how their mind meets yours. You may enjoy the way they think, the details they notice, the questions they ask, or the way they help a conversation unfold. There is often appreciation present from the beginning. The invitation is to share it.

This connection deepens when appreciation is spoken aloud. Let this person know what you value about them. Reflect back something they shared that stayed with you. Acknowledge the impact their words or actions have had. These small moments of recognition build trust over time. The more you practice naming what matters, the more supported, understood, and connected both of you are likely to feel.

Two people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.

You strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is a natural opening for warmth here, but it grows when it is expressed. This person may be easy to talk to not only because of what they say, but because of how their mind meets yours. You may enjoy the way they think, the details they notice, the questions they ask, or the way they help a conversation unfold. There is often appreciation present from the beginning. The invitation is to share it.\n\nThis connection deepens when appreciation is spoken aloud. Let this person know what you value about them. Reflect back something they shared that stayed with you. Acknowledge the impact their words or actions have had. These small moments of recognition build trust over time. The more you practice naming what matters, the more supported, understood, and connected both of you are likely to feel.\n\nTwo people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.\n\nYou strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Two people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"You strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-venus_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s love and values. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"There is a natural opening for warmth here, but it grows when it is expressed. This person may be easy to talk to not only because of what they say, but because of how their mind meets yours. You may enjoy the way they think, the details they notice, the questions they ask, or the way they help a conversation unfold. There is often appreciation present from the beginning. The invitation is to share it.\n\nThis connection deepens when appreciation is spoken aloud. Let this person know what you value about them. Reflect back something they shared that stayed with you. Acknowledge the impact their words or actions have had. These small moments of recognition build trust over time. The more you practice naming what matters, the more supported, understood, and connected both of you are likely to feel.\n\nTwo people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.\n\nYou strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference.","tension":"Two people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.","advice":"You strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-venus_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"venus","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-venus_square', 'synastry-mercury-square-venus', 'relationship-mercury-square-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-venus_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-venus_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Square Venus', null, 'This is the quiet distance between what one person says and what the other person needs to feel loved. It lives in a tender, specific place: the gap between being drawn to someone and actually feeling understood by them.

You may find yourself attracted and irritated in nearly the same breath. Something about this person''s mind, their humor, the particular way they put things, pulls you in. And then the same mouth that charmed you says something that lands wrong, and you feel the pull and the friction at once, unsure which one to trust.

Sometimes the mismatch is loud. One of you is too blunt, the other too careful. One wants the truth laid bare, the other wants it handled gently. But more often it is subtle, almost too small to name. A compliment that arrives slightly off. A joke that grazes a nerve. A conversation that was supposed to bring you closer and instead leaves one of you a little lonelier than before it started.

Because this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm.

The work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own version of it. We tend to offer love in the language we would want to receive it, and then feel hurt when it does not translate. What lands as tender to you may read as flat to them. What feels honest to them may feel sharp to you.

This is the slow practice the square asks for. Not better chemistry, you already have that. The harder thing: learning how this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This is the quiet distance between what one person says and what the other person needs to feel loved. It lives in a tender, specific place: the gap between being drawn to someone and actually feeling understood by them.\n\nYou may find yourself attracted and irritated in nearly the same breath. Something about this person''s mind, their humor, the particular way they put things, pulls you in. And then the same mouth that charmed you says something that lands wrong, and you feel the pull and the friction at once, unsure which one to trust.\n\nSometimes the mismatch is loud. One of you is too blunt, the other too careful. One wants the truth laid bare, the other wants it handled gently. But more often it is subtle, almost too small to name. A compliment that arrives slightly off. A joke that grazes a nerve. A conversation that was supposed to bring you closer and instead leaves one of you a little lonelier than before it started.\n\nBecause this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm.\n\nThe work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own version of it. We tend to offer love in the language we would want to receive it, and then feel hurt when it does not translate. What lands as tender to you may read as flat to them. What feels honest to them may feel sharp to you.\n\nThis is the slow practice the square asks for. Not better chemistry, you already have that. The harder thing: learning how this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Because this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own version of it. We tend to offer love in the language we would want to receive it, and then feel hurt when it does not translate. What lands as tender to you may read as flat to them. What feels honest to them may feel sharp to you.\n\nThis is the slow practice the square asks for. Not better chemistry, you already have that. The harder thing: learning how this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-venus_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s love and values. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This is the quiet distance between what one person says and what the other person needs to feel loved. It lives in a tender, specific place: the gap between being drawn to someone and actually feeling understood by them.\n\nYou may find yourself attracted and irritated in nearly the same breath. Something about this person''s mind, their humor, the particular way they put things, pulls you in. And then the same mouth that charmed you says something that lands wrong, and you feel the pull and the friction at once, unsure which one to trust.\n\nSometimes the mismatch is loud. One of you is too blunt, the other too careful. One wants the truth laid bare, the other wants it handled gently. But more often it is subtle, almost too small to name. A compliment that arrives slightly off. A joke that grazes a nerve. A conversation that was supposed to bring you closer and instead leaves one of you a little lonelier than before it started.\n\nBecause this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm.\n\nThe work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own version of it. We tend to offer love in the language we would want to receive it, and then feel hurt when it does not translate. What lands as tender to you may read as flat to them. What feels honest to them may feel sharp to you.\n\nThis is the slow practice the square asks for. Not better chemistry, you already have that. The harder thing: learning how this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed.","tension":"Because this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm.","advice":"The work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own version of it. We tend to offer love in the language we would want to receive it, and then feel hurt when it does not translate. What lands as tender to you may read as flat to them. What feels honest to them may feel sharp to you.\n\nThis is the slow practice the square asks for. Not better chemistry, you already have that. The harder thing: learning how this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-venus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"venus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-venus_trine', 'synastry-mercury-trine-venus', 'relationship-mercury-trine-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-venus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-venus_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Trine Venus', null, 'With this person, a lot of the attraction is in the conversation.

You may just enjoy talking to them. You like hearing what they have to say. Maybe they make you laugh, tell good stories, or notice things other people miss. Conversation can feel easy because you genuinely enjoy being around them.

When this works, affection tends to show up through everyday conversation. The text that makes you laugh when you''re having a bad day. The little check-in. The running joke that somehow never gets old. Whatever the relationship is, there is often a feeling of being understood through words. You don''t always have to spell out that you care about each other. It''s already there in how you talk.

One of the nicest things about this connection is feeling seen. This person may put something into words that you''ve been trying to explain for months. They may understand what you''re getting at before you''ve fully figured it out yourself. There can be a real sense of, "Oh, that''s exactly what I meant."

The thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.

The connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"With this person, a lot of the attraction is in the conversation.\n\nYou may just enjoy talking to them. You like hearing what they have to say. Maybe they make you laugh, tell good stories, or notice things other people miss. Conversation can feel easy because you genuinely enjoy being around them.\n\nWhen this works, affection tends to show up through everyday conversation. The text that makes you laugh when you''re having a bad day. The little check-in. The running joke that somehow never gets old. Whatever the relationship is, there is often a feeling of being understood through words. You don''t always have to spell out that you care about each other. It''s already there in how you talk.\n\nOne of the nicest things about this connection is feeling seen. This person may put something into words that you''ve been trying to explain for months. They may understand what you''re getting at before you''ve fully figured it out yourself. There can be a real sense of, \"Oh, that''s exactly what I meant.\"\n\nThe thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.\n\nThe connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-venus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s love and values. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"With this person, a lot of the attraction is in the conversation.\n\nYou may just enjoy talking to them. You like hearing what they have to say. Maybe they make you laugh, tell good stories, or notice things other people miss. Conversation can feel easy because you genuinely enjoy being around them.\n\nWhen this works, affection tends to show up through everyday conversation. The text that makes you laugh when you''re having a bad day. The little check-in. The running joke that somehow never gets old. Whatever the relationship is, there is often a feeling of being understood through words. You don''t always have to spell out that you care about each other. It''s already there in how you talk.\n\nOne of the nicest things about this connection is feeling seen. This person may put something into words that you''ve been trying to explain for months. They may understand what you''re getting at before you''ve fully figured it out yourself. There can be a real sense of, \"Oh, that''s exactly what I meant.\"\n\nThe thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.\n\nThe connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it.","tension":"The thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.","advice":"The connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-jupiter_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-jupiter_conjunction', 'synastry-moon-conjunction-jupiter', 'relationship-moon-conjunction-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-jupiter_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-jupiter_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Conjunction Jupiter', null, 'This person has a way of reminding you that your feelings deserve room to exist.

Their care can feel abundant. Their instinct is often to meet your emotions with generosity rather than judgment, encouragement rather than criticism. Around them it may feel easier to believe that what you are carrying does not have to be carried alone.

This person makes it easier to be yourself. Their response to your feelings is usually support, not judgment, so opening up feels safer than it does with most people. When life is hard, they remind you that you do not have to carry it alone. When life is good, they are genuinely happy for you. Around them, it is easier to trust your own feelings, ask for what you need, and believe that things can get better.

One thing to watch for is using comfort to avoid the truth. You may rush to make each other feel better instead of staying with what the feeling is trying to tell you.

Take the support. Face the problem anyway. This connection is strongest when the encouragement helps you deal with hard things instead of avoiding them.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a way of reminding you that your feelings deserve room to exist.\n\nTheir care can feel abundant. Their instinct is often to meet your emotions with generosity rather than judgment, encouragement rather than criticism. Around them it may feel easier to believe that what you are carrying does not have to be carried alone.\n\nThis person makes it easier to be yourself. Their response to your feelings is usually support, not judgment, so opening up feels safer than it does with most people. When life is hard, they remind you that you do not have to carry it alone. When life is good, they are genuinely happy for you. Around them, it is easier to trust your own feelings, ask for what you need, and believe that things can get better.\n\nOne thing to watch for is using comfort to avoid the truth. You may rush to make each other feel better instead of staying with what the feeling is trying to tell you.\n\nTake the support. Face the problem anyway. This connection is strongest when the encouragement helps you deal with hard things instead of avoiding them."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"One thing to watch for is using comfort to avoid the truth. You may rush to make each other feel better instead of staying with what the feeling is trying to tell you."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Take the support. Face the problem anyway. This connection is strongest when the encouragement helps you deal with hard things instead of avoiding them."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-jupiter_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s growth. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person has a way of reminding you that your feelings deserve room to exist.\n\nTheir care can feel abundant. Their instinct is often to meet your emotions with generosity rather than judgment, encouragement rather than criticism. Around them it may feel easier to believe that what you are carrying does not have to be carried alone.\n\nThis person makes it easier to be yourself. Their response to your feelings is usually support, not judgment, so opening up feels safer than it does with most people. When life is hard, they remind you that you do not have to carry it alone. When life is good, they are genuinely happy for you. Around them, it is easier to trust your own feelings, ask for what you need, and believe that things can get better.\n\nOne thing to watch for is using comfort to avoid the truth. You may rush to make each other feel better instead of staying with what the feeling is trying to tell you.\n\nTake the support. Face the problem anyway. This connection is strongest when the encouragement helps you deal with hard things instead of avoiding them.","tension":"One thing to watch for is using comfort to avoid the truth. You may rush to make each other feel better instead of staying with what the feeling is trying to tell you.","advice":"Take the support. Face the problem anyway. This connection is strongest when the encouragement helps you deal with hard things instead of avoiding them.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-jupiter_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-jupiter_opposition', 'synastry-moon-opposition-jupiter', 'relationship-moon-opposition-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-jupiter_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-jupiter_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Opposition Jupiter', null, 'This person gives emotional warmth freely, and sometimes it feels like more than you want.

They often respond to your feelings with encouragement, reassurance, or a desire to help. While their intentions are genuine, there may be moments when you feel like they are trying to move you past an emotion before you have had the chance to fully experience it. What feels supportive to them can sometimes leave you feeling unseen.

At its best, this connection teaches both of you something important. They remind you that you do not have to carry everything alone, and that support can be offered freely. You remind them that some feelings need to be witnessed before they can be healed. Not every difficult moment needs a solution right away.

They offer comfort when you want understanding, and they feel rejected when their care does not land. Neither of you is wrong. You are speaking different emotional languages.

Say what you need. Let their warmth in without letting it override your experience.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person gives emotional warmth freely, and sometimes it feels like more than you want.\n\nThey often respond to your feelings with encouragement, reassurance, or a desire to help. While their intentions are genuine, there may be moments when you feel like they are trying to move you past an emotion before you have had the chance to fully experience it. What feels supportive to them can sometimes leave you feeling unseen.\n\nAt its best, this connection teaches both of you something important. They remind you that you do not have to carry everything alone, and that support can be offered freely. You remind them that some feelings need to be witnessed before they can be healed. Not every difficult moment needs a solution right away.\n\nThey offer comfort when you want understanding, and they feel rejected when their care does not land. Neither of you is wrong. You are speaking different emotional languages.\n\nSay what you need. Let their warmth in without letting it override your experience."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"They offer comfort when you want understanding, and they feel rejected when their care does not land. Neither of you is wrong. You are speaking different emotional languages."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Say what you need. Let their warmth in without letting it override your experience."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-jupiter_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s growth. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person gives emotional warmth freely, and sometimes it feels like more than you want.\n\nThey often respond to your feelings with encouragement, reassurance, or a desire to help. While their intentions are genuine, there may be moments when you feel like they are trying to move you past an emotion before you have had the chance to fully experience it. What feels supportive to them can sometimes leave you feeling unseen.\n\nAt its best, this connection teaches both of you something important. They remind you that you do not have to carry everything alone, and that support can be offered freely. You remind them that some feelings need to be witnessed before they can be healed. Not every difficult moment needs a solution right away.\n\nThey offer comfort when you want understanding, and they feel rejected when their care does not land. Neither of you is wrong. You are speaking different emotional languages.\n\nSay what you need. Let their warmth in without letting it override your experience.","tension":"They offer comfort when you want understanding, and they feel rejected when their care does not land. Neither of you is wrong. You are speaking different emotional languages.","advice":"Say what you need. Let their warmth in without letting it override your experience.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry-moon-sextile-jupiter', 'relationship-moon-sextile-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-jupiter_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-jupiter_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Sextile Jupiter', null, 'Support in this connection grows when you actually let each other in.

There''s a natural sense of goodwill here. This person wants good things for you, and you probably want the same for them. But the closeness doesn''t happen automatically. It builds little by little, every time you share something real and find that it''s met with care instead of judgment.

What makes this connection special isn''t some huge emotional breakthrough. It''s the small stuff. Feeling listened to. Feeling remembered. Knowing someone notices when you''re having a hard time. Realizing you don''t have to handle everything on your own.

Because the support is gentle rather than overwhelming, it''s easy to miss. You might assume they know what''s going on without ever saying it. You might keep things to yourself until you''re already struggling, then wonder why the connection doesn''t feel as supportive as it could.

The more you let this person be part of your emotional world, the stronger the bond becomes. The more honest you are about what''s going on, the more room there is for real support. What starts as simple kindness can grow into something deeply comforting and reliable over time.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Support in this connection grows when you actually let each other in.\n\nThere''s a natural sense of goodwill here. This person wants good things for you, and you probably want the same for them. But the closeness doesn''t happen automatically. It builds little by little, every time you share something real and find that it''s met with care instead of judgment.\n\nWhat makes this connection special isn''t some huge emotional breakthrough. It''s the small stuff. Feeling listened to. Feeling remembered. Knowing someone notices when you''re having a hard time. Realizing you don''t have to handle everything on your own.\n\nBecause the support is gentle rather than overwhelming, it''s easy to miss. You might assume they know what''s going on without ever saying it. You might keep things to yourself until you''re already struggling, then wonder why the connection doesn''t feel as supportive as it could.\n\nThe more you let this person be part of your emotional world, the stronger the bond becomes. The more honest you are about what''s going on, the more room there is for real support. What starts as simple kindness can grow into something deeply comforting and reliable over time."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Because the support is gentle rather than overwhelming, it''s easy to miss. You might assume they know what''s going on without ever saying it. You might keep things to yourself until you''re already struggling, then wonder why the connection doesn''t feel as supportive as it could."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The more you let this person be part of your emotional world, the stronger the bond becomes. The more honest you are about what''s going on, the more room there is for real support. What starts as simple kindness can grow into something deeply comforting and reliable over time."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-jupiter_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s growth. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"Support in this connection grows when you actually let each other in.\n\nThere''s a natural sense of goodwill here. This person wants good things for you, and you probably want the same for them. But the closeness doesn''t happen automatically. It builds little by little, every time you share something real and find that it''s met with care instead of judgment.\n\nWhat makes this connection special isn''t some huge emotional breakthrough. It''s the small stuff. Feeling listened to. Feeling remembered. Knowing someone notices when you''re having a hard time. Realizing you don''t have to handle everything on your own.\n\nBecause the support is gentle rather than overwhelming, it''s easy to miss. You might assume they know what''s going on without ever saying it. You might keep things to yourself until you''re already struggling, then wonder why the connection doesn''t feel as supportive as it could.\n\nThe more you let this person be part of your emotional world, the stronger the bond becomes. The more honest you are about what''s going on, the more room there is for real support. What starts as simple kindness can grow into something deeply comforting and reliable over time.","tension":"Because the support is gentle rather than overwhelming, it''s easy to miss. You might assume they know what''s going on without ever saying it. You might keep things to yourself until you''re already struggling, then wonder why the connection doesn''t feel as supportive as it could.","advice":"The more you let this person be part of your emotional world, the stronger the bond becomes. The more honest you are about what''s going on, the more room there is for real support. What starts as simple kindness can grow into something deeply comforting and reliable over time.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-jupiter_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-jupiter_square', 'synastry-moon-square-jupiter', 'relationship-moon-square-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-jupiter_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-jupiter_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Square Jupiter', null, 'This person cares about how you feel, but they do not always know how to be with your feelings.

When you are hurting, they often respond by trying to make the pain feel lighter. Their care comes through reassurance, perspective, and a belief that things can improve. Even when their intentions are good, you may sometimes feel rushed past what you are actually experiencing. What you need in those moments is not a brighter outlook but the feeling that someone truly understands where you are before trying to fix it.

That can be a lonely feeling. You may know they care about you and still feel like something important got missed. You leave the interaction feeling comforted on the surface, but the deeper part of your experience remains untouched. Their optimism can feel reassuring when you need hope and frustrating when you need understanding.

At its best, this connection helps you carry your feelings without getting lost in them. They remind you that what hurts right now is not the whole story. When you feel overwhelmed, they bring perspective, helping you step back from the emotion without dismissing it and remember that there is still room for hope.

The challenge is making room for both truth and comfort. If every difficult feeling gets softened too quickly, important emotions get skipped over. If every attempt at reassurance is rejected, genuine care goes unnoticed.

The more you can meet in the middle, the more supported and understood you both feel.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person cares about how you feel, but they do not always know how to be with your feelings.\n\nWhen you are hurting, they often respond by trying to make the pain feel lighter. Their care comes through reassurance, perspective, and a belief that things can improve. Even when their intentions are good, you may sometimes feel rushed past what you are actually experiencing. What you need in those moments is not a brighter outlook but the feeling that someone truly understands where you are before trying to fix it.\n\nThat can be a lonely feeling. You may know they care about you and still feel like something important got missed. You leave the interaction feeling comforted on the surface, but the deeper part of your experience remains untouched. Their optimism can feel reassuring when you need hope and frustrating when you need understanding.\n\nAt its best, this connection helps you carry your feelings without getting lost in them. They remind you that what hurts right now is not the whole story. When you feel overwhelmed, they bring perspective, helping you step back from the emotion without dismissing it and remember that there is still room for hope.\n\nThe challenge is making room for both truth and comfort. If every difficult feeling gets softened too quickly, important emotions get skipped over. If every attempt at reassurance is rejected, genuine care goes unnoticed.\n\nThe more you can meet in the middle, the more supported and understood you both feel."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is making room for both truth and comfort. If every difficult feeling gets softened too quickly, important emotions get skipped over. If every attempt at reassurance is rejected, genuine care goes unnoticed."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The more you can meet in the middle, the more supported and understood you both feel."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-jupiter_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s growth. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This person cares about how you feel, but they do not always know how to be with your feelings.\n\nWhen you are hurting, they often respond by trying to make the pain feel lighter. Their care comes through reassurance, perspective, and a belief that things can improve. Even when their intentions are good, you may sometimes feel rushed past what you are actually experiencing. What you need in those moments is not a brighter outlook but the feeling that someone truly understands where you are before trying to fix it.\n\nThat can be a lonely feeling. You may know they care about you and still feel like something important got missed. You leave the interaction feeling comforted on the surface, but the deeper part of your experience remains untouched. Their optimism can feel reassuring when you need hope and frustrating when you need understanding.\n\nAt its best, this connection helps you carry your feelings without getting lost in them. They remind you that what hurts right now is not the whole story. When you feel overwhelmed, they bring perspective, helping you step back from the emotion without dismissing it and remember that there is still room for hope.\n\nThe challenge is making room for both truth and comfort. If every difficult feeling gets softened too quickly, important emotions get skipped over. If every attempt at reassurance is rejected, genuine care goes unnoticed.\n\nThe more you can meet in the middle, the more supported and understood you both feel.","tension":"The challenge is making room for both truth and comfort. If every difficult feeling gets softened too quickly, important emotions get skipped over. If every attempt at reassurance is rejected, genuine care goes unnoticed.","advice":"The more you can meet in the middle, the more supported and understood you both feel.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry-moon-trine-jupiter', 'relationship-moon-trine-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-jupiter_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-jupiter_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Trine Jupiter', null, 'This person has a way of making you feel emotionally supported without drawing attention to it.

Around them, your feelings seem to have somewhere soft to land. Instead of feeling examined or questioned, you often feel received. There is a sense that your inner world makes sense to them, even when you are struggling to make sense of it yourself.

One of the gifts of this connection is the feeling that someone is beside you when life gets heavy. They have a way of helping you remember that a difficult moment is not the whole story, while still respecting the reality of what you are going through. Their support can make it easier to breathe, easier to trust that things will move forward, and easier to feel less alone with whatever you are carrying.

Being cared for this consistently can change something in you. When someone meets your feelings with warmth instead of judgment, you stop bracing for rejection. It becomes easier to trust what you feel, ask for support when you need it, and believe your needs matter.

The challenge is not conflict but complacency. Because the support is so reliable, it can fade into the background. You may forget how much this connection contributes to your well-being, or stop actively nurturing something that feels like it will always be there.

Notice what this person brings into your life. Let yourself receive it fully, and make sure you give it value in return.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a way of making you feel emotionally supported without drawing attention to it.\n\nAround them, your feelings seem to have somewhere soft to land. Instead of feeling examined or questioned, you often feel received. There is a sense that your inner world makes sense to them, even when you are struggling to make sense of it yourself.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is the feeling that someone is beside you when life gets heavy. They have a way of helping you remember that a difficult moment is not the whole story, while still respecting the reality of what you are going through. Their support can make it easier to breathe, easier to trust that things will move forward, and easier to feel less alone with whatever you are carrying.\n\nBeing cared for this consistently can change something in you. When someone meets your feelings with warmth instead of judgment, you stop bracing for rejection. It becomes easier to trust what you feel, ask for support when you need it, and believe your needs matter.\n\nThe challenge is not conflict but complacency. Because the support is so reliable, it can fade into the background. You may forget how much this connection contributes to your well-being, or stop actively nurturing something that feels like it will always be there.\n\nNotice what this person brings into your life. Let yourself receive it fully, and make sure you give it value in return."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is not conflict but complacency. Because the support is so reliable, it can fade into the background. You may forget how much this connection contributes to your well-being, or stop actively nurturing something that feels like it will always be there."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Notice what this person brings into your life. Let yourself receive it fully, and make sure you give it value in return."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-jupiter_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s growth. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This person has a way of making you feel emotionally supported without drawing attention to it.\n\nAround them, your feelings seem to have somewhere soft to land. Instead of feeling examined or questioned, you often feel received. There is a sense that your inner world makes sense to them, even when you are struggling to make sense of it yourself.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is the feeling that someone is beside you when life gets heavy. They have a way of helping you remember that a difficult moment is not the whole story, while still respecting the reality of what you are going through. Their support can make it easier to breathe, easier to trust that things will move forward, and easier to feel less alone with whatever you are carrying.\n\nBeing cared for this consistently can change something in you. When someone meets your feelings with warmth instead of judgment, you stop bracing for rejection. It becomes easier to trust what you feel, ask for support when you need it, and believe your needs matter.\n\nThe challenge is not conflict but complacency. Because the support is so reliable, it can fade into the background. You may forget how much this connection contributes to your well-being, or stop actively nurturing something that feels like it will always be there.\n\nNotice what this person brings into your life. Let yourself receive it fully, and make sure you give it value in return.","tension":"The challenge is not conflict but complacency. Because the support is so reliable, it can fade into the background. You may forget how much this connection contributes to your well-being, or stop actively nurturing something that feels like it will always be there.","advice":"Notice what this person brings into your life. Let yourself receive it fully, and make sure you give it value in return.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mars","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry-moon-conjunction-mars', 'relationship-moon-conjunction-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mars_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mars_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Conjunction Mars', null, 'This person can get right under your skin, sometimes in a good way and sometimes not. Around them, your feelings may come up faster than usual. You may feel drawn in, stirred up, irritated, comforted, or more honest than you expected to be. It is hard to stay detached when someone touches this part of you.

There can be something very immediate about the bond. This person may make you feel wanted in a way that is hard to miss. They may not always say the softest thing, but you can feel that they are present. They respond. They engage. They do not treat your emotions like an inconvenience. If you are used to people going vague or quiet when things get intense, that can feel like a relief.

When this works, it can feel protective. You may feel like they would show up for you if something went wrong, or that they care enough to react when you are hurt. There is a kind of warmth here that is not always gentle, but still feels real.

The problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.

Notice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can get right under your skin, sometimes in a good way and sometimes not. Around them, your feelings may come up faster than usual. You may feel drawn in, stirred up, irritated, comforted, or more honest than you expected to be. It is hard to stay detached when someone touches this part of you.\n\nThere can be something very immediate about the bond. This person may make you feel wanted in a way that is hard to miss. They may not always say the softest thing, but you can feel that they are present. They respond. They engage. They do not treat your emotions like an inconvenience. If you are used to people going vague or quiet when things get intense, that can feel like a relief.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel protective. You may feel like they would show up for you if something went wrong, or that they care enough to react when you are hurt. There is a kind of warmth here that is not always gentle, but still feels real.\n\nThe problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.\n\nNotice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Notice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mars_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s drive. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person can get right under your skin, sometimes in a good way and sometimes not. Around them, your feelings may come up faster than usual. You may feel drawn in, stirred up, irritated, comforted, or more honest than you expected to be. It is hard to stay detached when someone touches this part of you.\n\nThere can be something very immediate about the bond. This person may make you feel wanted in a way that is hard to miss. They may not always say the softest thing, but you can feel that they are present. They respond. They engage. They do not treat your emotions like an inconvenience. If you are used to people going vague or quiet when things get intense, that can feel like a relief.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel protective. You may feel like they would show up for you if something went wrong, or that they care enough to react when you are hurt. There is a kind of warmth here that is not always gentle, but still feels real.\n\nThe problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.\n\nNotice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship.","tension":"The problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.","advice":"Notice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mars","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry-moon-opposition-mars', 'relationship-moon-opposition-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mars_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mars_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Opposition Mars', null, 'This person can pull a strong reaction out of you, but relaxing into it may not always be easy. You may want closeness from them and still feel like you have to brace yourself. They may come toward you with energy when what you really wanted was patience. Or they may think they are helping, while you feel rushed, handled, or pushed past your own pace.

A lot of the tension here comes from timing. One person is ready to act, while the other is still trying to feel their way through the moment. One person wants to fix it, while the other wants to be understood first. Nobody has to be wrong for both people to end up frustrated.

When this works, it can make the relationship more honest. This person may get you to say the thing you were trying not to say. They may make it harder for you to hide behind "I''m fine" when you are clearly not fine. That can be uncomfortable, but it can also be exactly what brings the truth into the room.

The hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.

Slow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can pull a strong reaction out of you, but relaxing into it may not always be easy. You may want closeness from them and still feel like you have to brace yourself. They may come toward you with energy when what you really wanted was patience. Or they may think they are helping, while you feel rushed, handled, or pushed past your own pace.\n\nA lot of the tension here comes from timing. One person is ready to act, while the other is still trying to feel their way through the moment. One person wants to fix it, while the other wants to be understood first. Nobody has to be wrong for both people to end up frustrated.\n\nWhen this works, it can make the relationship more honest. This person may get you to say the thing you were trying not to say. They may make it harder for you to hide behind \"I''m fine\" when you are clearly not fine. That can be uncomfortable, but it can also be exactly what brings the truth into the room.\n\nThe hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.\n\nSlow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Slow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mars_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s drive. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person can pull a strong reaction out of you, but relaxing into it may not always be easy. You may want closeness from them and still feel like you have to brace yourself. They may come toward you with energy when what you really wanted was patience. Or they may think they are helping, while you feel rushed, handled, or pushed past your own pace.\n\nA lot of the tension here comes from timing. One person is ready to act, while the other is still trying to feel their way through the moment. One person wants to fix it, while the other wants to be understood first. Nobody has to be wrong for both people to end up frustrated.\n\nWhen this works, it can make the relationship more honest. This person may get you to say the thing you were trying not to say. They may make it harder for you to hide behind \"I''m fine\" when you are clearly not fine. That can be uncomfortable, but it can also be exactly what brings the truth into the room.\n\nThe hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.\n\nSlow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you.","tension":"The hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.","advice":"Slow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mars","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry-moon-sextile-mars', 'relationship-moon-sextile-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mars_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mars_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Sextile Mars', null, 'This connection may not announce itself as loudly as the conjunction or square, but there is something here that responds when one of you reaches for it. The warmth grows when someone checks in, speaks honestly, follows through, or shows care in a way the other person can actually feel.

This is a contact where action matters. Not dramatic action, necessarily. More like showing up when you said you would. Asking the question instead of guessing. Helping with the thing that has been sitting there too long. Making it clear, through behavior, that the other person is not dealing with everything alone.

When this works, both people feel a little more willing to engage. One person says what they want, and the other has something to respond to. One person makes a move, and the connection gets warmer. The care becomes easier to trust because it is not only talked about. It is shown.

The hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to.

Do not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection may not announce itself as loudly as the conjunction or square, but there is something here that responds when one of you reaches for it. The warmth grows when someone checks in, speaks honestly, follows through, or shows care in a way the other person can actually feel.\n\nThis is a contact where action matters. Not dramatic action, necessarily. More like showing up when you said you would. Asking the question instead of guessing. Helping with the thing that has been sitting there too long. Making it clear, through behavior, that the other person is not dealing with everything alone.\n\nWhen this works, both people feel a little more willing to engage. One person says what they want, and the other has something to respond to. One person makes a move, and the connection gets warmer. The care becomes easier to trust because it is not only talked about. It is shown.\n\nThe hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to.\n\nDo not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Do not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mars_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s drive. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This connection may not announce itself as loudly as the conjunction or square, but there is something here that responds when one of you reaches for it. The warmth grows when someone checks in, speaks honestly, follows through, or shows care in a way the other person can actually feel.\n\nThis is a contact where action matters. Not dramatic action, necessarily. More like showing up when you said you would. Asking the question instead of guessing. Helping with the thing that has been sitting there too long. Making it clear, through behavior, that the other person is not dealing with everything alone.\n\nWhen this works, both people feel a little more willing to engage. One person says what they want, and the other has something to respond to. One person makes a move, and the connection gets warmer. The care becomes easier to trust because it is not only talked about. It is shown.\n\nThe hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to.\n\nDo not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do.","tension":"The hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to.","advice":"Do not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mars_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mars","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mars_square', 'synastry-moon-square-mars', 'relationship-moon-square-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mars_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mars_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Square Mars', 'This aspect can make feelings move fast. One person''s emotional reactions may trigger the other person''s defensiveness, desire, impatience, or anger before either of them has time to think.', 'The Moon person brings feeling. Mars brings heat. When these two square each other, the connection can feel alive, reactive, physical, and easily inflamed.

The Mars person may stir something immediate in the Moon person. Want, irritation, attraction, vulnerability, defensiveness. The Moon person may make the Mars person feel needed, challenged, provoked, or emotionally cornered. Neither person has to be trying to start something for the temperature to rise.

This can create chemistry, but it can also create conflict that feels personal fast. A small comment can land like an attack. A mood can feel like a demand. A need can be heard as criticism. If the bond is close, both people may need to learn how to pause before reacting.

This aspect is not gentle, but it is honest. It shows where instinct and emotion collide. Used well, it can create courage, protection, passion, and emotional directness. Used poorly, it becomes irritation, impatience, and fights that are really about feeling unsafe.

It may show up as quick attraction, arguments that start suddenly, feeling protective or provoked, emotional needs coming out as anger, or making up quickly and then repeating the same fight.

One person''s feelings can feel like pressure. The other person''s actions can feel insensitive or too forceful.

Slow the reaction down. Ask what hurt before defending what you meant. Do not turn every feeling into a fight.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"The Moon person brings feeling. Mars brings heat. When these two square each other, the connection can feel alive, reactive, physical, and easily inflamed.\n\nThe Mars person may stir something immediate in the Moon person. Want, irritation, attraction, vulnerability, defensiveness. The Moon person may make the Mars person feel needed, challenged, provoked, or emotionally cornered. Neither person has to be trying to start something for the temperature to rise.\n\nThis can create chemistry, but it can also create conflict that feels personal fast. A small comment can land like an attack. A mood can feel like a demand. A need can be heard as criticism. If the bond is close, both people may need to learn how to pause before reacting.\n\nThis aspect is not gentle, but it is honest. It shows where instinct and emotion collide. Used well, it can create courage, protection, passion, and emotional directness. Used poorly, it becomes irritation, impatience, and fights that are really about feeling unsafe.\n\nIt may show up as quick attraction, arguments that start suddenly, feeling protective or provoked, emotional needs coming out as anger, or making up quickly and then repeating the same fight."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"One person''s feelings can feel like pressure. The other person''s actions can feel insensitive or too forceful."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Slow the reaction down. Ask what hurt before defending what you meant. Do not turn every feeling into a fight."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mars_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"This aspect can make feelings move fast. One person''s emotional reactions may trigger the other person''s defensiveness, desire, impatience, or anger before either of them has time to think.","summaryDeep":"The Moon person brings feeling. Mars brings heat. When these two square each other, the connection can feel alive, reactive, physical, and easily inflamed.\n\nThe Mars person may stir something immediate in the Moon person. Want, irritation, attraction, vulnerability, defensiveness. The Moon person may make the Mars person feel needed, challenged, provoked, or emotionally cornered. Neither person has to be trying to start something for the temperature to rise.\n\nThis can create chemistry, but it can also create conflict that feels personal fast. A small comment can land like an attack. A mood can feel like a demand. A need can be heard as criticism. If the bond is close, both people may need to learn how to pause before reacting.\n\nThis aspect is not gentle, but it is honest. It shows where instinct and emotion collide. Used well, it can create courage, protection, passion, and emotional directness. Used poorly, it becomes irritation, impatience, and fights that are really about feeling unsafe.\n\nIt may show up as quick attraction, arguments that start suddenly, feeling protective or provoked, emotional needs coming out as anger, or making up quickly and then repeating the same fight.","tension":"One person''s feelings can feel like pressure. The other person''s actions can feel insensitive or too forceful.","advice":"Slow the reaction down. Ask what hurt before defending what you meant. Do not turn every feeling into a fight.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Gold standard Batch 2. Gift: passion, honesty, protection, emotional courage, and the ability to act on what is felt. Shadow: defensiveness, irritation, emotional reactivity, sexual tension turning into conflict, or confusing intensity with closeness.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mars_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mars","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mars_trine', 'synastry-moon-trine-mars', 'relationship-moon-trine-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mars_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mars_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Trine Mars', null, 'This person may stir something in you without making you feel unsafe. They can bring out a more honest, alive version of you, but it does not have to feel like a battle. Around them, you may find it easier to say what you feel, act on what matters, or stop sitting on something that needs your attention.

There is a good kind of responsiveness here. If you are upset, they may not freeze or disappear. If something matters to you, they may take it seriously. You can feel supported by their presence because they do not just listen from a distance. They seem willing to meet the feeling and do something with it.

When this works, comfort and heat can sit together. You may feel wanted without feeling pressured. You may feel protected without feeling controlled. The connection can make both people a little braver with their feelings, not because anyone is forcing it, but because the energy between you makes honesty feel possible.

The only real risk is letting this good rhythm go unused. Because it is easier than the harder Moon-Mars contacts, you may not notice how much it helps. The support is there, but it still needs somewhere to go.

Use it. Say what you feel. Act on the care. Let the trust between you become something you actually build with.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may stir something in you without making you feel unsafe. They can bring out a more honest, alive version of you, but it does not have to feel like a battle. Around them, you may find it easier to say what you feel, act on what matters, or stop sitting on something that needs your attention.\n\nThere is a good kind of responsiveness here. If you are upset, they may not freeze or disappear. If something matters to you, they may take it seriously. You can feel supported by their presence because they do not just listen from a distance. They seem willing to meet the feeling and do something with it.\n\nWhen this works, comfort and heat can sit together. You may feel wanted without feeling pressured. You may feel protected without feeling controlled. The connection can make both people a little braver with their feelings, not because anyone is forcing it, but because the energy between you makes honesty feel possible.\n\nThe only real risk is letting this good rhythm go unused. Because it is easier than the harder Moon-Mars contacts, you may not notice how much it helps. The support is there, but it still needs somewhere to go.\n\nUse it. Say what you feel. Act on the care. Let the trust between you become something you actually build with."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The only real risk is letting this good rhythm go unused. Because it is easier than the harder Moon-Mars contacts, you may not notice how much it helps. The support is there, but it still needs somewhere to go."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Use it. Say what you feel. Act on the care. Let the trust between you become something you actually build with."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mars_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s drive. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This person may stir something in you without making you feel unsafe. They can bring out a more honest, alive version of you, but it does not have to feel like a battle. Around them, you may find it easier to say what you feel, act on what matters, or stop sitting on something that needs your attention.\n\nThere is a good kind of responsiveness here. If you are upset, they may not freeze or disappear. If something matters to you, they may take it seriously. You can feel supported by their presence because they do not just listen from a distance. They seem willing to meet the feeling and do something with it.\n\nWhen this works, comfort and heat can sit together. You may feel wanted without feeling pressured. You may feel protected without feeling controlled. The connection can make both people a little braver with their feelings, not because anyone is forcing it, but because the energy between you makes honesty feel possible.\n\nThe only real risk is letting this good rhythm go unused. Because it is easier than the harder Moon-Mars contacts, you may not notice how much it helps. The support is there, but it still needs somewhere to go.\n\nUse it. Say what you feel. Act on the care. Let the trust between you become something you actually build with.","tension":"The only real risk is letting this good rhythm go unused. Because it is easier than the harder Moon-Mars contacts, you may not notice how much it helps. The support is there, but it still needs somewhere to go.","advice":"Use it. Say what you feel. Act on the care. Let the trust between you become something you actually build with.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry-moon-conjunction-mercury', 'relationship-moon-conjunction-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mercury_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mercury_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Conjunction Mercury', null, 'This person may help you find words for feelings you usually keep inside. Something about the way they listen, ask, or respond can make your inner world feel easier to name.

When this works, it can feel incredibly validating. You may start talking and realize they are following the emotional thread, not just the facts. They can help you understand why something affected you, why a small thing felt bigger than it looked, or why you could not simply "move on" when part of you was still holding the feeling.

There is a quiet intimacy in this. You may feel less alone with your moods because someone can meet them with language. They may help you hear yourself more clearly. Not by telling you who you are, but by giving shape to something you were already feeling.

The challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.

Let the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may help you find words for feelings you usually keep inside. Something about the way they listen, ask, or respond can make your inner world feel easier to name.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel incredibly validating. You may start talking and realize they are following the emotional thread, not just the facts. They can help you understand why something affected you, why a small thing felt bigger than it looked, or why you could not simply \"move on\" when part of you was still holding the feeling.\n\nThere is a quiet intimacy in this. You may feel less alone with your moods because someone can meet them with language. They may help you hear yourself more clearly. Not by telling you who you are, but by giving shape to something you were already feeling.\n\nThe challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.\n\nLet the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mercury_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s mind. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person may help you find words for feelings you usually keep inside. Something about the way they listen, ask, or respond can make your inner world feel easier to name.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel incredibly validating. You may start talking and realize they are following the emotional thread, not just the facts. They can help you understand why something affected you, why a small thing felt bigger than it looked, or why you could not simply \"move on\" when part of you was still holding the feeling.\n\nThere is a quiet intimacy in this. You may feel less alone with your moods because someone can meet them with language. They may help you hear yourself more clearly. Not by telling you who you are, but by giving shape to something you were already feeling.\n\nThe challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.\n\nLet the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace.","tension":"The challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.","advice":"Let the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry-moon-opposition-mercury', 'relationship-moon-opposition-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mercury_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mercury_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Opposition Mercury', null, 'You and this person may process things in very different ways. One of you may need to talk in order to understand what is happening. The other may need quiet before the words come. One person reaches for language. The other is still trying to feel their way through.

This can create a real mismatch in emotional timing. They may ask questions when you need comfort. You may go quiet when they need a conversation. They may think they are helping by making sense of the feeling, while you feel like they are standing outside of it and explaining it back to you.

At its best, this connection teaches both people range. The person with words learns that not everything needs to be solved out loud. The person with feeling learns that language can become a bridge, not a threat. You both get better at translating inner experience into something the other person can actually meet.

The harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other.

The practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, "I need comfort right now," or "I need help making sense of this." Clear language can soften the whole pattern.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You and this person may process things in very different ways. One of you may need to talk in order to understand what is happening. The other may need quiet before the words come. One person reaches for language. The other is still trying to feel their way through.\n\nThis can create a real mismatch in emotional timing. They may ask questions when you need comfort. You may go quiet when they need a conversation. They may think they are helping by making sense of the feeling, while you feel like they are standing outside of it and explaining it back to you.\n\nAt its best, this connection teaches both people range. The person with words learns that not everything needs to be solved out loud. The person with feeling learns that language can become a bridge, not a threat. You both get better at translating inner experience into something the other person can actually meet.\n\nThe harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other.\n\nThe practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, \"I need comfort right now,\" or \"I need help making sense of this.\" Clear language can soften the whole pattern."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, \"I need comfort right now,\" or \"I need help making sense of this.\" Clear language can soften the whole pattern."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mercury_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s mind. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"You and this person may process things in very different ways. One of you may need to talk in order to understand what is happening. The other may need quiet before the words come. One person reaches for language. The other is still trying to feel their way through.\n\nThis can create a real mismatch in emotional timing. They may ask questions when you need comfort. You may go quiet when they need a conversation. They may think they are helping by making sense of the feeling, while you feel like they are standing outside of it and explaining it back to you.\n\nAt its best, this connection teaches both people range. The person with words learns that not everything needs to be solved out loud. The person with feeling learns that language can become a bridge, not a threat. You both get better at translating inner experience into something the other person can actually meet.\n\nThe harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other.\n\nThe practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, \"I need comfort right now,\" or \"I need help making sense of this.\" Clear language can soften the whole pattern.","tension":"The harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other.","advice":"The practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, \"I need comfort right now,\" or \"I need help making sense of this.\" Clear language can soften the whole pattern.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry-moon-sextile-mercury', 'relationship-moon-sextile-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mercury_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mercury_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Sextile Mercury', null, 'There is a natural opening here, but it grows when someone uses it.

This person may be easy to talk to about emotional things. They may not always pull everything out of you, but when you choose to share, the conversation can become grounding. You may leave the exchange feeling clearer, softer, or more connected to what you actually feel.

When this works, the connection builds through small moments of emotional honesty. A check-in that becomes real. A question that helps you name the thing underneath the thing. A conversation that starts casually and ends with both people feeling a little more understood.

The strength here is gentle consistency. This person may help you trust that your feelings have a place to go. Not every emotion needs to become a crisis. Not every conversation needs to go deep. But over time, the willingness to listen, ask, and respond with care creates safety.

The challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.

Open the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is a natural opening here, but it grows when someone uses it.\n\nThis person may be easy to talk to about emotional things. They may not always pull everything out of you, but when you choose to share, the conversation can become grounding. You may leave the exchange feeling clearer, softer, or more connected to what you actually feel.\n\nWhen this works, the connection builds through small moments of emotional honesty. A check-in that becomes real. A question that helps you name the thing underneath the thing. A conversation that starts casually and ends with both people feeling a little more understood.\n\nThe strength here is gentle consistency. This person may help you trust that your feelings have a place to go. Not every emotion needs to become a crisis. Not every conversation needs to go deep. But over time, the willingness to listen, ask, and respond with care creates safety.\n\nThe challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.\n\nOpen the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Open the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mercury_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s mind. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"There is a natural opening here, but it grows when someone uses it.\n\nThis person may be easy to talk to about emotional things. They may not always pull everything out of you, but when you choose to share, the conversation can become grounding. You may leave the exchange feeling clearer, softer, or more connected to what you actually feel.\n\nWhen this works, the connection builds through small moments of emotional honesty. A check-in that becomes real. A question that helps you name the thing underneath the thing. A conversation that starts casually and ends with both people feeling a little more understood.\n\nThe strength here is gentle consistency. This person may help you trust that your feelings have a place to go. Not every emotion needs to become a crisis. Not every conversation needs to go deep. But over time, the willingness to listen, ask, and respond with care creates safety.\n\nThe challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.\n\nOpen the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly.","tension":"The challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.","advice":"Open the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mercury_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mercury_square', 'synastry-moon-square-mercury', 'relationship-moon-square-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mercury_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mercury_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Square Mercury', null, 'This person may say the thing in a way that lands wrong.

They may ask a simple question and it feels like criticism. They may try to explain your feelings and it sounds like they are correcting you. They may reach for logic at the exact moment you need warmth. The problem is not always what they say. It is how it lands in your body.

This can become exhausting if it keeps happening. You may start bracing before the conversation even begins. They may feel like they are trying to help, while you feel like you are being studied. You may feel pressured to explain your emotions clearly before you have even had a chance to understand them yourself.

When this works, it can make both people more skilled. You learn to say what you feel more directly. They learn to listen without rushing to organize or solve. The friction becomes useful when both people stop defending their method and start caring about the impact.

The deeper challenge is the temptation to become certain too quickly. One person decides they already know what the feeling means. The other decides they are not being heard. Then the conversation becomes less about understanding and more about protection.

Slow down. Put comfort before analysis. Say what landed. Ask what was meant. This connection improves when both people stop treating emotional clarity as something that can be forced.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may say the thing in a way that lands wrong.\n\nThey may ask a simple question and it feels like criticism. They may try to explain your feelings and it sounds like they are correcting you. They may reach for logic at the exact moment you need warmth. The problem is not always what they say. It is how it lands in your body.\n\nThis can become exhausting if it keeps happening. You may start bracing before the conversation even begins. They may feel like they are trying to help, while you feel like you are being studied. You may feel pressured to explain your emotions clearly before you have even had a chance to understand them yourself.\n\nWhen this works, it can make both people more skilled. You learn to say what you feel more directly. They learn to listen without rushing to organize or solve. The friction becomes useful when both people stop defending their method and start caring about the impact.\n\nThe deeper challenge is the temptation to become certain too quickly. One person decides they already know what the feeling means. The other decides they are not being heard. Then the conversation becomes less about understanding and more about protection.\n\nSlow down. Put comfort before analysis. Say what landed. Ask what was meant. This connection improves when both people stop treating emotional clarity as something that can be forced."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The deeper challenge is the temptation to become certain too quickly. One person decides they already know what the feeling means. The other decides they are not being heard. Then the conversation becomes less about understanding and more about protection."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Slow down. Put comfort before analysis. Say what landed. Ask what was meant. This connection improves when both people stop treating emotional clarity as something that can be forced."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mercury_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s mind. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This person may say the thing in a way that lands wrong.\n\nThey may ask a simple question and it feels like criticism. They may try to explain your feelings and it sounds like they are correcting you. They may reach for logic at the exact moment you need warmth. The problem is not always what they say. It is how it lands in your body.\n\nThis can become exhausting if it keeps happening. You may start bracing before the conversation even begins. They may feel like they are trying to help, while you feel like you are being studied. You may feel pressured to explain your emotions clearly before you have even had a chance to understand them yourself.\n\nWhen this works, it can make both people more skilled. You learn to say what you feel more directly. They learn to listen without rushing to organize or solve. The friction becomes useful when both people stop defending their method and start caring about the impact.\n\nThe deeper challenge is the temptation to become certain too quickly. One person decides they already know what the feeling means. The other decides they are not being heard. Then the conversation becomes less about understanding and more about protection.\n\nSlow down. Put comfort before analysis. Say what landed. Ask what was meant. This connection improves when both people stop treating emotional clarity as something that can be forced.","tension":"The deeper challenge is the temptation to become certain too quickly. One person decides they already know what the feeling means. The other decides they are not being heard. Then the conversation becomes less about understanding and more about protection.","advice":"Slow down. Put comfort before analysis. Say what landed. Ask what was meant. This connection improves when both people stop treating emotional clarity as something that can be forced.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mercury_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mercury_trine', 'synastry-moon-trine-mercury', 'relationship-moon-trine-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mercury_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mercury_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Trine Mercury', null, 'This person may make it easier to talk about what you feel.

There is often a natural trust in the way conversation moves between you. You may feel less afraid of being misunderstood. Less worried that your emotions will be dismissed, judged, or turned into a debate. The words come more easily because the listening feels safer.

When this works, it can be deeply steadying. This person may help you name what is happening inside without making it heavier. They may ask the right question, offer the right reflection, or simply give you enough room to hear yourself. You can talk through emotional things without feeling like you are being managed.

This kind of connection can become a place of repair. Not because every conversation is perfect, but because both people seem willing to understand. Feelings do not have to become chaos. Words do not have to become weapons. There is enough care in the exchange to keep both people connected.

The challenge is that ease can make you lazy with honesty. You may assume they already know what you feel. They may assume you will say it if it matters. But even natural understanding needs real information.

Keep telling the truth in real time. Let the conversation stay alive. The gift here is not just that this person understands you. It is that the two of you can keep learning how to understand each other more deeply.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may make it easier to talk about what you feel.\n\nThere is often a natural trust in the way conversation moves between you. You may feel less afraid of being misunderstood. Less worried that your emotions will be dismissed, judged, or turned into a debate. The words come more easily because the listening feels safer.\n\nWhen this works, it can be deeply steadying. This person may help you name what is happening inside without making it heavier. They may ask the right question, offer the right reflection, or simply give you enough room to hear yourself. You can talk through emotional things without feeling like you are being managed.\n\nThis kind of connection can become a place of repair. Not because every conversation is perfect, but because both people seem willing to understand. Feelings do not have to become chaos. Words do not have to become weapons. There is enough care in the exchange to keep both people connected.\n\nThe challenge is that ease can make you lazy with honesty. You may assume they already know what you feel. They may assume you will say it if it matters. But even natural understanding needs real information.\n\nKeep telling the truth in real time. Let the conversation stay alive. The gift here is not just that this person understands you. It is that the two of you can keep learning how to understand each other more deeply."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that ease can make you lazy with honesty. You may assume they already know what you feel. They may assume you will say it if it matters. But even natural understanding needs real information."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Keep telling the truth in real time. Let the conversation stay alive. The gift here 