  ('A-moon_B-uranus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"uranus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-uranus_trine', 'synastry-moon-trine-uranus', 'relationship-moon-trine-uranus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-uranus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-uranus_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Trine Uranus', null, 'A''s feelings meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Translation","body":"A''s feelings meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-uranus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":null,"tension":null,"advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":null,"weight":null}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-venus_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"venus","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-venus_conjunction', 'synastry-moon-conjunction-venus', 'relationship-moon-conjunction-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-venus_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-venus_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Conjunction Venus', null, 'This person may make you feel cared for in a way that is easy to receive. There is a natural softness here, the kind where affection does not have to be earned or pulled out of anyone. You may find yourself relaxing around each other quickly. Being close can feel comfortable instead of complicated, like you do not have to work so hard to feel liked.

At its best, this is one of the sweetest connections to have with someone. The warmth tends to land exactly where it is meant to. You may feel genuinely appreciated, not just wanted or needed. There is often real fondness here, the kind that makes ordinary moments feel special. Sharing a meal, checking in after a long day, sitting together doing nothing in particular can all feel surprisingly nourishing.

The harder part is that comfort can sometimes become the goal instead of closeness. You may avoid difficult conversations, smooth things over too quickly, or tell yourselves that everything is fine because neither of you wants to disrupt the good feeling. But relationships need more than sweetness to grow. They need room for honesty too.

Enjoy how easy this feels. Let yourself take in the affection. Just remember that real intimacy is not only about keeping things pleasant. It is also about trusting the connection enough to tell the truth when something matters.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may make you feel cared for in a way that is easy to receive. There is a natural softness here, the kind where affection does not have to be earned or pulled out of anyone. You may find yourself relaxing around each other quickly. Being close can feel comfortable instead of complicated, like you do not have to work so hard to feel liked.\n\nAt its best, this is one of the sweetest connections to have with someone. The warmth tends to land exactly where it is meant to. You may feel genuinely appreciated, not just wanted or needed. There is often real fondness here, the kind that makes ordinary moments feel special. Sharing a meal, checking in after a long day, sitting together doing nothing in particular can all feel surprisingly nourishing.\n\nThe harder part is that comfort can sometimes become the goal instead of closeness. You may avoid difficult conversations, smooth things over too quickly, or tell yourselves that everything is fine because neither of you wants to disrupt the good feeling. But relationships need more than sweetness to grow. They need room for honesty too.\n\nEnjoy how easy this feels. Let yourself take in the affection. Just remember that real intimacy is not only about keeping things pleasant. It is also about trusting the connection enough to tell the truth when something matters."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part is that comfort can sometimes become the goal instead of closeness. You may avoid difficult conversations, smooth things over too quickly, or tell yourselves that everything is fine because neither of you wants to disrupt the good feeling. But relationships need more than sweetness to grow. They need room for honesty too."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Enjoy how easy this feels. Let yourself take in the affection. Just remember that real intimacy is not only about keeping things pleasant. It is also about trusting the connection enough to tell the truth when something matters."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-venus_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Tenderness and care fold together. The Moon person feels nurtured by the Venus person''s affection; the Venus person feels emotionally safe. Warm, comforting, genuinely sweet. Failure mode: so cozy it avoids all friction and stays surface-soft. Enjoy the warmth; make room for honesty too.","summaryDeep":"This person may make you feel cared for in a way that is easy to receive. There is a natural softness here, the kind where affection does not have to be earned or pulled out of anyone. You may find yourself relaxing around each other quickly. Being close can feel comfortable instead of complicated, like you do not have to work so hard to feel liked.\n\nAt its best, this is one of the sweetest connections to have with someone. The warmth tends to land exactly where it is meant to. You may feel genuinely appreciated, not just wanted or needed. There is often real fondness here, the kind that makes ordinary moments feel special. Sharing a meal, checking in after a long day, sitting together doing nothing in particular can all feel surprisingly nourishing.\n\nThe harder part is that comfort can sometimes become the goal instead of closeness. You may avoid difficult conversations, smooth things over too quickly, or tell yourselves that everything is fine because neither of you wants to disrupt the good feeling. But relationships need more than sweetness to grow. They need room for honesty too.\n\nEnjoy how easy this feels. Let yourself take in the affection. Just remember that real intimacy is not only about keeping things pleasant. It is also about trusting the connection enough to tell the truth when something matters.","tension":"The harder part is that comfort can sometimes become the goal instead of closeness. You may avoid difficult conversations, smooth things over too quickly, or tell yourselves that everything is fine because neither of you wants to disrupt the good feeling. But relationships need more than sweetness to grow. They need room for honesty too.","advice":"Enjoy how easy this feels. Let yourself take in the affection. Just remember that real intimacy is not only about keeping things pleasant. It is also about trusting the connection enough to tell the truth when something matters.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-venus_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"venus","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-venus_opposition', 'synastry-moon-opposition-venus', 'relationship-moon-opposition-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-venus_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-venus_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Opposition Venus', null, 'There is real warmth here, but one of the biggest lessons in this connection is learning that care does not always look the way you expect it to. You may both want closeness, affection, and emotional connection, yet still find yourselves missing each other from time to time. Not because the love is not there, but because you naturally express it differently.

At its best, this relationship helps you expand your understanding of what it means to give and receive love. This person may show care in ways that are unfamiliar to you, and that can be a gift. It invites you to step outside your usual expectations and notice forms of affection you might otherwise overlook. Growth often happens when we realize there is more than one right way to love someone.

The challenge comes when expectations go unspoken. You may give what feels meaningful to you and feel disappointed when it is not fully appreciated. They may do the same. If you are not careful, you can start telling yourself stories about what the other person''s response means, when in reality both of you may be making sincere efforts.

The opportunity here is communication. Instead of assuming your partner should know what makes you feel loved, teach them. Be curious about what helps them feel cared for too. When both people are willing to learn each other''s language, the connection becomes stronger, warmer, and much easier to trust.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is real warmth here, but one of the biggest lessons in this connection is learning that care does not always look the way you expect it to. You may both want closeness, affection, and emotional connection, yet still find yourselves missing each other from time to time. Not because the love is not there, but because you naturally express it differently.\n\nAt its best, this relationship helps you expand your understanding of what it means to give and receive love. This person may show care in ways that are unfamiliar to you, and that can be a gift. It invites you to step outside your usual expectations and notice forms of affection you might otherwise overlook. Growth often happens when we realize there is more than one right way to love someone.\n\nThe challenge comes when expectations go unspoken. You may give what feels meaningful to you and feel disappointed when it is not fully appreciated. They may do the same. If you are not careful, you can start telling yourself stories about what the other person''s response means, when in reality both of you may be making sincere efforts.\n\nThe opportunity here is communication. Instead of assuming your partner should know what makes you feel loved, teach them. Be curious about what helps them feel cared for too. When both people are willing to learn each other''s language, the connection becomes stronger, warmer, and much easier to trust."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge comes when expectations go unspoken. You may give what feels meaningful to you and feel disappointed when it is not fully appreciated. They may do the same. If you are not careful, you can start telling yourself stories about what the other person''s response means, when in reality both of you may be making sincere efforts."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The opportunity here is communication. Instead of assuming your partner should know what makes you feel loved, teach them. Be curious about what helps them feel cared for too. When both people are willing to learn each other''s language, the connection becomes stronger, warmer, and much easier to trust."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-venus_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Warmth and need pulling in different directions. One wants closeness where the other offers a different flavor of care. Failure mode: mismatched bids for affection. Name what comforts you each; the difference can complement once it''s spoken.","summaryDeep":"There is real warmth here, but one of the biggest lessons in this connection is learning that care does not always look the way you expect it to. You may both want closeness, affection, and emotional connection, yet still find yourselves missing each other from time to time. Not because the love is not there, but because you naturally express it differently.\n\nAt its best, this relationship helps you expand your understanding of what it means to give and receive love. This person may show care in ways that are unfamiliar to you, and that can be a gift. It invites you to step outside your usual expectations and notice forms of affection you might otherwise overlook. Growth often happens when we realize there is more than one right way to love someone.\n\nThe challenge comes when expectations go unspoken. You may give what feels meaningful to you and feel disappointed when it is not fully appreciated. They may do the same. If you are not careful, you can start telling yourself stories about what the other person''s response means, when in reality both of you may be making sincere efforts.\n\nThe opportunity here is communication. Instead of assuming your partner should know what makes you feel loved, teach them. Be curious about what helps them feel cared for too. When both people are willing to learn each other''s language, the connection becomes stronger, warmer, and much easier to trust.","tension":"The challenge comes when expectations go unspoken. You may give what feels meaningful to you and feel disappointed when it is not fully appreciated. They may do the same. If you are not careful, you can start telling yourself stories about what the other person''s response means, when in reality both of you may be making sincere efforts.","advice":"The opportunity here is communication. Instead of assuming your partner should know what makes you feel loved, teach them. Be curious about what helps them feel cared for too. When both people are willing to learn each other''s language, the connection becomes stronger, warmer, and much easier to trust.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"venus","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry-moon-sextile-venus', 'relationship-moon-sextile-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-venus_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-venus_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Sextile Venus', null, 'This connection has a natural warmth to it, but it works best when you put that warmth into action. You may care about each other more than you realize, and the relationship tends to grow through simple, consistent acts of affection. A thoughtful text, remembering something important, checking in when it matters, making the other person feel seen. These small moments carry a lot of weight.

At its best, this is a relationship where kindness builds momentum. When one person makes an effort, the other usually responds. The more intentional you are about showing care, the easier it becomes to create trust, comfort, and closeness. You do not need grand gestures. You need consistency.

The challenge is that both of you may assume the relationship is doing fine because the feelings are there. You care about each other, you enjoy each other, and there may not be much conflict. But that can make it easy to stop reaching for each other. The check-ins happen less often. The compliments stay in your head. The thoughtful gesture never quite happens because you figure they already know how you feel.

Over time, it can be easy to assume the warmth will take care of itself. The connection may still be there, but if neither person is actively showing up for it, something valuable can start to fade into the background. Not because the feelings are gone, but because they are no longer being expressed.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection has a natural warmth to it, but it works best when you put that warmth into action. You may care about each other more than you realize, and the relationship tends to grow through simple, consistent acts of affection. A thoughtful text, remembering something important, checking in when it matters, making the other person feel seen. These small moments carry a lot of weight.\n\nAt its best, this is a relationship where kindness builds momentum. When one person makes an effort, the other usually responds. The more intentional you are about showing care, the easier it becomes to create trust, comfort, and closeness. You do not need grand gestures. You need consistency.\n\nThe challenge is that both of you may assume the relationship is doing fine because the feelings are there. You care about each other, you enjoy each other, and there may not be much conflict. But that can make it easy to stop reaching for each other. The check-ins happen less often. The compliments stay in your head. The thoughtful gesture never quite happens because you figure they already know how you feel.\n\nOver time, it can be easy to assume the warmth will take care of itself. The connection may still be there, but if neither person is actively showing up for it, something valuable can start to fade into the background. Not because the feelings are gone, but because they are no longer being expressed."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that both of you may assume the relationship is doing fine because the feelings are there. You care about each other, you enjoy each other, and there may not be much conflict. But that can make it easy to stop reaching for each other. The check-ins happen less often. The compliments stay in your head. The thoughtful gesture never quite happens because you figure they already know how you feel."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Over time, it can be easy to assume the warmth will take care of itself. The connection may still be there, but if neither person is actively showing up for it, something valuable can start to fade into the background. Not because the feelings are gone, but because they are no longer being expressed."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-venus_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Easy emotional warmth with a gentle spark. Affection and care mesh without strain. Failure mode: under-investing in something quietly lovely. Lean into it.","summaryDeep":"This connection has a natural warmth to it, but it works best when you put that warmth into action. You may care about each other more than you realize, and the relationship tends to grow through simple, consistent acts of affection. A thoughtful text, remembering something important, checking in when it matters, making the other person feel seen. These small moments carry a lot of weight.\n\nAt its best, this is a relationship where kindness builds momentum. When one person makes an effort, the other usually responds. The more intentional you are about showing care, the easier it becomes to create trust, comfort, and closeness. You do not need grand gestures. You need consistency.\n\nThe challenge is that both of you may assume the relationship is doing fine because the feelings are there. You care about each other, you enjoy each other, and there may not be much conflict. But that can make it easy to stop reaching for each other. The check-ins happen less often. The compliments stay in your head. The thoughtful gesture never quite happens because you figure they already know how you feel.\n\nOver time, it can be easy to assume the warmth will take care of itself. The connection may still be there, but if neither person is actively showing up for it, something valuable can start to fade into the background. Not because the feelings are gone, but because they are no longer being expressed.","tension":"The challenge is that both of you may assume the relationship is doing fine because the feelings are there. You care about each other, you enjoy each other, and there may not be much conflict. But that can make it easy to stop reaching for each other. The check-ins happen less often. The compliments stay in your head. The thoughtful gesture never quite happens because you figure they already know how you feel.","advice":"Over time, it can be easy to assume the warmth will take care of itself. The connection may still be there, but if neither person is actively showing up for it, something valuable can start to fade into the background. Not because the feelings are gone, but because they are no longer being expressed.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-venus_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"venus","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-venus_square', 'synastry-moon-square-venus', 'relationship-moon-square-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-venus_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-venus_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Square Venus', null, 'The care is there, but the delivery can be off. You may both want to make each other feel loved, yet keep missing the mark. One person gives what they would want to receive, while the other is left thinking, "That is not really what I needed."

The good news is that there is usually genuine affection underneath the frustration. You likely want the best for each other. The challenge is that good intentions do not automatically create emotional connection. If you keep assuming the other person should just know what works, you can end up feeling disappointed even when both of you are trying.

Over time, these small misses can start to tell a bigger story. You may begin to think your needs are not important, while they may feel like nothing they do is ever enough. That is when a simple misunderstanding turns into resentment.

Be direct. Tell this person what helps you feel cared for. Ask them what matters to them too. Stop grading each other on mind-reading. This connection gets stronger when you focus less on how love should look and more on whether it is actually reaching the other person.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"The care is there, but the delivery can be off. You may both want to make each other feel loved, yet keep missing the mark. One person gives what they would want to receive, while the other is left thinking, \"That is not really what I needed.\"\n\nThe good news is that there is usually genuine affection underneath the frustration. You likely want the best for each other. The challenge is that good intentions do not automatically create emotional connection. If you keep assuming the other person should just know what works, you can end up feeling disappointed even when both of you are trying.\n\nOver time, these small misses can start to tell a bigger story. You may begin to think your needs are not important, while they may feel like nothing they do is ever enough. That is when a simple misunderstanding turns into resentment.\n\nBe direct. Tell this person what helps you feel cared for. Ask them what matters to them too. Stop grading each other on mind-reading. This connection gets stronger when you focus less on how love should look and more on whether it is actually reaching the other person."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Over time, these small misses can start to tell a bigger story. You may begin to think your needs are not important, while they may feel like nothing they do is ever enough. That is when a simple misunderstanding turns into resentment."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Be direct. Tell this person what helps you feel cared for. Ask them what matters to them too. Stop grading each other on mind-reading. This connection gets stronger when you focus less on how love should look and more on whether it is actually reaching the other person."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-venus_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Affection and emotional need slightly at odds. What the Venus person offers isn''t quite what the Moon person needs to feel cared for. Failure mode: a recurring sense of being loved in the wrong language. Learn the other''s actual needs - workable and worth it.","summaryDeep":"The care is there, but the delivery can be off. You may both want to make each other feel loved, yet keep missing the mark. One person gives what they would want to receive, while the other is left thinking, \"That is not really what I needed.\"\n\nThe good news is that there is usually genuine affection underneath the frustration. You likely want the best for each other. The challenge is that good intentions do not automatically create emotional connection. If you keep assuming the other person should just know what works, you can end up feeling disappointed even when both of you are trying.\n\nOver time, these small misses can start to tell a bigger story. You may begin to think your needs are not important, while they may feel like nothing they do is ever enough. That is when a simple misunderstanding turns into resentment.\n\nBe direct. Tell this person what helps you feel cared for. Ask them what matters to them too. Stop grading each other on mind-reading. This connection gets stronger when you focus less on how love should look and more on whether it is actually reaching the other person.","tension":"Over time, these small misses can start to tell a bigger story. You may begin to think your needs are not important, while they may feel like nothing they do is ever enough. That is when a simple misunderstanding turns into resentment.","advice":"Be direct. Tell this person what helps you feel cared for. Ask them what matters to them too. Stop grading each other on mind-reading. This connection gets stronger when you focus less on how love should look and more on whether it is actually reaching the other person.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-venus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"venus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-venus_trine', 'synastry-moon-trine-venus', 'relationship-moon-trine-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-venus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-venus_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Trine Venus', null, 'This relationship can feel easy in the best way. You may find yourself relaxing around this person instead of wondering where you stand. Affection tends to flow naturally, and being kind to each other does not feel like work. There is often a sense of emotional safety here that makes it easier to let your guard down and be yourself.

At its best, this connection reminds you that love does not always have to be complicated. You may feel accepted, appreciated, and genuinely cared for. This person can bring out a softer side of you, not because they demand it, but because you feel comfortable enough to show it. There is less pressure to perform and more room to simply be.

The challenge is not conflict so much as taking each other for granted. When something feels this natural, it is easy to assume it will take care of itself. You may stop noticing the small things that make the relationship work because they have become so familiar.

Do not coast on good chemistry. Keep showing up. Keep making the effort to connect. The warmth between you is a gift, but it is not self-sustaining. The relationships that last are the ones where people keep choosing each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This relationship can feel easy in the best way. You may find yourself relaxing around this person instead of wondering where you stand. Affection tends to flow naturally, and being kind to each other does not feel like work. There is often a sense of emotional safety here that makes it easier to let your guard down and be yourself.\n\nAt its best, this connection reminds you that love does not always have to be complicated. You may feel accepted, appreciated, and genuinely cared for. This person can bring out a softer side of you, not because they demand it, but because you feel comfortable enough to show it. There is less pressure to perform and more room to simply be.\n\nThe challenge is not conflict so much as taking each other for granted. When something feels this natural, it is easy to assume it will take care of itself. You may stop noticing the small things that make the relationship work because they have become so familiar.\n\nDo not coast on good chemistry. Keep showing up. Keep making the effort to connect. The warmth between you is a gift, but it is not self-sustaining. The relationships that last are the ones where people keep choosing each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is not conflict so much as taking each other for granted. When something feels this natural, it is easy to assume it will take care of itself. You may stop noticing the small things that make the relationship work because they have become so familiar."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Do not coast on good chemistry. Keep showing up. Keep making the effort to connect. The warmth between you is a gift, but it is not self-sustaining. The relationships that last are the ones where people keep choosing each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-venus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Care and affection flow naturally. Emotional comfort, kindness, a soothing bond. Failure mode: comfort without challenge. A beautiful foundation; keep some edge alive.","summaryDeep":"This relationship can feel easy in the best way. You may find yourself relaxing around this person instead of wondering where you stand. Affection tends to flow naturally, and being kind to each other does not feel like work. There is often a sense of emotional safety here that makes it easier to let your guard down and be yourself.\n\nAt its best, this connection reminds you that love does not always have to be complicated. You may feel accepted, appreciated, and genuinely cared for. This person can bring out a softer side of you, not because they demand it, but because you feel comfortable enough to show it. There is less pressure to perform and more room to simply be.\n\nThe challenge is not conflict so much as taking each other for granted. When something feels this natural, it is easy to assume it will take care of itself. You may stop noticing the small things that make the relationship work because they have become so familiar.\n\nDo not coast on good chemistry. Keep showing up. Keep making the effort to connect. The warmth between you is a gift, but it is not self-sustaining. The relationships that last are the ones where people keep choosing each other.","tension":"The challenge is not conflict so much as taking each other for granted. When something feels this natural, it is easy to assume it will take care of itself. You may stop noticing the small things that make the relationship work because they have become so familiar.","advice":"Do not coast on good chemistry. Keep showing up. Keep making the effort to connect. The warmth between you is a gift, but it is not self-sustaining. The relationships that last are the ones where people keep choosing each other.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
