"tension":"The challenge is making sure encouragement is paired with accountability. Big dreams still require planning, consistency, and follow-through. It can be easy to focus on potential while overlooking the habits, skills, and effort needed to turn that potential into results.","advice":"Use their belief in you as fuel, not as a substitute for action. The most successful expression of this connection happens when optimism is matched with commitment and inspiration is translated into meaningful progress.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-jupiter_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-jupiter_opposition', 'synastry-sun-opposition-jupiter', 'relationship-sun-opposition-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-jupiter_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-jupiter_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Opposition Jupiter', null, 'This person may challenge you to think bigger about what is possible for your life, career, or future.

They often see opportunities where you see obstacles. They may encourage you to aim higher, take a calculated risk, or pursue goals that feel just beyond your current comfort zone. Their confidence in your potential can be motivating, but it can also feel intimidating if you''re focused on the practical realities of getting there.

When this dynamic is working well, you help each other grow. They push you to expand your vision and stop limiting yourself based on old assumptions. You help them turn big ideas into actionable plans. One person brings ambition and possibility; the other brings strategy and perspective. Together, you can balance inspiration with execution.

The opportunity here is learning that growth requires both vision and realism. Their optimism can help you see opportunities you might otherwise overlook. Your careful thinking can help ensure those opportunities are sustainable and achievable.

The challenge comes when encouragement starts to feel like pressure or when caution is mistaken for resistance. They may wonder why you''re not moving faster. You may wonder whether they''ve fully considered the risks. Conversations about goals, timing, or next steps can become debates about what is actually realistic.

The key is to use their belief in your potential as fuel, not as a substitute for your own decision-making. Let them expand your perspective while staying connected to your values, priorities, and plan. The strongest version of this connection combines bold vision with thoughtful execution.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may challenge you to think bigger about what is possible for your life, career, or future.\n\nThey often see opportunities where you see obstacles. They may encourage you to aim higher, take a calculated risk, or pursue goals that feel just beyond your current comfort zone. Their confidence in your potential can be motivating, but it can also feel intimidating if you''re focused on the practical realities of getting there.\n\nWhen this dynamic is working well, you help each other grow. They push you to expand your vision and stop limiting yourself based on old assumptions. You help them turn big ideas into actionable plans. One person brings ambition and possibility; the other brings strategy and perspective. Together, you can balance inspiration with execution.\n\nThe opportunity here is learning that growth requires both vision and realism. Their optimism can help you see opportunities you might otherwise overlook. Your careful thinking can help ensure those opportunities are sustainable and achievable.\n\nThe challenge comes when encouragement starts to feel like pressure or when caution is mistaken for resistance. They may wonder why you''re not moving faster. You may wonder whether they''ve fully considered the risks. Conversations about goals, timing, or next steps can become debates about what is actually realistic.\n\nThe key is to use their belief in your potential as fuel, not as a substitute for your own decision-making. Let them expand your perspective while staying connected to your values, priorities, and plan. The strongest version of this connection combines bold vision with thoughtful execution."},{"he