  ('A-sun_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry-sun-conjunction-mercury', 'relationship-sun-conjunction-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-mercury_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-mercury_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Conjunction Mercury', null, 'This person may seem to understand you right away. Conversation often feels easy, as if they naturally follow your train of thought and quickly pick up on what matters to you.

When this works well, it can feel deeply affirming. They may notice parts of you that often go unseen and reflect them back in a way that resonates. You might feel that they are paying close attention, not just to what you say, but to the energy, intentions, and essence behind it. Their observations can help you feel witnessed in a meaningful way, as though they are looking past the obvious and connecting with something more fundamental about who you are.

Being understood by them can feel like exhaling. You may feel less guarded, less alone in your experience, and more able to be yourself without explanation. At times, they may find the words for something you have always felt but never fully named.

Remember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.

Keep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may seem to understand you right away. Conversation often feels easy, as if they naturally follow your train of thought and quickly pick up on what matters to you.\n\nWhen this works well, it can feel deeply affirming. They may notice parts of you that often go unseen and reflect them back in a way that resonates. You might feel that they are paying close attention, not just to what you say, but to the energy, intentions, and essence behind it. Their observations can help you feel witnessed in a meaningful way, as though they are looking past the obvious and connecting with something more fundamental about who you are.\n\nBeing understood by them can feel like exhaling. You may feel less guarded, less alone in your experience, and more able to be yourself without explanation. At times, they may find the words for something you have always felt but never fully named.\n\nRemember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.\n\nKeep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Remember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Keep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-mercury_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s mind. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person may seem to understand you right away. Conversation often feels easy, as if they naturally follow your train of thought and quickly pick up on what matters to you.\n\nWhen this works well, it can feel deeply affirming. They may notice parts of you that often go unseen and reflect them back in a way that resonates. You might feel that they are paying close attention, not just to what you say, but to the energy, intentions, and essence behind it. Their observations can help you feel witnessed in a meaningful way, as though they are looking past the obvious and connecting with something more fundamental about who you are.\n\nBeing understood by them can feel like exhaling. You may feel less guarded, less alone in your experience, and more able to be yourself without explanation. At times, they may find the words for something you have always felt but never fully named.\n\nRemember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.\n\nKeep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other.","tension":"Remember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.","advice":"Keep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry-sun-opposition-mercury', 'relationship-sun-opposition-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-mercury_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-mercury_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Opposition Mercury', null, 'This person may reflect back a version of you that you do not immediately recognize.

They can notice qualities, patterns, and motivations that sit just outside your usual field of vision. Sometimes their observations feel illuminating, like they have found language for something you have always sensed but never fully understood. Other times, their perspective can feel unsettling, exposing a truth you were not ready to face or describing you in a way that misses the heart of who you are.

This connection often asks you to meet yourself through contrast. Their way of thinking may challenge your self-image, not because they are trying to change you, but because they naturally stand across from your point of view. What they see and what you know about yourself may not always match.

At its best, this dynamic expands your awareness. It invites you to consider that there may be more than one truth in the room. Their insight can help you understand how you impact others, while your perspective can remind them that no one is fully defined by an outside interpretation.

At its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal.

Stay open. You do not have to agree with everything they see, but you can stay curious. Keep your own perspective while making room for theirs.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may reflect back a version of you that you do not immediately recognize.\n\nThey can notice qualities, patterns, and motivations that sit just outside your usual field of vision. Sometimes their observations feel illuminating, like they have found language for something you have always sensed but never fully understood. Other times, their perspective can feel unsettling, exposing a truth you were not ready to face or describing you in a way that misses the heart of who you are.\n\nThis connection often asks you to meet yourself through contrast. Their way of thinking may challenge your self-image, not because they are trying to change you, but because they naturally stand across from your point of view. What they see and what you know about yourself may not always match.\n\nAt its best, this dynamic expands your awareness. It invites you to consider that there may be more than one truth in the room. Their insight can help you understand how you impact others, while your perspective can remind them that no one is fully defined by an outside interpretation.\n\nAt its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal.\n\nStay open. You do not have to agree with everything they see, but you can stay curious. Keep your own perspective while making room for theirs."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Stay open. You do not have to agree with everything they see, but you can stay curious. Keep your own perspective while making room for theirs."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-mercury_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s mind. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person may reflect back a version of you that you do not immediately recognize.\n\nThey can notice qualities, patterns, and motivations that sit just outside your usual field of vision. Sometimes their observations feel illuminating, like they have found language for something you have always sensed but never fully understood. Other times, their perspective can feel unsettling, exposing a truth you were not ready to face or describing you in a way that misses the heart of who you are.\n\nThis connection often asks you to meet yourself through contrast. Their way of thinking may challenge your self-image, not because they are trying to change you, but because they naturally stand across from your point of view. What they see and what you know about yourself may not always match.\n\nAt its best, this dynamic expands your awareness. It invites you to consider that there may be more than one truth in the room. Their insight can help you understand how you impact others, while your perspective can remind them that no one is fully defined by an outside interpretation.\n\nAt its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal.\n\nStay open. You do not have to agree with everything they see, but you can stay curious. Keep your own perspective while making room for theirs.","tension":"At its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal.","advice":"Stay open. You do not have to agree with everything they see, but you can stay curious. Keep your own perspective while making room for theirs.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry-sun-sextile-mercury', 'relationship-sun-sextile-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-mercury_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-mercury_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Sextile Mercury', null, 'This person may help you feel understood in a way that stays with you. They have a way of asking the question that gets to the heart of something, or noticing the detail that everyone else missed. Conversations with them can leave you feeling clearer about yourself. Not because they tell you who you are, but because they create space for you to hear your own thoughts more honestly.

There is often a quiet sense of safety here. You may find yourself sharing things you did not plan to say, simply because it feels natural to keep opening up. Their curiosity can feel genuine, and that makes it easier to let them see more of the real you.

The connection often grows through small moments that matter more than they seem. They remember something important to you. They ask about it later. They listen closely enough that you can feel the difference. Those moments can create a powerful feeling of being seen, valued, and understood.

At its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is.

The more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may help you feel understood in a way that stays with you. They have a way of asking the question that gets to the heart of something, or noticing the detail that everyone else missed. Conversations with them can leave you feeling clearer about yourself. Not because they tell you who you are, but because they create space for you to hear your own thoughts more honestly.\n\nThere is often a quiet sense of safety here. You may find yourself sharing things you did not plan to say, simply because it feels natural to keep opening up. Their curiosity can feel genuine, and that makes it easier to let them see more of the real you.\n\nThe connection often grows through small moments that matter more than they seem. They remember something important to you. They ask about it later. They listen closely enough that you can feel the difference. Those moments can create a powerful feeling of being seen, valued, and understood.\n\nAt its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is.\n\nThe more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-mercury_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s mind. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This person may help you feel understood in a way that stays with you. They have a way of asking the question that gets to the heart of something, or noticing the detail that everyone else missed. Conversations with them can leave you feeling clearer about yourself. Not because they tell you who you are, but because they create space for you to hear your own thoughts more honestly.\n\nThere is often a quiet sense of safety here. You may find yourself sharing things you did not plan to say, simply because it feels natural to keep opening up. Their curiosity can feel genuine, and that makes it easier to let them see more of the real you.\n\nThe connection often grows through small moments that matter more than they seem. They remember something important to you. They ask about it later. They listen closely enough that you can feel the difference. Those moments can create a powerful feeling of being seen, valued, and understood.\n\nAt its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is.\n\nThe more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more.","tension":"At its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is.","advice":"The more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-mercury_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-mercury_square', 'synastry-sun-square-mercury', 'relationship-sun-square-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-mercury_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-mercury_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Square Mercury', null, 'This person may misunderstand you in a way that gets under your skin. The tension isn''t necessarily about what is being said. It''s about the gap between what is meant and what is received. This person may reflect something back to you that feels slightly off. They may think they understand your intentions while missing an important piece of your experience. You may find yourself repeating, clarifying, or trying to find new language for something that feels obvious from your side.

That can be exhausting. It can also be revealing.

Squares ask us to work. They shine a light on patterns that may be holding you back from deeper connection. In this relationship, misunderstandings can become opportunities for growth. You may be encouraged to communicate more clearly and express what you truly mean, rather than assuming the other person already knows. They may be encouraged to slow down, stay curious, and listen with an open mind before jumping to conclusions.

When the tension builds, conversations can turn into arguments about who understands the situation better. One person feels unseen. The other feels like their efforts are being dismissed. Instead of getting curious, both people may become defensive.

The growth here comes from slowing down. Not by accepting being misunderstood, but by staying in the conversation long enough to understand each other more clearly. This connection isn''t really about proving who''s right. It''s about both of you getting better at seeing each other for who you actually are, instead of getting stuck in your own assumptions about each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may misunderstand you in a way that gets under your skin. The tension isn''t necessarily about what is being said. It''s about the gap between what is meant and what is received. This person may reflect something back to you that feels slightly off. They may think they understand your intentions while missing an important piece of your experience. You may find yourself repeating, clarifying, or trying to find new language for something that feels obvious from your side.\n\nThat can be exhausting. It can also be revealing.\n\nSquares ask us to work. They shine a light on patterns that may be holding you back from deeper connection. In this relationship, misunderstandings can become opportunities for growth. You may be encouraged to communicate more clearly and express what you truly mean, rather than assuming the other person already knows. They may be encouraged to slow down, stay curious, and listen with an open mind before jumping to conclusions.\n\nWhen the tension builds, conversations can turn into arguments about who understands the situation better. One person feels unseen. The other feels like their efforts are being dismissed. Instead of getting curious, both people may become defensive.\n\nThe growth here comes from slowing down. Not by accepting being misunderstood, but by staying in the conversation long enough to understand each other more clearly. This connection isn''t really about proving who''s right. It''s about both of you getting better at seeing each other for who you actually are, instead of getting stuck in your own assumptions about each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"When the tension builds, conversations can turn into arguments about who understands the situation better. One person feels unseen. The other feels like their efforts are being dismissed. Instead of getting curious, both people may become defensive."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The growth here comes from slowing down. Not by accepting being misunderstood, but by staying in the conversation long enough to understand each other more clearly. This connection isn''t really about proving who''s right. It''s about both of you getting better at seeing each other for who you actually are, instead of getting stuck in your own assumptions about each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-mercury_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s mind. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This person may misunderstand you in a way that gets under your skin. The tension isn''t necessarily about what is being said. It''s about the gap between what is meant and what is received. This person may reflect something back to you that feels slightly off. They may think they understand your intentions while missing an important piece of your experience. You may find yourself repeating, clarifying, or trying to find new language for something that feels obvious from your side.\n\nThat can be exhausting. It can also be revealing.\n\nSquares ask us to work. They shine a light on patterns that may be holding you back from deeper connection. In this relationship, misunderstandings can become opportunities for growth. You may be encouraged to communicate more clearly and express what you truly mean, rather than assuming the other person already knows. They may be encouraged to slow down, stay curious, and listen with an open mind before jumping to conclusions.\n\nWhen the tension builds, conversations can turn into arguments about who understands the situation better. One person feels unseen. The other feels like their efforts are being dismissed. Instead of getting curious, both people may become defensive.\n\nThe growth here comes from slowing down. Not by accepting being misunderstood, but by staying in the conversation long enough to understand each other more clearly. This connection isn''t really about proving who''s right. It''s about both of you getting better at seeing each other for who you actually are, instead of getting stuck in your own assumptions about each other.","tension":"When the tension builds, conversations can turn into arguments about who understands the situation better. One person feels unseen. The other feels like their efforts are being dismissed. Instead of getting curious, both people may become defensive.","advice":"The growth here comes from slowing down. Not by accepting being misunderstood, but by staying in the conversation long enough to understand each other more clearly. This connection isn''t really about proving who''s right. It''s about both of you getting better at seeing each other for who you actually are, instead of getting stuck in your own assumptions about each other.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-mercury_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-mercury_trine', 'synastry-sun-trine-mercury', 'relationship-sun-trine-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-mercury_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-mercury_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Trine Mercury', null, 'There is often an ease between the way you express who you are and the way this person listens, understands, and responds. You may feel less guarded around them. Less concerned with finding the perfect words. More able to trust that what you mean will actually land.

Their attention can feel affirming. Not because they agree with everything you say, but because they seem genuinely interested in understanding you. They may remember the details that matter, reflect your thoughts back with care, or help you articulate something that was still taking shape inside of you.

When this connection is flowing, conversation becomes a place of recognition. You may feel witnessed in ways that help you settle more fully into yourself. There can be a quiet confidence that grows from being understood without having to constantly explain or defend who you are.

Still, every gift asks something of us. The ease here can make it tempting to assume that understanding will always be available. You may stop sharing the parts of yourself that are changing. They may rely on what they already know instead of staying curious about who you are becoming.

This connection works best when both people stay engaged. Do not assume you already know each other. Keep sharing what is changing in your life. The understanding between you is a strength, and it keeps growing when you both stay informed.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is often an ease between the way you express who you are and the way this person listens, understands, and responds. You may feel less guarded around them. Less concerned with finding the perfect words. More able to trust that what you mean will actually land.\n\nTheir attention can feel affirming. Not because they agree with everything you say, but because they seem genuinely interested in understanding you. They may remember the details that matter, reflect your thoughts back with care, or help you articulate something that was still taking shape inside of you.\n\nWhen this connection is flowing, conversation becomes a place of recognition. You may feel witnessed in ways that help you settle more fully into yourself. There can be a quiet confidence that grows from being understood without having to constantly explain or defend who you are.\n\nStill, every gift asks something of us. The ease here can make it tempting to assume that understanding will always be available. You may stop sharing the parts of yourself that are changing. They may rely on what they already know instead of staying curious about who you are becoming.\n\nThis connection works best when both people stay engaged. Do not assume you already know each other. Keep sharing what is changing in your life. The understanding between you is a strength, and it keeps growing when you both stay informed."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Still, every gift asks something of us. The ease here can make it tempting to assume that understanding will always be available. You may stop sharing the parts of yourself that are changing. They may rely on what they already know instead of staying curious about who you are becoming."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This connection works best when both people stay engaged. Do not assume you already know each other. Keep sharing what is changing in your life. The understanding between you is a strength, and it keeps growing when you both stay informed."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-mercury_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s mind. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"There is often an ease between the way you express who you are and the way this person listens, understands, and responds. You may feel less guarded around them. Less concerned with finding the perfect words. More able to trust that what you mean will actually land.\n\nTheir attention can feel affirming. Not because they agree with everything you say, but because they seem genuinely interested in understanding you. They may remember the details that matter, reflect your thoughts back with care, or help you articulate something that was still taking shape inside of you.\n\nWhen this connection is flowing, conversation becomes a place of recognition. You may feel witnessed in ways that help you settle more fully into yourself. There can be a quiet confidence that grows from being understood without having to constantly explain or defend who you are.\n\nStill, every gift asks something of us. The ease here can make it tempting to assume that understanding will always be available. You may stop sharing the parts of yourself that are changing. They may rely on what they already know instead of staying curious about who you are becoming.\n\nThis connection works best when both people stay engaged. Do not assume you already know each other. Keep sharing what is changing in your life. The understanding between you is a strength, and it keeps growing when you both stay informed.","tension":"Still, every gift asks something of us. The ease here can make it tempting to assume that understanding will always be available. You may stop sharing the parts of yourself that are changing. They may rely on what they already know instead of staying curious about who you are becoming.","advice":"This connection works best when both people stay engaged. Do not assume you already know each other. Keep sharing what is changing in your life. The understanding between you is a strength, and it keeps growing when you both stay informed.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"moon","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry-sun-conjunction-moon', 'relationship-sun-conjunction-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-moon_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-moon_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Conjunction Moon', 'This can feel familiar right away. One person''s personality fits easily with the other person''s emotional needs, so being around each other may feel natural without either of you doing much.', 'This can feel familiar right away. One person''s personality fits easily with the other person''s emotional needs, so being around each other may feel natural without either of you doing much.

There''s a real comfort here. One person may feel seen, and the other may feel needed in a way that actually feels good. It''s not always dramatic or flashy. It''s more like, "Oh, I can relax around you."

The problem is that comfort can turn into dependence. One person may start expecting the other to always be their soft place to land, and the relationship can get a little too comfortable without anyone noticing.

Enjoy the closeness, but don''t disappear into it. This works best when both people still have their own life.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This can feel familiar right away. One person''s personality fits easily with the other person''s emotional needs, so being around each other may feel natural without either of you doing much.\n\nThere''s a real comfort here. One person may feel seen, and the other may feel needed in a way that actually feels good. It''s not always dramatic or flashy. It''s more like, \"Oh, I can relax around you.\"\n\nThe problem is that comfort can turn into dependence. One person may start expecting the other to always be their soft place to land, and the relationship can get a little too comfortable without anyone noticing.\n\nEnjoy the closeness, but don''t disappear into it. This works best when both people still have their own life."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is that comfort can turn into dependence. One person may start expecting the other to always be their soft place to land, and the relationship can get a little too comfortable without anyone noticing."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Enjoy the closeness, but don''t disappear into it. This works best when both people still have their own life."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-moon_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Wants and needs run as one instinct. The Sun person''s drive and the Moon person''s feelings fold together - you get each other at a level that''s hard to explain. Strong foundational glue. Failure mode: coasting on the ease and never building anything with it. Use the natural understanding to make something; don''t treat it as the whole relationship.","summaryDeep":"This can feel familiar right away. One person''s personality fits easily with the other person''s emotional needs, so being around each other may feel natural without either of you doing much.\n\nThere''s a real comfort here. One person may feel seen, and the other may feel needed in a way that actually feels good. It''s not always dramatic or flashy. It''s more like, \"Oh, I can relax around you.\"\n\nThe problem is that comfort can turn into dependence. One person may start expecting the other to always be their soft place to land, and the relationship can get a little too comfortable without anyone noticing.\n\nEnjoy the closeness, but don''t disappear into it. This works best when both people still have their own life.","tension":"The problem is that comfort can turn into dependence. One person may start expecting the other to always be their soft place to land, and the relationship can get a little too comfortable without anyone noticing.","advice":"Enjoy the closeness, but don''t disappear into it. This works best when both people still have their own life.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"moon","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry-sun-opposition-moon', 'relationship-sun-opposition-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-moon_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-moon_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Opposition Moon', 'There''s a strong pull here, but you may not always feel like you''re coming from the same place. One person''s way of being can bring up a lot of feelings in the other person, sometimes in a good way, sometimes in a "why am I reacting like this?" way.', 'There''s a strong pull here, but you may not always feel like you''re coming from the same place. One person''s way of being can bring up a lot of feelings in the other person, sometimes in a good way, sometimes in a "why am I reacting like this?" way.

At its best, you balance each other out. One person brings direction, confidence, or clarity. The other brings care, sensitivity, and emotional reality. You may feel like this person has something you need, even when they also get on your nerves.

The problem is that it can turn into a standoff. One person feels unseen. The other feels like nothing they do is enough.

Don''t make it a competition over whose needs matter more. Say what you need, listen to what they need, and meet somewhere in the middle.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There''s a strong pull here, but you may not always feel like you''re coming from the same place. One person''s way of being can bring up a lot of feelings in the other person, sometimes in a good way, sometimes in a \"why am I reacting like this?\" way.\n\nAt its best, you balance each other out. One person brings direction, confidence, or clarity. The other brings care, sensitivity, and emotional reality. You may feel like this person has something you need, even when they also get on your nerves.\n\nThe problem is that it can turn into a standoff. One person feels unseen. The other feels like nothing they do is enough.\n\nDon''t make it a competition over whose needs matter more. Say what you need, listen to what they need, and meet somewhere in the middle."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is that it can turn into a standoff. One person feels unseen. The other feels like nothing they do is enough."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Don''t make it a competition over whose needs matter more. Say what you need, listen to what they need, and meet somewhere in the middle."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-moon_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Opposite by nature, drawn together for it. One leads with identity, the other with feeling, and you complete and irritate each other in equal measure. Failure mode: keeping score, or swinging between fusion and friction. Trade roles on purpose, value the contrast, and stop tallying who gave more.","summaryDeep":"There''s a strong pull here, but you may not always feel like you''re coming from the same place. One person''s way of being can bring up a lot of feelings in the other person, sometimes in a good way, sometimes in a \"why am I reacting like this?\" way.\n\nAt its best, you balance each other out. One person brings 