  ('A-sun_B-moon_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"moon","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-moon_sextile', 'synastry-sun-sextile-moon', 'relationship-sun-sextile-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-moon_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-moon_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Sextile Moon', 'There''s a good fit here, but it gets better when both people actually put something into it. One person''s way of being can support the other person''s emotional needs, especially when there''s effort, attention, and basic follow-through.', 'There''s a good fit here, but it gets better when both people actually put something into it. One person''s way of being can support the other person''s emotional needs, especially when there''s effort, attention, and basic follow-through.

This is the kind of connection where small things count. Checking in. Remembering what matters. Being a little more present than you technically have to be. The more you invest, the safer and warmer it feels.

The problem is leaving it half-open. The compatibility is there, but it may stay kind of mild if both people wait for the other one to make it more real.

Make the effort. Not a grand gesture, just enough to show the connection matters.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There''s a good fit here, but it gets better when both people actually put something into it. One person''s way of being can support the other person''s emotional needs, especially when there''s effort, attention, and basic follow-through.\n\nThis is the kind of connection where small things count. Checking in. Remembering what matters. Being a little more present than you technically have to be. The more you invest, the safer and warmer it feels.\n\nThe problem is leaving it half-open. The compatibility is there, but it may stay kind of mild if both people wait for the other one to make it more real.\n\nMake the effort. Not a grand gesture, just enough to show the connection matters."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is leaving it half-open. The compatibility is there, but it may stay kind of mild if both people wait for the other one to make it more real."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Make the effort. Not a grand gesture, just enough to show the connection matters."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-moon_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Identity and emotion fit comfortably, with room to grow the bond. You support each other''s nature without much effort, and there''s an opening to deepen. Failure mode: leaving it at nice and not investing. Take the opening - this is good raw material for a real partnership.","summaryDeep":"There''s a good fit here, but it gets better when both people actually put something into it. One person''s way of being can support the other person''s emotional needs, especially when there''s effort, attention, and basic follow-through.\n\nThis is the kind of connection where small things count. Checking in. Remembering what matters. Being a little more present than you technically have to be. The more you invest, the safer and warmer it feels.\n\nThe problem is leaving it half-open. The compatibility is there, but it may stay kind of mild if both people wait for the other one to make it more real.\n\nMake the effort. Not a grand gesture, just enough to show the connection matters.","tension":"The problem is leaving it half-open. The compatibility is there, but it may stay kind of mild if both people wait for the other one to make it more real.","advice":"Make the effort. Not a grand gesture, just enough to show the connection matters.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-moon_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"moon","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-moon_square', 'synastry-sun-square-moon', 'relationship-sun-square-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-moon_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-moon_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Square Moon', 'There''s a connection here, but it can rub the wrong way. One person''s natural style may clash with what the other person needs to feel safe, cared for, or understood.', 'There''s a connection here, but it can rub the wrong way. One person''s natural style may clash with what the other person needs to feel safe, cared for, or understood.

It can show up in ordinary little moments. One person wants to move on, the other wants to talk it through. One person needs space, the other needs reassurance. Nobody has to be doing anything terrible for it to still feel frustrating.

The problem is taking the mismatch personally. You can start thinking, "Why are they like this?" when really, the two of you may just have different settings.

Don''t let every small rub become a larger story about the relationship. Name the pattern, adjust, and stop expecting the other person to magically know what would make you feel better.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There''s a connection here, but it can rub the wrong way. One person''s natural style may clash with what the other person needs to feel safe, cared for, or understood.\n\nIt can show up in ordinary little moments. One person wants to move on, the other wants to talk it through. One person needs space, the other needs reassurance. Nobody has to be doing anything terrible for it to still feel frustrating.\n\nThe problem is taking the mismatch personally. You can start thinking, \"Why are they like this?\" when really, the two of you may just have different settings.\n\nDon''t let every small rub become a larger story about the relationship. Name the pattern, adjust, and stop expecting the other person to magically know what would make you feel better."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is taking the mismatch personally. You can start thinking, \"Why are they like this?\" when really, the two of you may just have different settings."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Don''t let every small rub become a larger story about the relationship. Name the pattern, adjust, and stop expecting the other person to magically know what would make you feel better."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-moon_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Core friction between identity and emotional need. What one wants to be grates on what the other needs to feel safe. Workable, not doom; many lasting couples carry it. Failure mode: reading the friction as proof you''re wrong for each other. Name the specific clash and keep negotiating - this aspect rewards patience.","summaryDeep":"There''s a connection here, but it can rub the wrong way. One person''s natural style may clash with what the other person needs to feel safe, cared for, or understood.\n\nIt 