  ('A-sun_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry-sun-trine-saturn', 'relationship-sun-trine-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-saturn_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-saturn_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Trine Saturn', null, 'Discipline that backs your direction without friction. Reliable, maturing, quietly strengthening. Failure mode: undramatic enough to overlook. Use the stability to build; it won''t announce itself.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Translation","body":"Discipline that backs your direction without friction. Reliable, maturing, quietly strengthening. Failure mode: undramatic enough to overlook. Use the stability to build; it won''t announce itself."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-saturn_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Discipline that backs your direction without friction. Reliable, maturing, quietly strengthening. Failure mode: undramatic enough to overlook. Use the stability to build; it won''t announce itself.","summaryDeep":null,"tension":null,"advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":null,"weight":null}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"sun","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry-sun-conjunction-sun', 'relationship-sun-conjunction-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-sun_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-sun_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Conjunction Sun', null, 'You may recognize something familiar in this person right away. Maybe it is how they carry themselves, what they care about, or the way they handle life. Being around them can feel easy because you do not have to explain every little thing.

When this works, there is a relief in not having to explain yourself all the time. This person may understand why certain things matter to you, why you make the choices you do, or why you care as much as you do. You can feel seen in a way that feels simple and natural, like they already speak the language you''re speaking.

The tricky part is that being alike can also bring out competition. You may both want to lead, both want to be seen, or both expect the other person to move out of the way. What felt familiar at first can start to feel crowded if nobody leaves room.

Let the similarity make you feel understood, not threatened.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You may recognize something familiar in this person right away. Maybe it is how they carry themselves, what they care about, or the way they handle life. Being around them can feel easy because you do not have to explain every little thing.\n\nWhen this works, there is a relief in not having to explain yourself all the time. This person may understand why certain things matter to you, why you make the choices you do, or why you care as much as you do. You can feel seen in a way that feels simple and natural, like they already speak the language you''re speaking.\n\nThe tricky part is that being alike can also bring out competition. You may both want to lead, both want to be seen, or both expect the other person to move out of the way. What felt familiar at first can start to feel crowded if nobody leaves room.\n\nLet the similarity make you feel understood, not threatened."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The tricky part is that being alike can also bring out competition. You may both want to lead, both want to be seen, or both expect the other person to move out of the way. What felt familiar at first can start to feel crowded if nobody leaves room."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the similarity make you feel understood, not threatened."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-sun_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s identity. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"You may recognize something familiar in this person right away. Maybe it is how they carry themselves, what they care about, or the way they handle life. Being around them can feel easy because you do not have to explain every little thing.\n\nWhen this works, there is a relief in not having to explain yourself all the time. This person may understand why certain things matter to you, why you make the choices you do, or why you care as much as you do. You can feel seen in a way that feels simple and natural, like they already speak the language you''re speaking.\n\nThe tricky part is that being alike can also bring out competition. You may both want to lead, both want to be seen, or both expect the other person to move out of the way. What felt familiar at first can start to feel crowded if nobody leaves room.\n\nLet the similarity make you feel understood, not threatened.","tension":"The tricky part is that being alike can also bring out competition. You may both want to lead, both want to be seen, or both expect the other person to move out of the way. What felt familiar at first can start to feel crowded if nobody leaves room.","advice":"Let the similarity make you feel understood, not threatened.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"sun","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry-sun-opposition-sun', 'relationship-sun-opposition-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-sun_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-sun_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Opposition Sun', null, 'This person may have a way of approaching life that feels noticeably different from yours. They may make choices you would not make, focus on things you tend to overlook, or respond to situations from a completely different starting point. Part of what draws you to them may be that difference. Part of what frustrates you may be the same thing.

When this works, the difference can be surprisingly helpful. This person may show you another way of handling things, one that would not have occurred to you on your own. They can make you question old assumptions, consider a different approach, or appreciate strengths you usually overlook. You may not always understand where they are coming from at first, but over time they can broaden your sense of what is possible.

The harder part is when the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling frustrating. You do things one way, they do things another, and before long both of you are explaining, defending, or pushing back. What began as contrast can turn into a pattern where each person feels misunderstood by the other.

You do not have to agree on everything to respect each other. The difference becomes much easier to live with when neither person is trying to prove their way is the right one.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may have a way of approaching life that feels noticeably different from yours. They may make choices you would not make, focus on things you tend to overlook, or respond to situations from a completely different starting point. Part of what draws you to them may be that difference. Part of what frustrates you may be the same thing.\n\nWhen this works, the difference can be surprisingly helpful. This person may show you another way of handling things, one that would not have occurred to you on your own. They can make you question old assumptions, consider a different approach, or appreciate strengths you usually overlook. You may not always understand where they are coming from at first, but over time they can broaden your sense of what is possible.\n\nThe harder part is when the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling frustrating. You do things one way, they do things another, and before long both of you are explaining, defending, or pushing back. What began as contrast can turn into a pattern where each person feels misunderstood by the other.\n\nYou do not have to agree on everything to respect each other. The difference becomes much easier to live with when neither person is trying to prove their way is the right one."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part is when the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling frustrating. You do things one way, they do things another, and before long both of you are explaining, defending, or pushing back. What began as contrast can turn into a pattern where each person feels misunderstood by the other."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"You do not have to agree on everything to respect each other. The difference becomes much easier to live with when neither person is trying to prove their way is the right one."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-sun_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s identity. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person may have a way of approaching life that feels noticeably different from yours. They may make choices you would not make, focus on things you tend to overlook, or respond to situations from a completely different starting point. Part of what draws you to them may be that difference. Part of what frustrates you may be the same thing.\n\nWhen this works, the difference can be surprisingly helpful. This person may show you another way of handling things, one that would not have occurred to you on your own. They can make you question old assumptions, consider a different approach, or appreciate strengths you usually overlook. You may not always understand where they are coming from at first, but over time they can broaden your sense of what is possible.\n\nThe harder part is when the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling frustrating. You do things one way, they do things another, and before long both of you are explaining, defending, or pushing back. What began as contrast can turn into a pattern where each person feels misunderstood by the other.\n\nYou do not have to agree on everything to respect each other. The difference becomes much easier to live with when neither person is trying to prove their way is the right one.","tension":"The harder part is when the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling frustrating. You do things one way, they do things another, and before long both of you are explaining, defending, or pushing back. What began as contrast can turn into a pattern where each person feels misunderstood by the other.","advice":"You do not have to agree on everything to respect each other. The difference becomes much easier to live with when neither person is trying to prove their way 