  ('A-uranus_B-venus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"uranus","planetB":"venus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-uranus_B-venus_trine', 'synastry-uranus-trine-venus', 'relationship-uranus-trine-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-uranus_B-venus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-uranus_B-venus_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Uranus Trine Venus', null, 'A''s need for freedom meets B''s love and values. The trine lets them flow together easily.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Translation","body":"A''s need for freedom meets B''s love and values. The trine lets them flow together easily."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-uranus_B-venus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s need for freedom meets B''s love and values. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":null,"tension":null,"advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":null,"weight":null}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-ascendant_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"ascendant","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-ascendant_sextile', 'synastry-venus-sextile-ascendant', 'relationship-venus-sextile-ascendant']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-ascendant_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-ascendant_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Sextile Ascendant', 'The attraction or affection does not have to be forced. Venus softens the room, the Ascendant feels seen, and the connection can become warmer when both people let it be visible.', 'There is an ease to this one. The attraction or affection does not have to be worked for in an obvious way. It is often just there, soft and available, when the two of you are in the same room.

The Venus person usually notices first. Not only how the Ascendant person looks, though that can be part of it, but how they hold themselves, how they move through space, and how their presence arrives before they say anything. Something about them registers as lovely, charming, or worth lingering on, and Venus tends to let that show.

The Ascendant person feels it land. They may feel more like themselves here, and more attractive too. Being received that warmly can be a kind of relief: the wanting, liking, or sweetness is offered without making them perform for it. Their confidence comes up more naturally, and because Venus responds to that, the warmth can begin to move in both directions.

Affection comes easily. Touch may find a natural rhythm if the relationship allows for that. Flirting can feel less risky. A compliment lands where it is meant to. The two of you may simply like being near each other, standing close, catching each other''s eye, or letting the warmth be visible. There can be a public sweetness to it, a chemistry that does not hide itself particularly well.

Because this is a sextile, it does not take over the room. It offers. It opens a door and waits to see if you will walk through it. But if you both lean in, the physical or affectionate side can deepen naturally. What begins as charm and comfort can become desire, tenderness, or a very real pleasure in being close.

The thing to stay honest about is that ease is not the whole relationship. You can love what you see and love how you feel and still need the slower work: showing up, telling the truth, and staying present when the first glow settles.

The gift here is feeling wanted in a way that does not cost you anything to receive. Let the attraction be what it is. Let it become real. Just do not ask it to be the entire thing on its own.

The ease can become so pleasant that both people treat it as the whole story, even when the relationship needs clearer truth, follow-through, or emotional presence.

Let the warmth be visible, but keep it honest. Enjoy the attraction, offer the compliment, make the invitation, and give the connection enough presence to become real.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is an ease to this one. The attraction or affection does not have to be worked for in an obvious way. It is often just there, soft and available, when the two of you are in the same room.\n\nThe Venus person usually notices first. Not only how the Ascendant person looks, though that can be part of it, but how they hold themselves, how they move through space, and how their presence arrives before they say anything. Something about them registers as lovely, charming, or worth lingering on, and Venus tends to let that show.\n\nThe Ascendant person feels it land. They may feel more like themselves here, and more attractive too. Being received that warmly can be a kind of relief: the wanting, liking, or sweetness is offered without making them perform for it. Their confidence comes up more naturally, and because Venus responds to that, the warmth can begin to move in both directions.\n\nAffection comes easily. Touch may find a natural rhythm if the relationship allows for that. Flirting can feel less risky. A compliment lands where it is meant to. The two of you may simply like being near each other, standing close, catching each other''s eye, or letting the warmth be visible. There can be a public sweetness to it, a chemistry that does not hide itself particularly well.\n\nBecause this is a sextile, it does not take over the room. It offers. It opens a door and waits to see if you will walk through it. But if you both lean in, the physical or affectionate side can deepen naturally. What begins as charm and comfort can become desire, tenderness, or a very real pleasure in being close.\n\nThe thing to stay honest about is that ease is not the whole relationship. You can love what you see and love how you feel and still need the slower work: showing up, telling the truth, and staying present when the first glow settles.\n\nThe gift here is feeling wanted in a way that does not cost you anything to receive. Let the attraction be what it is. Let it become real. Just do not ask it to be the entire thing on its own."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The ease can become so pleasant that both people treat it as the whole story, even when the relationship needs clearer truth, follow-through, or emotional presence."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the warmth be visible, but keep it honest. Enjoy the attraction, offer the compliment, make the invitation, and give the connection enough presence to become real."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-ascendant_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"There is an easy warmth here. The Venus person tends to notice the Ascendant person''s presence, style, body language, or way of moving through the world, and the Ascendant person may feel more attractive and relaxed in response.","summaryDeep":"There is an ease to this one. The attraction or affection does not have to be worked for in an obvious way. It is often just there, soft and available, when the two of you are in the same room.\n\nThe Venus person usually notices first. Not only how the Ascendant person looks, though that can be part of it, but how they hold themselves, how they move through space, and how their presence arrives before they say anything. Something about them registers as lovely, charming, or worth lingering on, and Venus tends to let that show.\n\nThe Ascendant person feels it land. They may feel more like themselves here, and more attractive too. Being received that warmly can be a kind of relief: the wanting, liking, or sweetness is offered without making them perform for it. Their confidence comes up more naturally, and because Venus responds to that, the warmth can begin to move in both directions.\n\nAffection comes easily. Touch may find a natural rhythm if the relationship allows for that. Flirting can feel less risky. A compliment lands where it is meant to. The two of you may simply like being near each other, standing close, catching each other''s eye, or letting the warmth be visible. There can be a public sweetness to it, a chemistry that does not hide itself particularly well.\n\nBecause this is a sextile, it does not take over the room. It offers. It opens a door and waits to see if you will walk through it. But if you both lean in, the physical or affectionate side can deepen naturally. What begins as charm and comfort can become desire, tenderness, or a very real pleasure in being close.\n\nThe thing to stay honest about is that ease is not the whole relationship. You can love what you see and love how you feel and still need the slower work: showing up, telling the truth, and staying present when the first glow settles.\n\nThe gift here is feeling wanted in a way that does not cost you anything to receive. Let the attraction be what it is. Let it become real. Just do not ask it to be the entire thing on its own.","tension":"The ease can become so pleasant that both people treat it as the whole story, even when the relationship needs clearer truth, follow-through, or emotional presence.","advice":"Let the warmth be visible, but keep it honest. Enjoy the attraction, offer the compliment, make the invitation, and give the connection enough presence to become real.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Authored to cover planet-to-angle synastry fallback for the relationship interaspect list.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-jupiter_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-jupiter_conjunction', 'synastry-venus-conjunction-jupiter', 'relationship-venus-conjunction-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-jupiter_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-jupiter_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Conjunction Jupiter', null, 'This person expands your capacity for joy. Being with them can remind you that relationships are not only about solving problems or building security. They are also about feeling appreciated, welcomed, and genuinely enjoyed. Their presence may make it easier for you to relax, open up, and trust that there is enough affection, attention, and goodwill to go around.

When this works, you bring out each other''s confidence in life. You celebrate wins together. You encourage each other''s growth. You create an atmosphere where generosity feels natural and where both people feel seen for what is good and valuable in them. There is a sense of possibility here, as though the relationship helps both of you believe in more.

One of the gifts of this connection is that it can shift your mindset from scarcity to abundance. Instead of focusing on what is missing, you notice what is working. Instead of withholding appreciation, you offer it freely. The relationship can become a source of encouragement, optimism, and emotional nourishment.

The challenge is remembering that growth requires honesty as well as positivity. It is easy to focus on the good and overlook what needs attention. You may avoid difficult conversations, assume things will work themselves out, or mistake comfort for progress.

Enjoy what is good, but do not ignore what needs attention. This connection works best when appreciation and responsibility are both present.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person expands your capacity for joy. Being with them can remind you that relationships are not only about solving problems or building security. They are also about feeling appreciated, welcomed, and genuinely enjoyed. Their presence may make it easier for you to relax, open up, and trust that there is enough affection, attention, and goodwill to go around.\n\nWhen this works, you bring out each other''s confidence in life. You celebrate wins together. You encourage each other''s growth. You create an atmosphere where generosity feels natural and where both people feel seen for what is good and valuable in them. There is a sense of possibility here, as though the relationship helps both of you believe in more.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is that it can shift your mindset from scarcity to abundance. Instead of focusing on what is missing, you notice what is working. Instead of withholding appreciation, you offer it freely. The relationship can become a source of encouragement, optimism, and emotional nourishment.\n\nThe challenge is remembering that growth requires honesty as well as positivity. It is easy to focus on the good and overlook what needs attention. You may avoid difficult conversations, assume things will work themselves out, or mistake comfort for progress.\n\nEnjoy what is good, but do not ignore what needs attention. This connection works best when appreciation and responsibility are both present."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is remembering that growth requires honesty as well as positivity. It is easy to focus on the good and overlook what needs attention. You may avoid difficult conversations, assume things will work themselves out, or mistake comfort for progress."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Enjoy what is good, but do not ignore what needs attention. This connection works best when appreciation and responsibility are both present."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-jupiter_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s growth. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person expands your capacity for joy. Being with them can remind you that relationships are not only about solving problems or building security. They are also about feeling appreciated, welcomed, and genuinely enjoyed. Their presence may make it easier for you to relax, open up, and trust that there is enough affection, attention, and goodwill to go around.\n\nWhen this works, you bring out each other''s confidence in life. You celebrate wins together. You encourage each other''s growth. You create an atmosphere where generosity feels natural and where both people feel seen for what is good and valuable in them. There is a sense of possibility here, as though the relationship helps both of you believe in more.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is that it can shift your mindset from scarcity to abundance. Instead of focusing on what is missing, you notice what is working. Instead of withholding appreciation, you offer it freely. The relationship can become a source of encouragement, optimism, and emotional nourishment.\n\nThe challenge is remembering that growth requires honesty as well as positivity. It is easy to focus on the good and overlook what needs attention. You may avoid difficult conversations, assume things will work themselves out, or mistake comfort for progress.\n\nEnjoy what is good, but do not ignore what needs attention. This connection works best when appreciation and responsibility are both present.","tension":"The challenge is remembering that growth requires honesty as well as positivity. It is easy to focus on the good and overlook what needs attention. You may avoid difficult conversations, assume things will work themselves out, or mistake comfort for progress.","advice":"Enjoy what is good, but do not ignore what needs attention. This connection works best when appreciation and responsibility are both present.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-jupiter_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-jupiter_opposition', 'synastry-venus-opposition-jupiter', 'relationship-venus-opposition-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-jupiter_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-jupiter_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Opposition Jupiter', null, 'This person may bring more. More generosity. More enthusiasm. More willingness to say yes to what feels good. Part of you may find that deeply refreshing. Another part may wonder where the limit is. They can encourage you to open up to life''s pleasures while also challenging your sense of balance, moderation, and what feels sustainable.

This connection asks both of you to examine your relationship with receiving. They may encourage you to loosen your grip, trust life a little more, and stop acting as though joy always has to be justified. You may help them recognize when enough is enough and make better choices about where their time, energy, and generosity go.

The tension appears when your differences start to feel like judgments. A difference in perspective can slowly harden into a question of whose truth gets to lead. They may experience your caution as a limit on what is possible, while you may experience their faith in expansion as a refusal to acknowledge reality. Over time, what began as a difference in style can become a story about who has the better way of moving through life.

This connection is not about proving whose approach is right. It is about recognizing that both of your instincts can become excessive in different ways, and finding a balance that serves the relationship better than either extreme. Neither person needs to become the other. The goal is to find a balance where generosity has room to breathe and good judgment still has a voice.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may bring more. More generosity. More enthusiasm. More willingness to say yes to what feels good. Part of you may find that deeply refreshing. Another part may wonder where the limit is. They can encourage you to open up to life''s pleasures while also challenging your sense of balance, moderation, and what feels sustainable.\n\nThis connection asks both of you to examine your relationship with receiving. They may encourage you to loosen your grip, trust life a little more, and stop acting as though joy always has to be justified. You may help them recognize when enough is enough and make better choices about where their time, energy, and generosity go.\n\nThe tension appears when your differences start to feel like judgments. A difference in perspective can slowly harden into a question of whose truth gets to lead. They may experience your caution as a limit on what is possible, while you may experience their faith in expansion as a refusal to acknowledge reality. Over time, what began as a difference in style can become a story about who has the better way of moving through life.\n\nThis connection is not about proving whose approach is right. It is about recognizing that both of your instincts can become excessive in different ways, and finding a balance that serves the relationship better than either extreme. Neither person needs to become the other. The goal is to find a balance where generosity has room to breathe and good judgment still has a voice."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The tension appears when your differences start to feel like judgments. A difference in perspective can slowly harden into a question of whose truth gets to lead. They may experience your caution as a limit on what is possible, while you may experience their faith in expansion as a refusal to acknowledge reality. Over time, what began as a difference in style can become a story about who has the better way of moving through life."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This connection is not about proving whose approach is right. It is about recognizing that both of your instincts can become excessive in different ways, and finding a balance that serves the relationship better than either extreme. Neither person needs to become the other. The goal is to find a balance where generosity has room to breathe and good judgment still has a voice."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-jupiter_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s growth. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person may bring more. More generosity. More enthusiasm. More willingness to say yes to what feels good. Part of you may find that deeply refreshing. Another part may wonder where the limit is. They can encourage you to open up to life''s pleasures while also challenging your sense of balance, moderation, and what feels sustainable.\n\nThis connection asks both of you to examine your relationship with receiving. They may encourage you to loosen your grip, trust life a little more, and stop acting as though joy always has to be justified. You may help them recognize when enough is enough and make better choices about where their time, energy, and generosity go.\n\nThe tension appears when your differences start to feel like judgments. A difference in perspective can slowly harden into a question of whose truth gets to lead. They may experience your caution as a limit on what is possible, while you may experience their faith in expansion as a refusal to acknowledge reality. Over time, what began as a difference in style can become a story about who has the better way of moving through life.\n\nThis connection is not about proving whose approach is right. It is about recognizing that both of your instincts can become excessive in different ways, and finding a balance that serves the relationship better than either extreme. Neither person needs to become the other. The goal is to find a balance where generosity has room to breathe and good judgment still has a voice.","tension":"The tension appears when your differences start to feel like judgments. A difference in perspective can slowly harden into a question of whose truth gets to lead. They may experience your caution as a limit on what is possible, while you may experience their faith in expansion as a refusal to acknowledge reality. Over time, what began as a difference in style can become a story about who has the better way of moving through life.","advice":"This connection is not about proving whose approach is right. It is about recognizing that both of your instincts can become excessive in different ways, and finding a balance that serves the relationship better than either extreme. Neither person needs to become the other. The goal is to find a balance where generosity has room to breathe and good judgment still has a voice.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry-venus-sextile-jupiter', 'relationship-venus-sextile-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-jupiter_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-jupiter_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Sextile Jupiter', null, 'This person likes you. Roots for you, sees the best in you, makes you feel good without you having to earn it. Right away it''s obvious this could be one of the easy, happy ones, a connection that adds to your life instead of draining it.

The good feeling won''t do the work for you. A little effort goes a long way here, the text that says you were thinking of them, the plan you actually make, saying the nice thing out loud instead of figuring they know. Small stuff, and it adds up fast.

That''s the catch with this one. The warmth opens the door and then just stands there. Coast on it, assume it runs itself, and you end up with a great connection you never actually used.

So treat it like anything good. Show up for it. The more you put in, the more this person becomes someone you can count on, instead of a nice thing you let slip.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person likes you. Roots for you, sees the best in you, makes you feel good without you having to earn it. Right away it''s obvious this could be one of the easy, happy ones, a connection that adds to your life instead of draining it.\n\nThe good feeling won''t do the work for you. A little effort goes a long way here, the text that says you were thinking of them, the plan you actually make, saying the nice thing out loud instead of figuring they know. Small stuff, and it adds up fast.\n\nThat''s the catch with this one. The warmth opens the door and then just stands there. Coast on it, assume it runs itself, and you end up with a great connection you never actually used.\n\nSo treat it like anything good. Show up for it. The more you put in, the more this person becomes someone you can count on, instead of a nice thing you let slip."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"That''s the catch with this one. The warmth opens the door and then just stands there. Coast on it, assume it runs itself, and you end up with a great connection you never actually used."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"So treat it like anything good. Show up for it. The more you put in, the more this person becomes someone you can count on, instead of a nice thing you let slip."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-jupiter_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s growth. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This person likes you. Roots for you, sees the best in you, makes you feel good without you having to earn it. Right away it''s obvious this could be one of the easy, happy ones, a connection that adds to your life instead of draining it.\n\nThe good feeling won''t do the work for you. A little effort goes a long way here, the text that says you were thinking of them, the plan you actually make, saying the nice thing out loud instead of figuring they know. Small stuff, and it adds up fast.\n\nThat''s the catch with this one. The warmth opens the door and then just stands there. Coast on it, assume it runs itself, and you end up with a great connection you never actually used.\n\nSo treat it like anything good. Show up for it. The more you put in, the more this person becomes someone you can count on, instead of a nice thing you let slip.","tension":"That''s the catch with this one. The warmth opens the door and then just stands there. Coast on it, assume it runs itself, and you end up with a great connection you never actually used.","advice":"So treat it like anything good. Show up for it. The more you put in, the more this person becomes someone you can count on, instead of a nice thing you let slip.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-jupiter_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-jupiter_square', 'synastry-venus-square-jupiter', 'relationship-venus-square-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-jupiter_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-jupiter_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Square Jupiter', null, 'This person may awaken in you a larger appetite for life. In their presence, pleasure expands. You may feel drawn to celebrate more, give more, forgive more, and say yes to experiences you would normally hold at a distance. There is a temptation to get carried away by what feels good in the moment. This can be a blessing, because it encourages openness, generosity, and joy. But it can also become a kind of unconsciousness when enjoyment begins to run ahead of awareness.

When this works, they help you soften. They may remind you that joy matters, that generosity matters, that life does not have to be all restraint and responsibility. Their presence can pull you out of scarcity and into a more open relationship with pleasure.

The challenge is excess. Too much spending. Too much saying yes because the moment feels good. Too much relying on good feelings to carry the relationship instead of addressing what needs attention. This is where the connection needs honesty. Pleasure is not the problem. Avoidance is. Generosity is not the problem. Lack of limits is.

Let this person broaden your perspective without losing sight of your priorities. This connection works best when both people appreciate the opportunities in front of them while staying realistic.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may awaken in you a larger appetite for life. In their presence, pleasure expands. You may feel drawn to celebrate more, give more, forgive more, and say yes to experiences you would normally hold at a distance. There is a temptation to get carried away by what feels good in the moment. This can be a blessing, because it encourages openness, generosity, and joy. But it can also become a kind of unconsciousness when enjoyment begins to run ahead of awareness.\n\nWhen this works, they help you soften. They may remind you that joy matters, that generosity matters, that life does not have to be all restraint and responsibility. Their presence can pull you out of scarcity and into a more open relationship with pleasure.\n\nThe challenge is excess. Too much spending. Too much saying yes because the moment feels good. Too much relying on good feelings to carry the relationship instead of addressing what needs attention. This is where the connection needs honesty. Pleasure is not the problem. Avoidance is. Generosity is not the problem. Lack of limits is.\n\nLet this person broaden your perspective without losing sight of your priorities. This connection works best when both people appreciate the opportunities in front of them while staying realistic."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is excess. Too much spending. Too much saying yes because the moment feels good. Too much relying on good feelings to carry the relationship instead of addressing what needs attention. This is where the connection needs honesty. Pleasure is not the problem. Avoidance is. Generosity is not the problem. Lack of limits is."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let this person broaden your perspective without losing sight of your priorities. This connection works best when both people appreciate the opportunities in front of them while staying realistic."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-jupiter_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s growth. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This person may awaken in you a larger appetite for life. In their presence, pleasure expands. You may feel drawn to celebrate more, give more, forgive more, and say yes to experiences you would normally hold at a distance. There is a temptation to get carried away by what feels good in the moment. This can be a blessing, because it encourages openness, generosity, and joy. But it can also become a kind of unconsciousness when enjoyment begins to run ahead of awareness.\n\nWhen this works, they help you soften. They may remind you that joy matters, that generosity matters, that life does not have to be all restraint and responsibility. Their presence can pull you out of scarcity and into a more open relationship with pleasure.\n\nThe challenge is excess. Too much spending. Too much saying yes because the moment feels good. Too much relying on good feelings to carry the relationship instead of addressing what needs attention. This is where the connection needs honesty. Pleasure is not the problem. Avoidance is. Generosity is not the problem. Lack of limits is.\n\nLet this person broaden your perspective without losing sight of your priorities. This connection works best when both people appreciate the opportunities in front of them while staying realistic.","tension":"The challenge is excess. Too much spending. Too much saying yes because the moment feels good. Too much relying on good feelings to carry the relationship instead of addressing what needs attention. This is where the connection needs honesty. Pleasure is not the problem. Avoidance is. Generosity is not the problem. Lack of limits is.","advice":"Let this person broaden your perspective without losing sight of your priorities. This connection works best when both people appreciate the opportunities in front of them while staying realistic.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry-venus-trine-jupiter', 'relationship-venus-trine-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-jupiter_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-jupiter_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Trine Jupiter', null, 'This relationship has a way of bringing out the best in both of you. You tend to give each other the benefit of the doubt, let small mistakes go, and pay more attention to what is working than what is not. Being together usually feels good. You enjoy each other, and life can seem a little easier in each other''s company.

When this works, the relationship creates a sense of momentum. You encourage each other to take up space, pursue what matters, and enjoy the good things life has to offer. Time together can leave both of you feeling more optimistic than before, as though the relationship reminds you of your strengths rather than your limitations. There is a natural generosity in the way you relate, making it easier to feel supported, appreciated, and genuinely happy for each other''s growth.

One of the best things about this connection is that it helps you appreciate what is working. It encourages both of you to enjoy the relationship instead of focusing only on responsibilities or problems. Time together can feel genuinely enjoyable, creating moments of happiness and connection that bring you closer.

A relationship can feel good and still need attention, effort, and honest conversation to keep moving forward.

Enjoy the vibe and everything that flows easily between you, but don''t just coast on it. Keep showing up, keep putting something into it. The connections that last are the ones people choose again and again, not just the ones that start out easy.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This relationship has a way of bringing out the best in both of you. You tend to give each other the benefit of the doubt, let small mistakes go, and pay more attention to what is working than what is not. Being together usually feels good. You enjoy each other, and life can seem a little easier in each other''s company.\n\nWhen this works, the relationship creates a sense of momentum. You encourage each other to take up space, pursue what matters, and enjoy the good things life has to offer. Time together can leave both of you feeling more optimistic than before, as though the relationship reminds you of your strengths rather than your limitations. There is a natural generosity in the way you relate, making it easier to feel supported, appreciated, and genuinely happy for each other''s growth.\n\nOne of the best things about this connection is that it helps you appreciate what is working. It encourages both of you to enjoy the relationship instead of focusing only on responsibilities or problems. Time together can feel genuinely enjoyable, creating moments of happiness and connection that bring you closer.\n\nA relationship can feel good and still need attention, effort, and honest conversation to keep moving forward.\n\nEnjoy the vibe and everything that flows easily between you, but don''t just coast on it. Keep showing up, keep putting something into it. The connections that last are the ones people choose again and again, not just the ones that start out easy."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"A relationship can feel good and still need attention, effort, and honest conversation to keep moving forward."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Enjoy the vibe and everything that flows easily between you, but don''t just coast on it. Keep showing up, keep putting something into it. The connections that last are the ones people choose again and again, not just the ones that start out easy."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-jupiter_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s growth. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This relationship has a way of bringing out the best in both of you. You tend to give each other the benefit of the doubt, let small mistakes go, and pay more attention to what is working than what is not. Being together usually feels good. You enjoy each other, and life can seem a little easier in each other''s company.\n\nWhen this works, the relationship creates a sense of momentum. You encourage each other to take up space, pursue what matters, and enjoy the good things life has to offer. Time together can leave both of you feeling more optimistic than before, as though the relationship reminds you of your strengths rather than your limitations. There is a natural generosity in the way you relate, making it easier to feel supported, appreciated, and genuinely happy for each other''s growth.\n\nOne of the best things about this connection is that it helps you appreciate what is working. It encourages both of you to enjoy the relationship instead of focusing only on responsibilities or problems. Time together can feel genuinely enjoyable, creating moments of happiness and connection that bring you closer.\n\nA relationship can feel good and still need attention, effort, and honest conversation to keep moving forward.\n\nEnjoy the vibe and everything that flows easily between you, but don''t just coast on it. Keep showing up, keep putting something into it. The connections that last are the ones people choose again and again, not just the ones that start out easy.","tension":"A relationship can feel good and still need attention, effort, and honest conversation to keep moving forward.","advice":"Enjoy the vibe and everything that flows easily between you, but don''t just coast on it. Keep showing up, keep putting something into it. The connections that last are the ones people choose again and again, not just the ones that start out easy.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"mars","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry-venus-conjunction-mars', 'relationship-venus-conjunction-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-mars_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-mars_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Conjunction Mars', 'The attraction is immediate. Venus and Mars are in the same place, so there isn''t much distance between liking someone and wanting them. One person''s pull meets the other person''s drive directly, and the chemistry can feel obvious from the start.', 'The attraction is immediate. Venus and Mars are in the same place, so there isn''t much distance between liking someone and wanting them. One person''s pull meets the other person''s drive directly, and the chemistry can feel obvious from the start.

This is the kind of connection where everything feels a little charged, even when the conversation itself is normal. There''s heat, there''s interest, and it can be easy to assume that because the attraction is strong, the relationship must be strong too.

Failure mode: mistaking wanting someone for actually being compatible with them. Things can burn hot and fast, then you realize there may not be much holding it together once the charge settles.

Let the spark introduce you. Then take a minute and see if you actually like each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"The attraction is immediate. Venus and Mars are in the same place, so there isn''t much distance between liking someone and wanting them. One person''s pull meets the other person''s drive directly, and the chemistry can feel obvious from the start.\n\nThis is the kind of connection where everything feels a little charged, even when the conversation itself is normal. There''s heat, there''s interest, and it can be easy to assume that because the attraction is strong, the relationship must be strong too.\n\nFailure mode: mistaking wanting someone for actually being compatible with them. Things can burn hot and fast, then you realize there may not be much holding it together once the charge settles.\n\nLet the spark introduce you. Then take a minute and see if you actually like each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Failure mode: mistaking wanting someone for actually being compatible with them. Things can burn hot and fast, then you realize there may not be much holding it together once the charge settles."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the spark introduce you. Then take a minute and see if you actually like each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-mars_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The classic chemistry contact. The Venus person feels wanted and pursued; the Mars person feels the pull and goes after it. Physical, immediate, hard to sit still around each other. Failure mode: mistaking heat for foundation - the attraction is real but says nothing about whether you can live together. Enjoy the spark, build the rest deliberately, and check what''s under it.","summaryDeep":"The attraction is immediate. Venus and Mars are in the same place, so there isn''t much distance between liking someone and wanting them. One person''s pull meets the other person''s drive directly, and the chemistry can feel obvious from the start.\n\nThis is the kind of connection where everything feels a little charged, even when the conversation itself is normal. There''s heat, there''s interest, and it can be easy to assume that because the attraction is strong, the relationship must be strong too.\n\nFailure mode: mistaking wanting someone for actually being compatible with them. Things can burn hot and fast, then you realize there may not be much holding it together once the charge settles.\n\nLet the spark introduce you. Then take a minute and see if you actually like each other.","tension":"Failure mode: mistaking wanting someone for actually being compatible with them. Things can burn hot and fast, then you realize there may not be much holding it together once the charge settles.","advice":"Let the spark introduce you. Then take a minute and see if you actually like each other.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"mars","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry-venus-opposition-mars', 'relationship-venus-opposition-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-mars_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-mars_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Opposition Mars', 'There''s real attraction here, but it may not feel simple. One person might move forward while the other pulls back, and that back-and-forth can become part of the chemistry. The distance creates heat, but it can also make the relationship feel like something always has to be chased.', 'There''s real attraction here, but it may not feel simple. One person might move forward while the other pulls back, and that back-and-forth can become part of the chemistry. The distance creates heat, but it can also make the relationship feel like something always has to be chased.

At its best, this keeps things exciting. At its worst, both people start confusing tension with connection. One person may feel rejected, while the other feels pressured.

Failure mode: only feeling the romance when there is friction, distance, or someone to win over. Once things get simple, the connection may start looking for a new problem.

Say what you want directly. Don''t make the other person figure it out from hints, timing, or attitude.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There''s real attraction here, but it may not feel simple. One person might move forward while the other pulls back, and that back-and-forth can become part of the chemistry. The distance creates heat, but it can also make the relationship feel like something always has to be chased.\n\nAt its best, this keeps things exciting. At its worst, both people start confusing tension with connection. One person may feel rejected, while the other feels pressured.\n\nFailure mode: only feeling the romance when there is friction, distance, or someone to win over. Once things get simple, the connection may start looking for a new problem.\n\nSay what you want directly. Don''t make the other person figure it out from hints, timing, or attitude."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Failure mode: only feeling the romance when there is friction, distance, or someone to win over. Once things get simple, the connection may start looking for a new problem."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Say what you want directly. Don''t make the other person figure it out from hints, timing, or attitude."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-mars_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Magnetic across a gap. Opposite styles of wanting - one pursues, one receives - and that polarity is exactly the draw. Failure mode: swinging between chase and retreat until both are worn out. Meet in the middle on purpose instead of acting out the chase.","summaryDeep":"There''s real attraction here, but it may not feel simple. One person might move forward while the other pulls back, and that back-and-forth can become part of the chemistry. The distance creates heat, but it can also make the relationship feel like something always has to be chased.\n\nAt its best, this keeps things exciting. At its worst, both people start confusing tension with connection. One person may feel rejected, while the other feels pressured.\n\nFailure mode: only feeling the romance when there is friction, distance, or someone to win over. Once things get simple, the connection may start looking for a new problem.\n\nSay what you want directly. Don''t make the other person figure it out from hints, timing, or attitude.","tension":"Failure mode: only feeling the romance when there is friction, distance, or someone to win over. Once things get simple, the connection may start looking for a new problem.","advice":"Say what you want directly. Don''t make the other person figure it out from hints, timing, or attitude.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"mars","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry-venus-sextile-mars', 'relationship-venus-sextile-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-mars_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-mars_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Sextile Mars', 'The attraction is there, but it usually needs someone to do something with it. Venus and Mars support each other here, so charm and desire can work well together, but the chemistry may not fully open unless someone makes a move.', 'The attraction is there, but it usually needs someone to do something with it. Venus and Mars support each other here, so charm and desire can work well together, but the chemistry may not fully open unless someone makes a move.

This can start in a subtle way. A little flirting, a little effort, a little willingness to show interest. The more both people participate, the more the attraction has somewhere to go.

Failure mode: leaving the spark sitting there because everyone is waiting for it to become obvious on its own.

Reach for it. This aspect opens when someone acts.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"The attraction is there, but it usually needs someone to do something with it. Venus and Mars support each other here, so charm and desire can work well together, but the chemistry may not fully open unless someone makes a move.\n\nThis can start in a subtle way. A little flirting, a little effort, a little willingness to show interest. The more both people participate, the more the attraction has somewhere to go.\n\nFailure mode: leaving the spark sitting there because everyone is waiting for it to become obvious on its own.\n\nReach for it. This aspect opens when someone acts."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Failure mode: leaving the spark sitting there because everyone is waiting for it to become obvious on its own."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Reach for it. This aspect opens when someone acts."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-mars_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Easy, low-friction attraction with a little spark. Desire and affection line up without much effort, and there''s room to act on it. Failure mode: pleasant enough to coast on and never deepen. Take the opening - make the move, plan the date - instead of waiting for it to escalate on its own.","summaryDeep":"The attraction is there, but it usually needs someone to do something with it. Venus and Mars support each other here, so charm and desire can work well together, but the chemistry may not fully open unless someone makes a move.\n\nThis can start in a subtle way. A little flirting, a little effort, a little willingness to show interest. The more both people participate, the more the attraction has somewhere to go.\n\nFailure mode: leaving the spark sitting there because everyone is waiting for it to become obvious on its own.\n\nReach for it. This aspect opens when someone acts.","tension":"Failure mode: leaving the spark sitting there because everyone is waiting for it to become obvious on its own.","advice":"Reach for it. This aspect opens when someone acts.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-mars_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"mars","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-mars_square', 'synastry-venus-square-mars', 'relationship-venus-square-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-mars_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-mars_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Square Mars', 'This is attraction with some edge to it. Venus and Mars want each other, but they don''t move together easily. The chemistry is real, but it can come with irritation, mixed signals, and that feeling that the other person knows exactly how to get under your skin.', 'This is attraction with some edge to it. Venus and Mars want each other, but they don''t move together easily. The chemistry is real, but it can come with irritation, mixed signals, and that feeling that the other person knows exactly how to get under your skin.

There may be a lot of heat here, but not all heat is intimacy. Sometimes the charge comes from being challenged. Sometimes it comes from feeling provoked. The trick is knowing the difference between passion and a pattern that keeps making you tense.

Failure mode: confusing friction for chemistry and staying because the conflict makes the connection feel alive.

Use the charge for something you''re building together. Don''t keep turning it on each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This is attraction with some edge to it. Venus and Mars want each other, but they don''t move together easily. The chemistry is real, but it can come with irritation, mixed signals, and that feeling that the other person knows exactly how to get under your skin.\n\nThere may be a lot of heat here, but not all heat is intimacy. Sometimes the charge comes from being challenged. Sometimes it comes from feeling provoked. The trick is knowing the difference between passion and a pattern that keeps making you tense.\n\nFailure mode: confusing friction for chemistry and staying because the conflict makes the connection feel alive.\n\nUse the charge for something you''re building together. Don''t keep turning it on each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Failure mode: confusing friction for chemistry and staying because the conflict makes the connection feel alive."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Use the charge for something you''re building together. Don''t keep turning it on each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-mars_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Friction and pull in the same breath. You want each other and rub each other wrong - fights that turn into heat, heat that turns into fights. Failure mode: the fighting becomes the fuel and you confuse intensity for intimacy. Aim the charge at desire, not combat, and notice if the spark needs conflict to stay lit, because that burns out.","summaryDeep":"This is attraction with some edge to it. Venus and Mars want each other, but they don''t move together easily. The chemistry is real, but it can come with irritation, mixed signals, and that feeling that the other person knows exactly how to get under your skin.\n\nThere may be a lot of heat here, but not all heat is intimacy. Sometimes the charge comes from being challenged. Sometimes it comes from feeling provoked. The trick is knowing the difference between passion and a pattern that keeps making you tense.\n\nFailure mode: confusing friction for chemistry and staying because the conflict makes the connection feel alive.\n\nUse the charge for something you''re building together. Don''t keep turning it on each other.","tension":"Failure mode: confusing friction for chemistry and staying because the conflict makes the connection feel alive.","advice":"Use the charge for something you''re building together. Don''t keep turning it on each other.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-mars_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"mars","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-mars_trine', 'synastry-venus-trine-mars', 'relationship-venus-trine-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-mars_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-mars_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Trine Mars', 'Desire and attraction move easily here. The chemistry feels natural, warm, and unforced. Nobody has to work too hard to create interest, and there''s often a physical ease between the two people that feels simple in a good way.', 'Desire and attraction move easily here. The chemistry feels natural, warm, and unforced. Nobody has to work too hard to create interest, and there''s often a physical ease between the two people that feels simple in a good way.

This can be a very comfortable kind of attraction. The rhythm makes sense. The timing is easier. There''s less guessing, less proving, and less drama around who wants what.

Failure mode: taking the ease for granted. Because the connection does not demand constant effort, it can quietly stop being fed.

Keep choosing it. Just because something feels natural does not mean it can run forever on its own.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Desire and attraction move easily here. The chemistry feels natural, warm, and unforced. Nobody has to work too hard to create interest, and there''s often a physical ease between the two people that feels simple in a good way.\n\nThis can be a very comfortable kind of attraction. The rhythm makes sense. The timing is easier. There''s less guessing, less proving, and less drama around who wants what.\n\nFailure mode: taking the ease for granted. Because the connection does not demand constant effort, it can quietly stop being fed.\n\nKeep choosing it. Just because something feels natural does not mean it can run forever on its own."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Failure mode: taking the ease for granted. Because the connection does not demand constant effort, it can quietly stop being fed."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Keep choosing it. Just because something feels natural does not mean it can run forever on its own."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-mars_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Attraction that flows naturally. You want each other in a way that feels effortless and warm, with little push-pull drama. Failure mode: effortless slides into complacency; easy chemistry still needs tending. Keep showing up for it - don''t assume it runs itself.","summaryDeep":"Desire and attraction move easily here. The chemistry feels natural, warm, and unforced. Nobody has to work too hard to create interest, and there''s often a physical ease between the two people that feels simple in a good way.\n\nThis can be a very comfortable kind of attraction. The rhythm makes sense. The timing is easier. There''s less guessing, less proving, and less drama around who wants what.\n\nFailure mode: taking the ease for granted. Because the connection does not demand constant effort, it can quietly stop being fed.\n\nKeep choosing it. Just because something feels natural does not mean it can run forever on its own.","tension":"Failure mode: taking the ease for granted. Because the connection does not demand constant effort, it can quietly stop being fed.","advice":"Keep choosing it. Just because something feels natural does not mean it can run forever on its own.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry-venus-conjunction-mercury', 'relationship-venus-conjunction-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-mercury_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-mercury_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Conjunction Mercury', null, 'This connection often feels good from the start. There may be something about the way this person speaks that puts you at ease. Their words can make you feel seen, appreciated, and understood. After spending time with them, you may walk away feeling a little lighter, a little more confident, or simply more like yourself.

When this aspect flows well, conversation becomes a source of connection. You encourage each other naturally. You may spend hours sharing ideas, talking about your hopes, or reflecting on life together. There is often a feeling that this person understands where you''re coming from, and that feeling can be deeply attractive.

You may also find that your values align in meaningful ways. What matters to you matters to them.

The downside is that comfort can become a habit. When things are easy between you, it''s tempting to stick to what feels good and avoid the conversations that are messier, riskier, or harder to navigate.

One of the gifts of this connection is that you naturally help each other feel seen and valued. That creates a strong foundation. The opportunity is to build on it.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection often feels good from the start. There may be something about the way this person speaks that puts you at ease. Their words can make you feel seen, appreciated, and understood. After spending time with them, you may walk away feeling a little lighter, a little more confident, or simply more like yourself.\n\nWhen this aspect flows well, conversation becomes a source of connection. You encourage each other naturally. You may spend hours sharing ideas, talking about your hopes, or reflecting on life together. There is often a feeling that this person understands where you''re coming from, and that feeling can be deeply attractive.\n\nYou may also find that your values align in meaningful ways. What matters to you matters to them.\n\nThe downside is that comfort can become a habit. When things are easy between you, it''s tempting to stick to what feels good and avoid the conversations that are messier, riskier, or harder to navigate.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is that you naturally help each other feel seen and valued. That creates a strong foundation. The opportunity is to build on it."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The downside is that comfort can become a habit. When things are easy between you, it''s tempting to stick to what feels good and avoid the conversations that are messier, riskier, or harder to navigate."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"One of the gifts of this connection is that you naturally help each other feel seen and valued. That creates a strong foundation. The opportunity is to build on it."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-mercury_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s mind. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This connection often feels good from the start. There may be something about the way this person speaks that puts you at ease. Their words can make you feel seen, appreciated, and understood. After spending time with them, you may walk away feeling a little lighter, a little more confident, or simply more like yourself.\n\nWhen this aspect flows well, conversation becomes a source of connection. You encourage each other naturally. You may spend hours sharing ideas, talking about your hopes, or reflecting on life together. There is often a feeling that this person understands where you''re coming from, and that feeling can be deeply attractive.\n\nYou may also find that your values align in meaningful ways. What matters to you matters to them.\n\nThe downside is that comfort can become a habit. When things are easy between you, it''s tempting to stick to what feels good and avoid the conversations that are messier, riskier, or harder to navigate.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is that you naturally help each other feel seen and valued. That creates a strong foundation. The opportunity is to build on it.","tension":"The downside is that comfort can become a habit. When things are easy between you, it''s tempting to stick to what feels good and avoid the conversations that are messier, riskier, or harder to navigate.","advice":"One of the gifts of this connection is that you naturally help each other feel seen and valued. That creates a strong foundation. The opportunity is to build on it.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry-venus-opposition-mercury', 'relationship-venus-opposition-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-mercury_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-mercury_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Opposition Mercury', null, 'This connection asks you to stretch beyond your usual understanding of affection.

This person may communicate care in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. The way they flirt, compliment, joke, or express appreciation may not be what you instinctively recognize as warmth. Still, there may be something magnetic about the contrast. Their way of expressing affection can challenge your assumptions and open you to forms of care you might not have noticed before.

Oppositions often bring us face-to-face with another perspective. In this case, the contrast can be compelling. This person may express warmth, affection, or appreciation in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. Their approach can stretch your understanding of connection, showing you that care does not always arrive in the form you expect. Over time, you may discover new ways of giving and receiving affection through the differences between you.

The challenge is that affection does not always arrive in a recognizable form. One person may think they are showing care, while the other does not feel cared for at all. What one person sees as thoughtful may feel distant to the other. What feels sincere may feel awkward. What seems obvious may not register at all.

Both people can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood.

The more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection asks you to stretch beyond your usual understanding of affection.\n\nThis person may communicate care in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. The way they flirt, compliment, joke, or express appreciation may not be what you instinctively recognize as warmth. Still, there may be something magnetic about the contrast. Their way of expressing affection can challenge your assumptions and open you to forms of care you might not have noticed before.\n\nOppositions often bring us face-to-face with another perspective. In this case, the contrast can be compelling. This person may express warmth, affection, or appreciation in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. Their approach can stretch your understanding of connection, showing you that care does not always arrive in the form you expect. Over time, you may discover new ways of giving and receiving affection through the differences between you.\n\nThe challenge is that affection does not always arrive in a recognizable form. One person may think they are showing care, while the other does not feel cared for at all. What one person sees as thoughtful may feel distant to the other. What feels sincere may feel awkward. What seems obvious may not register at all.\n\nBoth people can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood.\n\nThe more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that affection does not always arrive in a recognizable form. One person may think they are showing care, while the other does not feel cared for at all. What one person sees as thoughtful may feel distant to the other. What feels sincere may feel awkward. What seems obvious may not register at all.\n\nBoth people can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-mercury_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s mind. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This connection asks you to stretch beyond your usual understanding of affection.\n\nThis person may communicate care in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. The way they flirt, compliment, joke, or express appreciation may not be what you instinctively recognize as warmth. Still, there may be something magnetic about the contrast. Their way of expressing affection can challenge your assumptions and open you to forms of care you might not have noticed before.\n\nOppositions often bring us face-to-face with another perspective. In this case, the contrast can be compelling. This person may express warmth, affection, or appreciation in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. Their approach can stretch your understanding of connection, showing you that care does not always arrive in the form you expect. Over time, you may discover new ways of giving and receiving affection through the differences between you.\n\nThe challenge is that affection does not always arrive in a recognizable form. One person may think they are showing care, while the other does not feel cared for at all. What one person sees as thoughtful may feel distant to the other. What feels sincere may feel awkward. What seems obvious may not register at all.\n\nBoth people can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood.\n\nThe more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there.","tension":"The challenge is that affection does not always arrive in a recognizable form. One person may think they are showing care, while the other does not feel cared for at all. What one person sees as thoughtful may feel distant to the other. What feels sincere may feel awkward. What seems obvious may not register at all.\n\nBoth people can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood.","advice":"The more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry-venus-sextile-mercury', 'relationship-venus-sextile-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-mercury_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-mercury_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Sextile Mercury', null, 'There is a natural opening for warmth here, but it grows when it is expressed. This person may be easy to talk to not only because of what they say, but because of how their mind meets yours. You may enjoy the way they think, the details they notice, the questions they ask, or the way they help a conversation unfold. There is often appreciation present from the beginning. The invitation is to share it.

This connection deepens when appreciation is spoken aloud. Let this person know what you value about them. Reflect back something they shared that stayed with you. Acknowledge the impact their words or actions have had. These small moments of recognition build trust over time. The more you practice naming what matters, the more supported, understood, and connected both of you are likely to feel.

Two people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.

You strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is a natural opening for warmth here, but it grows when it is expressed. This person may be easy to talk to not only because of what they say, but because of how their mind meets yours. You may enjoy the way they think, the details they notice, the questions they ask, or the way they help a conversation unfold. There is often appreciation present from the beginning. The invitation is to share it.\n\nThis connection deepens when appreciation is spoken aloud. Let this person know what you value about them. Reflect back something they shared that stayed with you. Acknowledge the impact their words or actions have had. These small moments of recognition build trust over time. The more you practice naming what matters, the more supported, understood, and connected both of you are likely to feel.\n\nTwo people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.\n\nYou strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Two people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"You strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-mercury_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s mind. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"There is a natural opening for warmth here, but it grows when it is expressed. This person may be easy to talk to not only because of what they say, but because of how their mind meets yours. You may enjoy the way they think, the details they notice, the questions they ask, or the way they help a conversation unfold. There is often appreciation present from the beginning. The invitation is to share it.\n\nThis connection deepens when appreciation is spoken aloud. Let this person know what you value about them. Reflect back something they shared that stayed with you. Acknowledge the impact their words or actions have had. These small moments of recognition build trust over time. The more you practice naming what matters, the more supported, understood, and connected both of you are likely to feel.\n\nTwo people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.\n\nYou strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference.","tension":"Two people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.","advice":"You strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-mercury_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-mercury_square', 'synastry-venus-square-mercury', 'relationship-venus-square-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-mercury_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-mercury_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Square Mercury', null, 'This is the quiet distance between what one person says and what the other person needs to feel loved. It lives in a tender, specific place: the gap between being drawn to someone and actually feeling understood by them.

You may find yourself attracted and irritated in nearly the same breath. Something about this person''s mind, their humor, the particular way they put things, pulls you in. And then the same mouth that charmed you says something that lands wrong, and you feel the pull and the friction at once, unsure which one to trust.

Sometimes the mismatch is loud. One of you is too blunt, the other too careful. One wants the truth laid bare, the other wants it handled gently. But more often it is subtle, almost too small to name. A compliment that arrives slightly off. A joke that grazes a nerve. A conversation that was supposed to bring you closer and instead leaves one of you a little lonelier than before it started.

Because this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm.

The work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own version of it. We tend to offer love in the language we would want to receive it, and then feel hurt when it does not translate. What lands as tender to you may read as flat to them. What feels honest to them may feel sharp to you.

This is the slow practice the square asks for. Not better chemistry, you already have that. The harder thing: learning how this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This is the quiet distance between what one person says and what the other person needs to feel loved. It lives in a tender, specific place: the gap between being drawn to someone and actually feeling understood by them.\n\nYou may find yourself attracted and irritated in nearly the same breath. Something about this person''s mind, their humor, the particular way they put things, pulls you in. And then the same mouth that charmed you says something that lands wrong, and you feel the pull and the friction at once, unsure which one to trust.\n\nSometimes the mismatch is loud. One of you is too blunt, the other too careful. One wants the truth laid bare, the other wants it handled gently. But more often it is subtle, almost too small to name. A compliment that arrives slightly off. A joke that grazes a nerve. A conversation that was supposed to bring you closer and instead leaves one of you a little lonelier than before it started.\n\nBecause this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm.\n\nThe work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own versio