  ('A-venus_B-uranus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"uranus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-uranus_trine', 'synastry-venus-trine-uranus', 'relationship-venus-trine-uranus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-uranus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-uranus_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Trine Uranus', null, 'A''s love and values meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Translation","body":"A''s love and values meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-uranus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":null,"tension":null,"advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":null,"weight":null}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-venus_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"venus","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-venus_conjunction', 'synastry-venus-conjunction-venus', 'relationship-venus-conjunction-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-venus_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-venus_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Conjunction Venus', null, 'You probably noticed it early, in something small. They reached for the same thing you would have. They lit up at the place you secretly love. You did not have to explain why something was worth it, because they already felt the pull. There is a specific pleasure in being wanted-alike, in not having to translate your taste to someone who already shares it.

When this works, ordinary life gets easy in a way you might not even notice until you compare it to other relationships. So many small choices never have to become discussions. Where to eat, how to spend the afternoon, what is worth the money. You agree before anyone has to argue, and that agreement is its own kind of intimacy. You feel recognized, not just liked.

Here is the part that is harder to see from inside it. Wanting the same things is not the same as wanting good things. The very fact that you never have to justify yourselves to each other means nobody is ever the brake. You may indulge the same habit, overspend in the same place, talk each other into the same thing, and call it shared taste when it is closer to a shared blind spot. The person who would normally talk you down is busy agreeing with you.

Enjoy how good it feels to want the same things. Just stay awake inside it. The gift is not that you agree. The gift is the chance to choose well together, which sometimes means being the one who asks whether you actually should.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You probably noticed it early, in something small. They reached for the same thing you would have. They lit up at the place you secretly love. You did not have to explain why something was worth it, because they already felt the pull. There is a specific pleasure in being wanted-alike, in not having to translate your taste to someone who already shares it.\n\nWhen this works, ordinary life gets easy in a way you might not even notice until you compare it to other relationships. So many small choices never have to become discussions. Where to eat, how to spend the afternoon, what is worth the money. You agree before anyone has to argue, and that agreement is its own kind of intimacy. You feel recognized, not just liked.\n\nHere is the part that is harder to see from inside it. Wanting the same things is not the same as wanting good things. The very fact that you never have to justify yourselves to each other means nobody is ever the brake. You may indulge the same habit, overspend in the same place, talk each other into the same thing, and call it shared taste when it is closer to a shared blind spot. The person who would normally talk you down is busy agreeing with you.\n\nEnjoy how good it feels to want the same things. Just stay awake inside it. The gift is not that you agree. The gift is the chance to choose well together, which sometimes means being the one who asks whether you actually should."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Here is the part that is harder to see from inside it. Wanting the same things is not the same as wanting good things. The very fact that you never have to justify yourselves to each other means nobody is ever the brake. You may indulge the same habit, overspend in the same place, talk each other into the same thing, and call it shared taste when it is closer to a shared blind spot. The person who would normally talk you down is busy agreeing with you."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Enjoy how good it feels to want the same things. Just stay awake inside it. The gift is not that you agree. The gift is the chance to choose well together, which sometimes means being the one who asks whether you actually should."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-venus_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"You love the same way and value the same things. Shared tastes, aligned affection, an easy sense that you like the same stuff. Failure mode: so similar you never grow past shared blind spots - including how you both dodge hard conversations. Enjoy the harmony; bring in some difference so it doesn''t go stale.","summaryDeep":"You probably noticed it early, in something small. They reached for the same thing you would have. They lit up at the place you secretly love. You did not have to explain why something was worth it, because they already felt the pull. There is a specific pleasure in being wanted-alike, in not having to translate your taste to someone who already shares it.\n\nWhen this works, ordinary life gets easy in a way you might not even notice until you compare it to other relationships. So many small choices never have to become discussions. Where to eat, how to spend the afternoon, what is worth the money. You agree before anyone has to argue, and that agreement is its own kind of intimacy. You feel recognized, not just liked.\n\nHere is the part that is harder to see from inside it. Wanting the same things is not the same as wanting good things. The very fact that you never have to justify yourselves to each other means nobody is ever the brake. You may indulge the same habit, overspend in the same place, talk each other into the same thing, and call it shared taste when it is closer to a shared blind spot. The person who would normally talk you down is busy agreeing with you.\n\nEnjoy how good it feels to want the same things. Just stay awake inside it. The gift is not that you agree. The gift is the chance to choose well together, which sometimes means being the one who asks whether you actually should.","tension":"Here is the part that is harder to see from inside it. Wanting the same things is not the same as wanting good things. The very fact that you never have to justify yourselves to each other means nobody is ever the brake. You may indulge the same habit, overspend in the same place, talk each other into the same thing, and call it shared taste when it is closer to a shared blind spot. The person who would normally talk you down is busy agreeing with you.","advice":"Enjoy how good it feels to want the same things. Just stay awake inside it. The gift is not that you agree. The gift is the chance to choose well together, which sometimes means being the one who asks whether you actually should.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-venus_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"venus","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-venus_opposition', 'synastry-venus-opposition-venus', 'relationship-venus-opposition-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-venus_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-venus_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Opposition Venus', null, 'You may have felt it the first time you saw how they spent their money, or how they spent a free day. Something in you went, that is not what I would do. One of you feels safest when there is something saved. The other feels most alive spending on the thing that makes life beautiful right now. One wants the life settled. The other wants room to keep changing their mind about what they want.

At first the difference can be part of the draw. This person reaches for things you would never have reached for, and being near that can feel like a window into another way to live. They can widen you. You start to notice pleasures you had written off, and to suspect that your own taste is less a law of nature and more a habit you inherited.

The harder part is the moment the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling like a verdict. What feels generous to you can look reckless to them. What feels responsible to them can feel joyless to you. Nobody says it directly. It comes out as a small face at the restaurant bill, a certain silence about the purchase, a sense that the other person is quietly grading how you live. Few things sting like feeling judged for what genuinely makes you happy.

This one needs you to say it out loud instead of letting it curdle. Tell them what the thing actually gives you. Ask them the same, and listen past the part you find baffling. You do not have to want the same life. You have to stop treating your own preferences as the obviously correct ones.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You may have felt it the first time you saw how they spent their money, or how they spent a free day. Something in you went, that is not what I would do. One of you feels safest when there is something saved. The other feels most alive spending on the thing that makes life beautiful right now. One wants the life settled. The other wants room to keep changing their mind about what they want.\n\nAt first the difference can be part of the draw. This person reaches for things you would never have reached for, and being near that can feel like a window into another way to live. They can widen you. You start to notice pleasures you had written off, and to suspect that your own taste is less a law of nature and more a habit you inherited.\n\nThe harder part is the moment the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling like a verdict. What feels generous to you can look reckless to them. What feels responsible to them can feel joyless to you. Nobody says it directly. It comes out as a small face at the restaurant bill, a certain silence about the purchase, a sense that the other person is quietly grading how you live. Few things sting like feeling judged for what genuinely makes you happy.\n\nThis one needs you to say it out loud instead of letting it curdle. Tell them what the thing actually gives you. Ask them the same, and listen past the part you find baffling. You do not have to want the same life. You have to stop treating your own preferences as the obviously correct ones."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part is the moment the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling like a verdict. What feels generous to you can look reckless to them. What feels responsible to them can feel joyless to you. Nobody says it directly. It comes out as a small face at the restaurant bill, a certain silence about the purchase, a sense that the other person is quietly grading how you live. Few things sting like feeling judged for what genuinely makes you happy."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This one needs you to say it out loud instead of letting it curdle. Tell them what the thing actually gives you. Ask them the same, and listen past the part you find baffling. You do not have to want the same life. You have to stop treating your own preferences as the obviously correct ones."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-venus_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Opposite tastes and values that attract. You''re drawn to what you don''t share. Failure mode: friction over whose way is right. Treat the difference as range, not a referendum.","summaryDeep":"You may have felt it the first time you saw how they spent their money, or how they spent a free day. Something in you went, that is not what I would do. One of you feels safest when there is something saved. The other feels most alive spending on the thing that makes life beautiful right now. One wants the life settled. The other wants room to keep changing their mind about what they want.\n\nAt first the difference can be part of the draw. This person reaches for things you would never have reached for, and being near that can feel like a window into another way to live. They can widen you. You start to notice pleasures you had written off, and to suspect that your own taste is less a law of nature and more a habit you inherited.\n\nThe harder part is the moment the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling like a verdict. What feels generous to you can look reckless to them. What feels responsible to them can feel joyless to you. Nobody says it directly. It comes out as a small face at the restaurant bill, a