  ('A-venus_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"venus","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry-venus-sextile-venus', 'relationship-venus-sextile-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-venus_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-venus_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Sextile Venus', null, 'The overlap is there, but you may have noticed it tends to sit unused. You both know the kind of thing you enjoy. You both can picture the good weekend, the nice meal, the small ritual that would make life feel richer. And then the week happens, and the default is routine, distraction, nothing in particular. The taste is shared. The acting on it is what goes missing.

When this works, it is because someone makes the move. One of you books the thing, plans the evening, spends on the experience instead of letting it stay a someday. And it lands, because you already know what the other person enjoys, so the effort almost never misses. The pleasure does not have to be extravagant. It just has to actually happen.

This contact teaches something quietly important. The life you both want does not assemble itself out of good intentions. It gets built in small deliberate choices, the reservation made, the money set aside for the thing that matters, the ordinary evening someone decided to make nice on purpose.

Act on what you both already value. Make the plan instead of imagining it. This connection gets richer every single time one of you turns the shared wanting into something you actually did, rather than something you both agreed would be lovely sometime.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"The overlap is there, but you may have noticed it tends to sit unused. You both know the kind of thing you enjoy. You both can picture the good weekend, the nice meal, the small ritual that would make life feel richer. And then the week happens, and the default is routine, distraction, nothing in particular. The taste is shared. The acting on it is what goes missing.\n\nWhen this works, it is because someone makes the move. One of you books the thing, plans the evening, spends on the experience instead of letting it stay a someday. And it lands, because you already know what the other person enjoys, so the effort almost never misses. The pleasure does not have to be extravagant. It just has to actually happen.\n\nThis contact teaches something quietly important. The life you both want does not assemble itself out of good intentions. It gets built in small deliberate choices, the reservation made, the money set aside for the thing that matters, the ordinary evening someone decided to make nice on purpose.\n\nAct on what you both already value. Make the plan instead of imagining it. This connection gets richer every single time one of you turns the shared wanting into something you actually did, rather than something you both agreed would be lovely sometime."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"This contact teaches something quietly important. The life you both want does not assemble itself out of good intentions. It gets built in small deliberate choices, the reservation made, the money set aside for the thing that matters, the ordinary evening someone decided to make nice on purpose."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Act on what you both already value. Make the plan instead of imagining it. This connection gets richer every single time one of you turns the shared wanting into something you actually did, rather than something you both agreed would be lovely sometime."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-venus_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Compatible values and affection with a spark of difference. You get along easily and complement each other''s tastes. Failure mode: leaving the rapport unexamined. Use it; stay curious where you diverge.","summaryDeep":"The overlap is there, but you may have noticed it tends to sit unused. You both know the kind of thing you enjoy. You both can picture the good weekend, the nice meal, the small ritual that would make life feel richer. And then the week happens, and the default is routine, distraction, nothing in particular. The taste is shared. The acting on it is what goes missing.\n\nWhen this works, it is because someone makes the move. One of you books the thing, plans the evening, spends on the experience instead of letting it stay a someday. And it lands, because you already know what the other person enjoys, so the effort almost never misses. The pleasure does not have to be extravagant. It just has to actually happen.\n\nThis contact teaches something quietly important. The life you both want does not assemble itself out of good intentions. It gets built in small deliberate choices, the reservation made, the money set aside for the thing that matters, the ordinary evening someone decided to make nice on purpose.\n\nAct on what you both already value. Make the plan instead of imagining it. This connection gets richer every single time one of you turns the shared wanting into something you actually did, rather than something you both agreed would be lovely sometime.","tension":"This contact teaches something quietly important. The life you both want does not assemble itself out of good intentions. It gets built in small deliberate choices, the reservation made, the money set aside for the thing that matters, the ordinary evening someone decided to make nice on purpose.","advice":"Act on what you both already value. Make the plan instead of imagining it. This connection gets richer every single time one of you turns the shared wanting into something you actually did, rather than something you both agreed would be lovely sometime.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-venus_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"venus","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-venus_square', 'synastry-venus-square-venus', 'relationship-venus-square-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-venus_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-venus_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Square Venus', null, 'This person can make you question your own taste without ever meaning to. You look at what they want, buy, or prize, and some part of you doesn''t get it. Maybe you even feel a flicker of judgment, and then a flicker of doubt, because they are looking back at your choices with the same quiet question. The things that feel obviously worth it to you do not register the same way to them.

It usually shows up somewhere ordinary and a little exposing. The thermostat. The grocery cart. How much is reasonable to spend on a good time. Whether a nice thing is a treat or a waste. One of you treats pleasure as something you have earned and need, the other treats it as a little suspect, and you can each feel faintly criticized by the other''s whole approach to enjoying life.

When this works, the friction does something useful. It shows you where your taste has gone on autopilot. You may catch that some of what you call practical is actually fear of letting yourself have things. Some of what you call beautiful is a need you have not fully admitted to. The other person becomes a mirror you did not ask for and learn from anyway.

The harder part is how fast different taste becomes a story about character. Shallow. Boring. Reckless. Cheap. Once you are quietly assigning those words, every small choice becomes more evidence.

Get curious before you get superior. Ask why it matters to them, and tell the truth about why it matters to you. This eases the moment you stop hearing their preference as a comment on yours.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can make you question your own taste without ever meaning to. You look at what they want, buy, or prize, and some part of you doesn''t get it. Maybe you even feel a flicker of judgment, and then a flicker of doubt, because they are looking back at your choices with the same quiet question. The things that feel obviously worth it to you do not register the same way to them.\n\nIt usually shows up somewhere ordinary and a little exposing. The thermostat. The grocery cart. How much is reasonable to spend on a good time. Whether a nice thing is a treat or a waste. One of you treats pleasure as something you have earned and need, the other treats it as a little suspect, and you can each feel faintly criticized by the other''s whole approach to enjoying life.\n\nWhen this works, the friction does something useful. It shows you where your taste has gone on autopilot. You may catch that some of what you call practical is actually fear of letting yourself have things. Some of what you call beautiful is a need you have not fully admitted to. The other person becomes a mirror you did not ask for and learn from anyway.\n\nThe harder part is how fast different taste becomes a story about character. Shallow. Boring. Reckless. Cheap. Once you are quietly assigning those words, every small choice becomes more evidence.\n\nGet curious before you get superior. Ask why it matters to them, and tell the truth about why it matters to you. This eases the moment you stop hearing their preference as a comment on yours."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part is how fast different taste becomes a story about character. Shallow. Boring. Reckless. Cheap. Once you are quietly assigning those words, every small choice becomes more evidence."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Get curious before you get superior. Ask why it matters to them, and tell the truth about why it matters to you. This eases the moment you stop hearing their preference as a comment on yours."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-venus_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Clashing values or styles of affection. You want different things from love, or show it in ways the other doesn''t read. Failure mode: each feeling unappreciated in their own language. Learn how the other gives and wants love - the clash is workable with translation.","summaryDeep":"This person can make you question your own taste without ever meaning to. You look at what they want, buy, or prize, and some part of you doesn''t get it. Maybe you even feel a flicker of judgment, and then a flicker of doubt, because they are looking back at your choices with the same quiet question. The things that feel obviously worth it to you do not register the same way to them.\n\nIt usually shows up somewhere ordinary and a little exposing. The thermostat. The grocery cart. How much is reasonable to spend on a good time. Whether a nice thing is a treat or a waste. One of you treats pleasure as something you have earned and need, the other treats it as a little suspect, and you can each feel faintly criticized by the other''s whole approach to enjoying life.\n\nWhen this works, the friction does something useful. It shows you where your taste has gone on autopilot. You may catch that some of what you call practical is actually fear of letting yourself have things. Some of what you call beautiful is a need you have not fully admitted to. The other person becomes a mirror you did not ask for and learn from anyway.\n\nThe harder part is how fast different taste becomes a story about character. Shallow. Boring. Reckless. Cheap. Once you are quietly assigning those words, every small choice becomes more evidence.\n\nGet curious before you get superior. Ask why it matters to them, and tell the truth about why it matters to you. This eases the moment you stop hearing their preference as a comment on yours.","tension":"The harder part is how fast different taste becomes a story about character. Shallow. Boring. Reckless. Cheap. Once you are quietly assigning those words, every small choice becomes more evidence.","advice":"Get curious before you get superior. Ask why it matters to them, and tell the truth about why it matters to you. This eases the moment you stop hearing their preference as a comment on yours.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-venus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"venus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-venus_trine', 'synastry-venus-trine-venus', 'relationship-venus-trine-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-venus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-venus_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Trine Venus', null, 'There is an ease here you might take for granted until you are with someone who does not share it. You tend to want the same kind of evening, find the same things lovely, agree without trying on what is worth the money and the time. You are not constantly selling each other on what matters. You just relax into the same pleasures, and a whole layer of the usual relationship friction never appears.

When this works, it makes ordinary life feel good in a low, steady way. Plans are easy. Spending is easy. You move toward a similar idea of comfort and beauty without negotiating every step. There is a sweetness to being with someone whose sense of a good life rhymes with your own, where enjoying things together is the default rather than a compromise.

The catch is quiet and easy to miss. Because you already agree, you may stop checking whether what you both want is still what you actually need. You can drift into the same comforts, the same purchases, the same pleasant routines, simply because they feel good and nobody is asking the question. Ease has a way of becoming unconscious.

Keep choosing your pleasures on purpose instead of by habit. The shared taste is a real gift, but it gets more powerful when it has a direction, when you point it at the life you are actually trying to build rather than just the one that feels nice today.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is an ease here you might take for granted until you are with someone who does not share it. You tend to want the same kind of evening, find the same things lovely, agree without trying on what is worth the money and the time. You are not constantly selling each other on what matters. You just relax into the same pleasures, and a whole layer of the usual relationship friction never appears.\n\nWhen this works, it makes ordinary life feel good in a low, steady way. Plans are easy. Spending is easy. You move toward a similar idea of comfort and beauty without negotiating every step. There is a sweetness to being with someone whose sense of a good life rhymes with your own, where enjoying things together is the default rather than a compromise.\n\nThe catch is quiet and easy to miss. Because you already agree, you may stop checking whether what you both want is still what you actually need. You can drift into the same comforts, the same purchases, the same pleasant routines, simply because they feel good and nobody is asking the question. Ease has a way of becoming unconscious.\n\nKeep choosing your pleasures on purpose instead of by habit. The shared taste is a real gift, but it gets more powerful when it has a direction, when you point it at the life you are actually trying to build rather than just the one that feels nice today."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The catch is quiet and easy to miss. Because you already agree, you may stop checking whether what you both want is still what you actually need. You can drift into the same comforts, the same purchases, the same pleasant routines, simply because they feel good and nobody is asking the question. Ease has a way of becoming unconscious."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Keep choosing your pleasures on purpose instead of by habit. The shared taste is a real gift, but it gets more powerful when it has a direction, when you point it at the life you are actually trying to build rather than just the one that feels nice today."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-venus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Love styles and values that flow together naturally. Comfortable, harmonious, genuinely pleasant. Failure mode: comfort with no challenge. A lovely foundation; make sure something else brings the heat.","summaryDeep":"There is an ease here you might take for granted until you are with someone who does not share it. You tend to want the same kind of evening, find the same things lovely, agree without trying on what is worth the money and the time. You are not constantly selling each other on what matters. You just relax into the same pleasures, and a whole layer of the usual relationship friction never appears.\n\nWhen this works, it makes ordinary life feel good in a low, steady way. Plans are easy. Spending is easy. You move toward a similar idea of comfort and beauty without negotiating every step. There is a sweetness to being with someone whose sense of a good life rhymes with your own, where enjoying things together is the default rather than a compromise.\n\nThe catch is quiet and easy to miss. Because you already agree, you may stop checking whether what you both want is still what you actually need. You can drift into the same comforts, the same purchases, the same pleasant routines, simply because they feel good and nobody is asking the question. Ease has a way of becoming unconscious.\n\nKeep choosing your pleasures on purpose instead of by habit. The shared taste is a real gift, but it gets more powerful when it has a direction, when you point it at the life you are actually trying to build rather than just the one that feels nice today.","tension":"The catch is quiet and easy to miss. Because you already agree, you may stop checking whether what you both want is still what you actually need. You can drift into the same comforts, the same purchases, the same pleasant routines, simply because they feel good and nobody is asking the question. Ease has a way of becoming unconscious.","advice":"Keep choosing your pleasures on purpose instead of by habit. The shared taste is a real gift, but it gets more powerful when it has a direction, when you point it at the life you are actually trying to build rather than just the one that feels nice today.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from approved project marquee synastry aspect material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
